desc:TT-303 Acid Machine
// @description TT-303 Acid Machine
// @author TimTechlor
// @version 2.0.0
// @license MIT
// @tags synth instrument acid 303 tb-303 bass techno
// @provides
//   [nomain] TT-303/tt-303-jsfx-manual.html
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-ui-options/303-front.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-ui-options/303-options.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-acid-machine/tt-303-acid-machine-drum-machine-panel-with-the-kit-dropdown-and-one-r.webp
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-acid-machine/tt-303-acid-machine-fx-panel-with-drive-delay-reverb-and-compressor-se.webp
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-acid-machine/tt-303-acid-machine-header-showing-the-tt-303-logo-the-accent-indicato.webp
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-acid-machine/tt-303-acid-machine-sequencer-panel-with-pattern-banks-a-to-d-the-note.webp
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-acid-machine/tt-303-acid-machine-synth-panel-with-the-eight-sound-shaping-knobs-the.webp
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-acid-machine/tt-303-acid-machine-the-full-tt-303-acid-machine-interface-showing-the.jpg
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-acid-machine/tt-303-acid-machine-transport-bar-detail-highlighting-the-midi-in-out.webp
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-acid-machine/tt-303-acid-machine-transport-bar-with-play-button-bpm-field-preset-co.webp
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-acid-machine/tt-303-acid-machine-tt-303-acid-machine-web-logo.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-jsfx/tt-303-jsfx-logo.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-jsfx/tt-303-jsfx-midi.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-jsfx/tt-303-jsfx-presets.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-jsfx/tt-303-jsfx-save.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-jsfx/tt-303-jsfx-seq.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-jsfx/tt-303-jsfx-sequencer.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/img/tt-303-jsfx/tt-303-jsfx-synth-fx.png
//   [nomain] TT-303/TT-303_manual.html
// @about
//   # TT-303 Acid Machine
//
//   Monophonic acid bass synthesizer in the style of the Roland TB-303.
//   Tribute model, no samples.
//
//   - Oscillator: saw / square, 1-sample PolyBLEP, 2x oversampled
//   - VCF: 18 dB ladder (ZDF/TPT), level-dependent resonance
//   - Slide + accent, internal 16-step sequencer with 4 banks A-D
//   - HOST mode like the Devil Fish MIDI In: note stack 10 deep,
//     sustain on CC 64, accent velocity threshold 65 (DF button steps
//     through 65 / 80 / 100 / 120)
//   - Drive (parallel EQ + WaveShaper), ping-pong delay, Freeverb reverb,
//     compressor with adjustable mix
//   - Fully drawn device front with version display, factory presets
//     and 32 user presets per project
//
//   HOST mode: sound generator from the piano roll. SEQ mode: internal
//   sequencer on the timeline or free-running.
// @changelog
//   2.0.0
//   - First ReaPack release since 1.07. Renumbered from 1.5.0: ReaPack reads 1.07 as 1.7,
//     so 1.5.0 would not be offered as an update. Includes all changes listed below.
//   1.5.0
//   - HOST mode aligned further with the Devil Fish MIDI In: note stack
//     10 deep (oldest falls out), sustain on CC 64 (gate stays on while
//     CC 64 >= 64), accent velocity default 65 with the four Devil Fish
//     thresholds 65/80/100/120 on a DF button; existing projects and
//     presets keep their stored accent velocity
//   1.4.1
//   - HOST mode as the Devil Fish MIDI In: a note-on for a key that is
//     already on is ignored (no retrigger, no hanging note); the first
//     note-off ends it
//   1.4.0
//   - HOST mode: an overlapping note of the same pitch was struck again
//     (replaced by 1.4.1)
//   1.3.4
//   - Persistent UI size and options; larger default, stable colours
//     when zooming
//   1.07
//   - Sound engine recalibrated against reference recordings; slide time
//     sets the arrival time; hotter distortion and +12 dB output make-up
//     (noticeably louder); several HOST/SEQ fixes
//tags: synth instrument acid 303 bass techno
//author: TimTechlor
//about:
// TT-303 ACID MACHINE — mono acid synth in the style of the TB-303.
// Tribute, no samples, no sample ROM, all model.
//
// CONTROLS AS ON THE ORIGINAL
//   TUNING     semitones (-24..+24), plus FINE in cents
//   CUTOFF     filter frequency, ~150 Hz .. ~2 kHz exponential (rises with resonance)
//   RESONANCE  feedback of the 18 dB ladder up to self-oscillation
//   ENV MOD    depth of the filter envelope, up to 5.2 octaves
//   DECAY      decay of the filter envelope, ~30 ms .. ~570 ms
//   ACCENT     level AND filter boost of the accent circuit
//   WAVEFORM   sawtooth / square
//
// MODEL DETAILS (after R. Whittle / Devil Fish documentation)
//  - Filter: 3-pole ladder (18 dB/oct) in ZDF/TPT form,
//    level-dependent feedback k/(1+0.4|y|), 2x oversampled,
//    then 3-point decimation. Soft clip only at the master, never in
//    the OS loop (it never engages there at real levels anyway).
//  - Pole correction 1/(1+0.10*kRes): mild peak correction; the
//    resonance hump moves up with rising resonance, as on the reference.
//  - Feedback HP 20 Hz IN the feedback path (DC block).
//  - Square with frequency-dependent duty + tilt, classic 1-sample PolyBLEP.
//  - Accent capacitor: recharge +0.95, saturation 1.65.
//    Accent sweep with non-linearity and slight cutoff dependency.
//  - On accent: fixed 0.2 s filter decay + shortened VCA attack (1.8 ms).
//  - Slide: constant time, log frequency space; the same note stays held.
//  - FX: delay/reverb bypassed at mix < 0.5 %. EQ OFF = true bypass.
//  - MIDI: notes are consumed, CC/pitchbend keep going.
//
// OPERATING MODES
//   HOST  Pure sound generator, played from the piano roll.
//         Velocity >= threshold = accent, overlapping notes = slide.
//         The same note again while held is ignored (Devil Fish: the first note-off ends it).
//         Last note wins from a stack of 10 held notes (the oldest falls out); CC 64 (sustain) keeps
//         the gate on while its value is >= 64 (Devil Fish). Accent threshold default 65; the DF
//         button steps through the Devil Fish thresholds 65 / 80 / 100 / 120.
//   SEQ   Internal 16-step sequencer, four pattern banks A-D with
//         copy function, random and mutation, shuffle, gate length.
//         Runs on the project timeline or free (FREE RUN).
//         MIDI notes transpose the pattern (C2 = original pitch).
//         MIDI OUT also sends the sequence out.
//         All four banks travel with the project.
//
// Effect path: ahead of each of the three units — WaveShaper (Soft/Hard/
// Fold/Fuzz), ping-pong delay, Freeverb reverb — sits an input EQ
// as a dual slider (lowcut left, highcut right, 0..20 kHz). After that
// compressor (-14 dB, 5:1) and master.
//
// The input EQ only shapes what is sent into each effect; the dry
// signal runs alongside untouched. On the drive what the EQ removes is
// added back after the WaveShaper, so a raised lowcut takes the bass
// out of the DISTORTION, not out of the output (drive off = transparent).
//
// OPTIONS box: FONT SIZE (FONT 1/2) and a custom HSV colour picker
// (FONT 1 / FONT 2 / BG) with RESET / RESET ALL, live and per instance,
// with low-contrast warning; TOOLTIPS ON / OFF (saved with the project),
// tooltips on every control.
//
// A slide into the same note ties (no retrigger, one note-on at SEQ
// OUT); pattern and bank edits create a REAPER undo point and UNDO
// restores the bank it was made in; the mouse wheel steps whole-number
// knobs one step at a time.
//
// PRESETS: bar in the header, left of OPTIONS: [<] [name v] [>] [SAVE] [...].
// FACTORY = INIT, DEEP, SQUELCH, SCREAM, HOOVER, DUB (the former patch buttons);
// USER = 32 slots that travel with the project (@serialize, after the four
// pattern banks; old projects load with an empty bank). A user preset holds
// all sound sliders (2..20, 27..32, 34, 35), the pattern settings (length,
// shuffle, gate, active bank 21/22/23/25) AND the four pattern banks A-D.
// Not part of it: MODE, FREE RUN, SEQ OUT, MIDI THRU, UI Color, transport.
// A native REAPER preset file of this plugin carries the whole bank.
//
// MIDI: THRU at the top of the header passes INCOMING notes on to the
// output (CC and pitchbend always pass through anyway).
// SEQ OUT in the sequencer panel sends the SELF-GENERATED sequence
// out. Two different sources, hence two switches. In SEQ mode incoming
// notes are transpose commands — whoever also passes them on with
// THRU sends them out next to the sequence.
//
// SURFACE after the Tim Techlor design kit: Core Black, Core White,
// Acid Green #39FF14, traces at a 45 degree angle with solder pads.
// Wordmark in Zilap Orion, if installed. Labels sans-serif
// (Segoe UI / Helvetica Neue / DejaVu Sans / Arial), numeric values
// monospaced (Consolas / DejaVu Sans Mono / Menlo / Courier New).
// Which of these is present the script measures itself.
// The front computes in a fixed design grid and scales to the
// window size — to enlarge, just drag the FX window open.
// HiDPI is honoured via gfx_ext_retina. All internal
// JSFX sliders are hidden ("-" before the name), operation is
// exclusively via the device front.

in_pin:none
out_pin:TT-303 L
out_pin:TT-303 R

options:gfx_hz=45 gmem=tt303_acid

slider1:0<0,1,1{HOST,SEQ}>-Mode
slider2:0<0,1,1{Sawtooth,Square}>-Waveform
slider3:0<-24,24,1>-Tuning (semitones)
slider4:0<-50,50,1>-Fine (cents)
slider5:32<0,100,0.1>-Cutoff Freq
slider6:55<0,100,0.1>-Resonance
slider7:62<0,100,0.1>-Env Mod
slider8:35<0,100,0.1>-Decay
slider9:60<0,100,0.1>-Accent
slider10:70<0,100,0.1>-Volume
slider11:60<0,300,1>-Slide time (ms)
slider12:65<1,127,1>-Accent from velocity
slider13:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Distortion
slider14:0<0,3,1{Soft,Hard,Fold,Fuzz}>-Distortion model
slider15:8<1,40,0.1>-Drive
slider16:15<0,100,0.5>-Delay mix (%)
slider17:1<0,3,1{1/8,Dotted 1/8,1/4,1/2}>-Delay division
slider18:60<0,90,1>-Delay feedback (%)
slider19:18<0,100,0.5>-Reverb mix (%)
slider20:70<20,100,1>-Room size (%)
slider21:16<1,16,1>-SEQ pattern length
slider22:0<0,75,1>-SEQ Shuffle (%)
slider23:55<10,100,1>-SEQ Gate (%)
slider24:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-SEQ Free Run
slider25:0<0,3,1{A,B,C,D}>-SEQ pattern bank
slider26:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-SEQ Out (sequence to output)
slider27:0<0,20000,1>-Drive EQ Lowcut (Hz)
slider28:20000<20,20000,1>-Drive EQ Highcut (Hz)
slider29:250<0,20000,1>-Delay EQ Lowcut (Hz)
slider30:3000<20,20000,1>-Delay EQ Highcut (Hz)
slider31:300<0,20000,1>-Reverb EQ Lowcut (Hz)
slider32:2300<20,20000,1>-Reverb EQ Highcut (Hz)
slider33:0<0,1,1{Off,On}>-MIDI Thru (incoming notes)
slider34:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Compressor
slider35:100<0,100,1>-Compressor mix
slider36:0<0,9,1>-UI Color
slider37:0<0,31,1>-Q IDX (test)
slider38:0<0,20,1>-Q CMD (test)
slider39:0<-1000000000,1000000000,1>-Q A (ro)
slider40:0<-1000000000,1000000000,1>-Q B (ro)

/* ============================================================
   @init — memory map, functions, base state.
   Functions must come BEFORE their first use, which is why
   everything sits together here.
   ============================================================ */
options:want_all_kb

@init
// __THEME_BEGIN__   // generated from _shared/tt-theme.jsfx-inc
// ==========================  TT-Theme (THEME_VER 5)  ==================
// Ten colour schemes (accent + secondary + tinted base) and the OPTIONS box
// with style options: font sizes, custom HSV colour picker (FONT 1 / FONT 2 / BG).
// Generated by _shared/tt_theme_gen.py - do not edit by hand.
// Integration in the product (details: _shared/THEME.md):
//   @init   : tth_sync(sliderN);                 // scheme from the hidden slider
//   @gfx    : tth_pre();  tth_sync(sliderN);     // AT THE VERY TOP (masks the mouse while the box is open)
//             ... draw the front ...
//             c = tth_post(px, py, sc);          // AT THE VERY END; px/py = button top left in window pixels, sc = scale
//             c >= 0 ? ( sliderN = c; slider_automate(sliderN); );
// Globals (prefix tth_ / acc*): accR/G/B = accent, tth_dmR.. = dimmed accent (contrast-raised,
// WCAG >= 4.5 against panel), tth_alR.. = secondary colour, tth_ikR.. = primary text (ink, tinted),
// tth_bgR.. base, tth_pnR.. panel, tth_bdR.. border, tth_knR.. knob face.
// Style options (per instance, serialized by the preset module - block TTPB_MAG2):
// tth_f1sz/tth_f2sz = font steps -4..+8 (slot 1 = title, slots 2..5 = text; the kit scales in uikit_begin);
// tth_f1on/f2on + tth_f1R../f2R.. = custom text colours; tth_bgon + tth_bgUR.. = custom base
// (pn/bd/kn follow with the scheme offset, see tth_bgmix).
THEME_VER = 5;
TTH_FONT  = 10;      // font slot of the box (products use 1..5 and 9)
tth_on    = 1;
tth_cur   = -1;      // last applied scheme
// tth_open/tth_hold are not reset on every @init - @init runs again at
// every transport start; a reset with the button held would cause a
// phantom click on the OPTIONS button in the next frame.
tth_ini1 != 1 ? ( tth_ini1 = 1; tth_pcap = 0; );       // tth_pcap = mouse_cap of the previous frame (edge detection)
tth_fsCur = 0;
tth_tint  = 0;       // 1 = tint greys with the accent (schemes 5..9)
tth_bx = 0; tth_by = 0; tth_bw = 0; tth_bh = 0;   // button rectangle (for masking in the next frame)

// Style state: deliberately initialised only on the first @init (a re-init
// on samplerate/transport start must not lose the chosen options).
tth_styok != 1 ? (
  tth_styok = 1;
  tth_uisize = 125; tth_panx = 0; tth_pany = 0; // larger default; saved per instance
  tth_f1sz = 0; tth_f2sz = 0;                 // font steps -4..+8
  tth_f1on = 0; tth_f2on = 0; tth_bgon = 0;   // custom colours active?
  tth_f1R = 0.92; tth_f1G = 0.95; tth_f1B = 0.92;
  tth_f2R = 0.92; tth_f2G = 0.95; tth_f2B = 0.92;
  tth_bgUR = 0.050; tth_bgUG = 0.054; tth_bgUB = 0.050;
  tth_ctgt = 0;                              // picker target: 0 = FONT 1, 1 = FONT 2, 2 = BG
  tth_ch = 0.30; tth_cs = 0.85; tth_cv = 0.9; // HSV of the picker
  tth_cdrag = 0;                             // 1 = SV field, 2 = hue bar
);

// ---------- WCAG contrast (runtime: warning + helper) ----------
function tth_lin(c) ( c <= 0.04045 ? c/12.92 : ((c + 0.055)/1.055)^2.4; );

// contrast ratio (L light + 0.05)/(L dark + 0.05)
function tth_cr(r1, g1, b1, r2, g2, b2) local(l1, l2, t) (
  l1 = 0.2126*tth_lin(r1) + 0.7152*tth_lin(g1) + 0.0722*tth_lin(b1);
  l2 = 0.2126*tth_lin(r2) + 0.7152*tth_lin(g2) + 0.0722*tth_lin(b2);
  l1 < l2 ? ( t = l1; l1 = l2; l2 = t; );
  (l1 + 0.05)/(l2 + 0.05);
);

// ---------- HSV <-> RGB for the colour picker ----------
// tth_hsv(h, s, v): result in tth_hr/hg/hb
function tth_hsv(h, s, v) local(i, f, p, q, t) (
  h -= floor(h); i = floor(h*6); f = h*6 - i;
  p = v*(1 - s); q = v*(1 - s*f); t = v*(1 - s*(1 - f));
  i == 0 ? ( tth_hr = v; tth_hg = t; tth_hb = p; )
  : i == 1 ? ( tth_hr = q; tth_hg = v; tth_hb = p; )
  : i == 2 ? ( tth_hr = p; tth_hg = v; tth_hb = t; )
  : i == 3 ? ( tth_hr = p; tth_hg = q; tth_hb = v; )
  : i == 4 ? ( tth_hr = t; tth_hg = p; tth_hb = v; )
  : ( tth_hr = v; tth_hg = p; tth_hb = q; );
);

// tth_rgb2hsv(r, g, b): result in tth_ch/cs/cv (picker state)
function tth_rgb2hsv(r, g, b) local(mx, mn, dd, h) (
  mx = max(r, max(g, b)); mn = min(r, min(g, b)); dd = mx - mn;
  h = 0;
  dd > 0.000001 ? (
    mx == r ? h = (g - b)/dd : mx == g ? h = 2 + (b - r)/dd : h = 4 + (r - g)/dd;
    h < 0 ? h += 6;
    h /= 6;
  );
  tth_ch = h; tth_cs = mx > 0.000001 ? dd/mx : 0; tth_cv = mx;
);

// Apply custom base: tth_bg = desired colour, pn/bd/kn follow with the
// offset of the active scheme (snapshot tth_s* on scheme change).
function tth_bgmix() (
  tth_bgR = tth_bgUR; tth_bgG = tth_bgUG; tth_bgB = tth_bgUB;
  tth_pnR = min(1, max(0, tth_spnR + (tth_bgUR - tth_sbgR)));
  tth_pnG = min(1, max(0, tth_spnG + (tth_bgUG - tth_sbgG)));
  tth_pnB = min(1, max(0, tth_spnB + (tth_bgUB - tth_sbgB)));
  tth_bdR = min(1, max(0, tth_sbdR + (tth_bgUR - tth_sbgR)));
  tth_bdG = min(1, max(0, tth_sbdG + (tth_bgUG - tth_sbgG)));
  tth_bdB = min(1, max(0, tth_sbdB + (tth_bgUB - tth_sbgB)));
  tth_knR = min(1, max(0, tth_sknR + (tth_bgUR - tth_sbgR)));
  tth_knG = min(1, max(0, tth_sknG + (tth_bgUG - tth_sbgG)));
  tth_knB = min(1, max(0, tth_sknB + (tth_bgUB - tth_sbgB)));
);

function tth_apply(i) (
  i = max(0, min(9, floor(i + 0.5)));
  tth_cur = i;
  i == 0 ? ( tth_tint = 0; accR = 0.224; accG = 1.000; accB = 0.078; tth_dmR = 0.128; tth_dmG = 0.570; tth_dmB = 0.044; tth_alR = 1.000; tth_alG = 0.702; tth_alB = 0.361; tth_ikR = 0.750; tth_ikG = 0.810; tth_ikB = 0.750; tth_bgR = 0.050; tth_bgG = 0.054; tth_bgB = 0.050; tth_pnR = 0.072; tth_pnG = 0.077; tth_pnB = 0.072; tth_bdR = 0.125; tth_bdG = 0.155; tth_bdB = 0.115; tth_knR = 0.105; tth_knG = 0.110; tth_knB = 0.105; ) :
  i == 1 ? ( tth_tint = 0; accR = 0.133; accG = 0.827; accB = 0.933; tth_dmR = 0.088; tth_dmG = 0.546; tth_dmB = 0.616; tth_alR = 1.000; tth_alG = 0.620; tth_alB = 0.300; tth_ikR = 0.750; tth_ikG = 0.810; tth_ikB = 0.750; tth_bgR = 0.050; tth_bgG = 0.054; tth_bgB = 0.050; tth_pnR = 0.072; tth_pnG = 0.077; tth_pnB = 0.072; tth_bdR = 0.125; tth_bdG = 0.155; tth_bdB = 0.115; tth_knR = 0.105; tth_knG = 0.110; tth_knB = 0.105; ) :
  i == 2 ? ( tth_tint = 0; accR = 1.000; accG = 0.353; accB = 0.122; tth_dmR = 0.860; tth_dmG = 0.304; tth_dmB = 0.105; tth_alR = 0.350; tth_alG = 0.850; tth_alB = 1.000; tth_ikR = 0.750; tth_ikG = 0.810; tth_ikB = 0.750; tth_bgR = 0.050; tth_bgG = 0.054; tth_bgB = 0.050; tth_pnR = 0.072; tth_pnG = 0.077; tth_pnB = 0.072; tth_bdR = 0.125; tth_bdG = 0.155; tth_bdB = 0.115; tth_knR = 0.105; tth_knG = 0.110; tth_knB = 0.105; ) :
  i == 3 ? ( tth_tint = 0; accR = 0.878; accG = 0.251; accB = 0.984; tth_dmR = 0.790; tth_dmG = 0.226; tth_dmB = 0.886; tth_alR = 0.350; tth_alG = 1.000; tth_alB = 0.750; tth_ikR = 0.750; tth_ikG = 0.810; tth_ikB = 0.750; tth_bgR = 0.050; tth_bgG = 0.054; tth_bgB = 0.050; tth_pnR = 0.072; tth_pnG = 0.077; tth_pnB = 0.072; tth_bdR = 0.125; tth_bdG = 0.155; tth_bdB = 0.115; tth_knR = 0.105; tth_knG = 0.110; tth_knB = 0.105; ) :
  i == 4 ? ( tth_tint = 0; accR = 1.000; accG = 0.839; accB = 0.039; tth_dmR = 0.580; tth_dmG = 0.487; tth_dmB = 0.023; tth_alR = 0.450; tth_alG = 0.750; tth_alB = 1.000; tth_ikR = 0.750; tth_ikG = 0.810; tth_ikB = 0.750; tth_bgR = 0.050; tth_bgG = 0.054; tth_bgB = 0.050; tth_pnR = 0.072; tth_pnG = 0.077; tth_pnB = 0.072; tth_bdR = 0.125; tth_bdG = 0.155; tth_bdB = 0.115; tth_knR = 0.105; tth_knG = 0.110; tth_knB = 0.105; ) :
  i == 5 ? ( tth_tint = 1; accR = 1.000; accG = 0.176; accB = 0.333; tth_dmR = 0.940; tth_dmG = 0.165; tth_dmB = 0.313; tth_alR = 1.000; tth_alG = 0.780; tth_alB = 0.350; tth_ikR = 0.805; tth_ikG = 0.752; tth_ikB = 0.768; tth_bgR = 0.058; tth_bgG = 0.050; tth_bgB = 0.051; tth_pnR = 0.082; tth_pnG = 0.070; tth_pnB = 0.073; tth_bdR = 0.155; tth_bdG = 0.120; tth_bdB = 0.127; tth_knR = 0.110; tth_knG = 0.105; tth_knB = 0.106; ) :
  i == 6 ? ( tth_tint = 1; accR = 0.300; accG = 0.550; accB = 1.000; tth_dmR = 0.264; tth_dmG = 0.484; tth_dmB = 0.880; tth_alR = 1.000; tth_alG = 0.750; tth_alB = 0.300; tth_ikR = 0.755; tth_ikG = 0.778; tth_ikB = 0.815; tth_bgR = 0.051; tth_bgG = 0.053; tth_bgB = 0.058; tth_pnR = 0.072; tth_pnG = 0.076; tth_pnB = 0.082; tth_bdR = 0.126; tth_bdG = 0.136; tth_bdB = 0.155; tth_knR = 0.106; tth_knG = 0.107; tth_knB = 0.110; ) :
  i == 7 ? ( tth_tint = 1; accR = 0.620; accG = 0.480; accB = 1.000; tth_dmR = 0.533; tth_dmG = 0.413; tth_dmB = 0.860; tth_alR = 1.000; tth_alG = 0.720; tth_alB = 0.400; tth_ikR = 0.778; tth_ikG = 0.773; tth_ikB = 0.815; tth_bgR = 0.054; tth_bgG = 0.053; tth_bgB = 0.058; tth_pnR = 0.077; tth_pnG = 0.075; tth_pnB = 0.082; tth_bdR = 0.139; tth_bdG = 0.133; tth_bdB = 0.155; tth_knR = 0.108; tth_knG = 0.107; tth_knB = 0.110; ) :
  i == 8 ? ( tth_tint = 1; accR = 0.176; accG = 0.886; accB = 0.651; tth_dmR = 0.113; tth_dmG = 0.567; tth_dmB = 0.417; tth_alR = 1.000; tth_alG = 0.600; tth_alB = 0.450; tth_ikR = 0.747; tth_ikG = 0.802; tth_ikB = 0.790; tth_bgR = 0.050; tth_bgG = 0.058; tth_bgB = 0.055; tth_pnR = 0.071; tth_pnG = 0.082; tth_pnB = 0.078; tth_bdR = 0.121; tth_bdG = 0.155; tth_bdB = 0.144; tth_knR = 0.105; tth_knG = 0.110; tth_knB = 0.108; ) :
  ( tth_tint = 1; accR = 0.900; accG = 0.930; accB = 0.960; tth_dmR = 0.495; tth_dmG = 0.512; tth_dmB = 0.528; tth_alR = 1.000; tth_alG = 0.700; tth_alB = 0.360; tth_ikR = 0.798; tth_ikG = 0.805; tth_ikB = 0.812; tth_bgR = 0.057; tth_bgG = 0.058; tth_bgB = 0.058; tth_pnR = 0.081; tth_pnG = 0.082; tth_pnB = 0.082; tth_bdR = 0.152; tth_bdG = 0.154; tth_bdB = 0.155; tth_knR = 0.110; tth_knG = 0.110; tth_knB = 0.110; );
  // scheme snapshot (basis for the BG offset) + custom base
  tth_sbgR = tth_bgR; tth_sbgG = tth_bgG; tth_sbgB = tth_bgB;
  tth_spnR = tth_pnR; tth_spnG = tth_pnG; tth_spnB = tth_pnB;
  tth_sbdR = tth_bdR; tth_sbdG = tth_bdG; tth_sbdB = tth_bdB;
  tth_sknR = tth_knR; tth_sknG = tth_knG; tth_sknB = tth_knB;
  tth_bgon ? tth_bgmix();
);

// scheme i for drawing the preview only: accent (tth_sa), secondary (tth_sl), base (tth_sg) - does not change the active scheme
function tth_swatch(i) (
  i == 0 ? ( tth_saR = 0.224; tth_saG = 1.000; tth_saB = 0.078; tth_slR = 1.000; tth_slG = 0.702; tth_slB = 0.361; tth_sgR = 0.050; tth_sgG = 0.054; tth_sgB = 0.050; ) :
  i == 1 ? ( tth_saR = 0.133; tth_saG = 0.827; tth_saB = 0.933; tth_slR = 1.000; tth_slG = 0.620; tth_slB = 0.300; tth_sgR = 0.050; tth_sgG = 0.054; tth_sgB = 0.050; ) :
  i == 2 ? ( tth_saR = 1.000; tth_saG = 0.353; tth_saB = 0.122; tth_slR = 0.350; tth_slG = 0.850; tth_slB = 1.000; tth_sgR = 0.050; tth_sgG = 0.054; tth_sgB = 0.050; ) :
  i == 3 ? ( tth_saR = 0.878; tth_saG = 0.251; tth_saB = 0.984; tth_slR = 0.350; tth_slG = 1.000; tth_slB = 0.750; tth_sgR = 0.050; tth_sgG = 0.054; tth_sgB = 0.050; ) :
  i == 4 ? ( tth_saR = 1.000; tth_saG = 0.839; tth_saB = 0.039; tth_slR = 0.450; tth_slG = 0.750; tth_slB = 1.000; tth_sgR = 0.050; tth_sgG = 0.054; tth_sgB = 0.050; ) :
  i == 5 ? ( tth_saR = 1.000; tth_saG = 0.176; tth_saB = 0.333; tth_slR = 1.000; tth_slG = 0.780; tth_slB = 0.350; tth_sgR = 0.058; tth_sgG = 0.050; tth_sgB = 0.051; ) :
  i == 6 ? ( tth_saR = 0.300; tth_saG = 0.550; tth_saB = 1.000; tth_slR = 1.000; tth_slG = 0.750; tth_slB = 0.300; tth_sgR = 0.051; tth_sgG = 0.053; tth_sgB = 0.058; ) :
  i == 7 ? ( tth_saR = 0.620; tth_saG = 0.480; tth_saB = 1.000; tth_slR = 1.000; tth_slG = 0.720; tth_slB = 0.400; tth_sgR = 0.054; tth_sgG = 0.053; tth_sgB = 0.058; ) :
  i == 8 ? ( tth_saR = 0.176; tth_saG = 0.886; tth_saB = 0.651; tth_slR = 1.000; tth_slG = 0.600; tth_slB = 0.450; tth_sgR = 0.050; tth_sgG = 0.058; tth_sgB = 0.055; ) :
  ( tth_saR = 0.900; tth_saG = 0.930; tth_saB = 0.960; tth_slR = 1.000; tth_slG = 0.700; tth_slB = 0.360; tth_sgR = 0.057; tth_sgG = 0.058; tth_sgB = 0.058; );
);

function tth_name(i) (
  i == 0 ? "ACID" : i == 1 ? "CYAN" : i == 2 ? "ORANGE" : i == 3 ? "MAGENTA" : i == 4 ? "YELLOW"
  : i == 5 ? "RED" : i == 6 ? "BLUE" : i == 7 ? "VIOLET" : i == 8 ? "MINT" : "ICE";
);

// Tint (schemes 5..9 only; the classic 0..4 leave the greys unchanged): transfers a greenish-tinted grey value (r,g,b - acid look) into the active scheme; exactly neutral on ACID.
function tth_tn(r, g, b, a) local(f) (
  f = tth_tint ? max(0, (g - (r + b)*0.5)/0.849) : 0;
  gfx_set(min(1, max(0, r + f*(accR - 0.224))), min(1, max(0, g + f*(accG - 1.000))), min(1, max(0, b + f*(accB - 0.078))), a);
);

// Text colour of the font slots: FONT 1 = slot 1 (title), FONT 2 = slots 2..5 (text).
// Called at the end of the kit text functions before gfx_drawstr; the caller's alpha is kept.
// Does nothing without a custom colour (tth_f*on = 0).
function tth_txt() local(f) (
  f = gfx_getfont(#tth_tf) + 1;      // gfx_getfont returns the slot MINUS 1
  (tth_f1on && f == 1) ? gfx_set(tth_f1R, tth_f1G, tth_f1B, gfx_a)
  : (tth_f2on && f >= 2 && f <= 5) ? gfx_set(tth_f2R, tth_f2G, tth_f2B, gfx_a);
);

function tth_sync(v) ( v != tth_cur ? tth_apply(v); );

function tth_inbox(x, y, w, h) ( tth_rmx >= x && tth_rmx < x + w && tth_rmy >= y && tth_rmy < y + h; );


// UI zoom: real vector drawing at the chosen size, not a scaled bitmap.
// JSFX cannot enlarge its host window. On overflow the whole front stays
// reachable via the scrollbars; OPTIONS stays fixed at the visible top edge.
function tth_view(w, h) local(vw, vh, cw, ch) (
  tth_vw = w; tth_vh = h;
  SC = tth_uisize / 100;
  cw = w*SC; ch = h*SC;
  vw = gfx_w; vh = gfx_h;
  tth_vbar = ch > vh; tth_hbar = cw > vw - 14*tth_vbar;
  tth_vbar = ch > vh - 14*tth_hbar;
  tth_visw = max(1, vw - 14*tth_vbar); tth_vish = max(1, vh - 14*tth_hbar);
  tth_maxx = max(0, cw - tth_visw); tth_maxy = max(0, ch - tth_vish);
  tth_panx = max(0, min(tth_maxx, tth_panx)); tth_pany = max(0, min(tth_maxy, tth_pany));
  OX = max(0, (tth_visw - cw)*0.5) - tth_panx;
  OY = max(0, (tth_vish - ch)*0.5) - tth_pany;
  mX = (mouse_x - OX)/SC; mY = (mouse_y - OY)/SC;
);
function tth_parsepercent(s) local(n,i,k,v,ok) (
  n=strlen(s); i=0; v=0; ok=n>0 && n<=3;
  loop(n, k=str_getchar(s,i); ok=ok && k>=48 && k<=57; v=v*10+k-48; i+=1; );
  ok && v>0 ? v : 0;
);
function tth_size(v) (
  v = max(50, min(400, floor(v + 0.5)));
  v != tth_uisize ? ( tth_uisize = v; tth_panx = 0; tth_pany = 0; tt_undoreq = 1; );
);
function tth_sizekey(k) local(v) (
k==13 ? ( v=tth_parsepercent(#tth_szinput); v>0 ? tth_size(v); tth_edit=0; )
        : k==27 ? tth_edit=0
        : k==8 ? ( tth_editfirst=0; strcpy_substr(#tth_szback,#tth_szinput,0,max(0,strlen(#tth_szinput)-1)); strcpy(#tth_szinput,#tth_szback); )
        : k>=48 && k<=57 ? (
          tth_editfirst ? ( strcpy(#tth_szinput,""); tth_editfirst=0; );
          strlen(#tth_szinput)<3 ? ( sprintf(#tth_szchar,"%c",k); strcat(#tth_szinput,#tth_szchar); );
        );
);
// Help texts of the OPTIONS/scroll elements use window pixels and the raw mouse.
function tth_hint(x,y,w,h,s) (
  tth_inbox(x,y,w,h) ? ( strcpy(#tth_help,s); tth_helpon = 1; );
);
function tth_hintflush() local(t,x,y,w,h,fs,n,st,e,k,nl,lw,lh,d) (
  tth_helpon && !tth_tipoff && !(tth_rcap0 & 1) ? (
    t = time_precise();
    strcmp(#tth_help,#tth_helpprev) ? ( strcpy(#tth_helpprev,#tth_help); tth_helptime = t; );
    t - tth_helptime >= 0.35 ? (
      fs = max(11, floor(12*min(2,tth_uisize/100)+0.5));
      gfx_setfont(16,"Arial",fs);
      // keep long help fully inside the window even at 300 %; measure the real line width.
      n=strlen(#tth_help); st=0; nl=0; w=0;
      loop(4,
        st<n ? (
          e=n; d=nl==0 ? #tth_hl0 : nl==1 ? #tth_hl1 : nl==2 ? #tth_hl2 : #tth_hl3;
          strcpy_substr(d,#tth_help,st,e-st); gfx_measurestr(d,lw,lh);
          while(lw>max(1,gfx_w-16) && e>st+1) (
            e-=1; strcpy_substr(d,#tth_help,st,e-st); gfx_measurestr(d,lw,lh);
          );
          e<n ? (
            k=e; while(k>st+1 && str_getchar(#tth_help,k)!=32) ( k-=1; );
            k>st+1 ? ( e=k; strcpy_substr(d,#tth_help,st,e-st); gfx_measurestr(d,lw,lh); );
          );
          w=max(w,lw); st=e; str_getchar(#tth_help,st)==32 ? st+=1; nl+=1;
        );
      );
      w += 16; h = nl*lh+10;
      x = max(0,min(tth_rmx+14,gfx_w-w)); y = max(0,min(tth_rmy+18,gfx_h-h));
      gfx_set(tth_bgR,tth_bgG,tth_bgB,1); gfx_rect(x,y,w,h,1);
      gfx_set(accR,accG,accB,1); gfx_rect(x,y,w,h,0);
      gfx_set(tth_ikR,tth_ikG,tth_ikB,1); k=0;
      loop(nl, d=k==0 ? #tth_hl0 : k==1 ? #tth_hl1 : k==2 ? #tth_hl2 : #tth_hl3;
        gfx_x=x+8; gfx_y=y+5+k*lh; gfx_drawstr(d); k+=1;
      );
    );
  ) : strcpy(#tth_helpprev,"");
  tth_helpon = 0;
);
function tth_scrollbars() local(l,p) (
  tth_hbar ? (
    gfx_set(tth_bgR,tth_bgG,tth_bgB,1); gfx_rect(0,tth_vish,tth_visw,14,1);
    l=max(24,tth_visw*tth_visw/(tth_vw*SC)); p=tth_maxx>0 ? tth_panx/tth_maxx*(tth_visw-l) : 0;
    gfx_set(accR,accG,accB,0.8); gfx_rect(p,tth_vish+3,l,8,1);
    tth_hint(0,tth_vish,tth_visw,14,"Scroll horizontally to reach the enlarged front.");
  );
  tth_vbar ? (
    gfx_set(tth_bgR,tth_bgG,tth_bgB,1); gfx_rect(tth_visw,0,14,tth_vish,1);
    l=max(24,tth_vish*tth_vish/(tth_vh*SC)); p=tth_maxy>0 ? tth_pany/tth_maxy*(tth_vish-l) : 0;
    gfx_set(accR,accG,accB,0.8); gfx_rect(tth_visw+3,p,8,l,1);
    tth_hint(tth_visw,0,14,tth_vish,"Scroll vertically to reach the enlarged front.");
  );
);

// Small button of the box: panel + border (accent when hot/on), text centred in the accent colour.
function tth_sbtn(x, y, w, h, s, hot, on) (
  gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); gfx_rect(x, y, w, h, 1);
  (hot || on) ? gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.95) : gfx_set(tth_bdR, tth_bdG, tth_bdB, 1);
  gfx_rect(x, y, w, h, 0);
  gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, (hot || on) ? 1 : 0.85);
  gfx_measurestr(s, tth_tw, tth_th);
  gfx_x = x + (w - tth_tw)*0.5; gfx_y = y + (h - tth_th)*0.5; gfx_drawstr(s);
);

// Active colour of the picker target (for preview + write-back into the picker)
function tth_tgtcol() (
  tth_ctgt == 0 ? ( tth_tr = tth_f1on ? tth_f1R : accR;       tth_tg = tth_f1on ? tth_f1G : accG;        tth_tb = tth_f1on ? tth_f1B : accB; )
  : tth_ctgt == 1 ? ( tth_tr = tth_f2on ? tth_f2R : tth_ikR;  tth_tg = tth_f2on ? tth_f2G : tth_ikG;     tth_tb = tth_f2on ? tth_f2B : tth_ikB; )
  : ( tth_tr = tth_bgR; tth_tg = tth_bgG; tth_tb = tth_bgB; );
);

// Apply the picker colour (tth_ch/cs/cv -> RGB) live to the target
function tth_pick() (
  tth_hsv(tth_ch, tth_cs, tth_cv);
  tth_ctgt == 0 ? ( tth_f1on = 1; tth_f1R = tth_hr; tth_f1G = tth_hg; tth_f1B = tth_hb; )
  : tth_ctgt == 1 ? ( tth_f2on = 1; tth_f2R = tth_hr; tth_f2G = tth_hg; tth_f2B = tth_hb; )
  : ( tth_bgon = 1; tth_bgUR = tth_hr; tth_bgUG = tth_hg; tth_bgUB = tth_hb; tth_bgmix(); );
);

// Reset one target to the scheme (text colours take effect when drawing, the base via re-applying)
function tth_reset_tgt() (
  tth_ctgt == 0 ? ( tth_f1on = 0; )
  : tth_ctgt == 1 ? ( tth_f2on = 0; )
  : ( tth_bgon = 0; tth_apply(tth_cur); );
);

// Test hook: only active when the product sets tth_test = 1 (and has declared options:gmem).
// gmem[5190] = command, written back to 0 after execution:
//   1 = open box, 2 = close,
//   3 = set style: gmem[5191]=f1sz, [5192]=f2sz, [5193]=target(-1 = none, 0/1/2), [5194..5196]=h/s/v,
//       [5197] = -1 RESET target, -2 RESET ALL
//   4 = style state -> gmem[5200..5211] (f1sz,f2sz,f1on,f1rgb,f2on,f2rgb,bgon,bgUrgb)
//   5 = WCAG contrasts -> gmem[5200..5206] (dm/ik/al/acc against pn, dm/ik/acc against bg)
//   6 = set scheme (gmem[5191] = 0..9)
//   7 = set tooltips (gmem[5191] = 1 on / 0 off); command 4 also reports tth_tipoff in gmem[5214]
// NOTE: deliberately placed after tth_pick/tth_reset_tgt — EEL2 compiles a function body only
// on first call; calling a not-yet-defined function is a runtime error.
// Base address of the test cells. Default 5190; a product whose gmem namespace holds its own
// data there (TT-TRUEAB / TT-FREIRAUM: ring in the ttab namespace) sets tth_gmb to a free area
// BEFORE the module. The comments above name the default addresses (5190 = tth_gmb).
tth_gmb == 0 ? ( tth_gmb = 5190; );
// Suite test unlock. Test scripts first write the token 20261001 to gmem[tth_gmb - 1].
// Without the token the theme test hook AND all writing test commands of the products are inert
// (products check tt_testok() before every destructive test command). tth_test is no longer needed.
function tt_testok() ( gmem[tth_gmb - 1] == 20261001; );
function tth_testcmd() (
  tth_gm = gmem[tth_gmb];
  tth_gm == 1 ? ( tth_open = 1; gmem[tth_gmb] = 0; )
  : tth_gm == 2 ? ( tth_open = 0; gmem[tth_gmb] = 0; )
  : tth_gm == 3 ? (
      tth_f1sz = max(-4, min(8, floor(gmem[tth_gmb + 1]))); tth_f2sz = max(-4, min(8, floor(gmem[tth_gmb + 2])));
      gmem[tth_gmb + 3] >= 0 ? (
        tth_ctgt = max(0, min(2, floor(gmem[tth_gmb + 3])));
        tth_ch = gmem[tth_gmb + 4]; tth_cs = gmem[tth_gmb + 5]; tth_cv = gmem[tth_gmb + 6]; tth_pick();
      );
      gmem[tth_gmb + 7] == -1 ? tth_reset_tgt()
      : gmem[tth_gmb + 7] == -2 ? ( tth_f1on = 0; tth_f2on = 0; tth_bgon = 0; tth_f1sz = 0; tth_f2sz = 0; tth_apply(tth_cur); );
      gmem[tth_gmb] = 0;
    )
  : tth_gm == 4 ? (
      gmem[tth_gmb + 10] = tth_f1sz; gmem[tth_gmb + 11] = tth_f2sz;
      gmem[tth_gmb + 12] = tth_f1on; gmem[tth_gmb + 13] = tth_f1R; gmem[tth_gmb + 14] = tth_f1G; gmem[tth_gmb + 15] = tth_f1B;
      gmem[tth_gmb + 16] = tth_f2on; gmem[tth_gmb + 17] = tth_f2R; gmem[tth_gmb + 18] = tth_f2G; gmem[tth_gmb + 19] = tth_f2B;
      gmem[tth_gmb + 20] = tth_bgon; gmem[tth_gmb + 21] = tth_bgUR; gmem[tth_gmb + 22] = tth_bgUG; gmem[tth_gmb + 23] = tth_bgUB;
      gmem[tth_gmb + 24] = tth_tipoff;
      gmem[tth_gmb + 25] = tth_uisize; gmem[tth_gmb + 26] = tth_panx; gmem[tth_gmb + 27] = tth_pany;
      gmem[tth_gmb + 28] = tth_ctgt; gmem[tth_gmb + 29] = SC; gmem[tth_gmb + 30] = tth_cur;
      gmem[tth_gmb] = 0;
    )
  : tth_gm == 5 ? (
      gmem[tth_gmb + 10] = tth_cr(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB);
      gmem[tth_gmb + 11] = tth_cr(tth_ikR, tth_ikG, tth_ikB, tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB);
      gmem[tth_gmb + 12] = tth_cr(tth_alR, tth_alG, tth_alB, tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB);
      gmem[tth_gmb + 13] = tth_cr(accR, accG, accB, tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB);
      gmem[tth_gmb + 14] = tth_cr(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, tth_bgR, tth_bgG, tth_bgB);
      gmem[tth_gmb + 15] = tth_cr(tth_ikR, tth_ikG, tth_ikB, tth_bgR, tth_bgG, tth_bgB);
      gmem[tth_gmb + 16] = tth_cr(accR, accG, accB, tth_bgR, tth_bgG, tth_bgB);
      gmem[tth_gmb] = 0;
    )
  : tth_gm == 6 ? ( tth_apply(max(0, min(9, floor(gmem[tth_gmb + 1])))); gmem[tth_gmb] = 0; )
  : tth_gm == 7 ? ( tth_tipoff = gmem[tth_gmb + 1] > 0.5 ? 0 : 1; gmem[tth_gmb] = 0; )
  : tth_gm == 8 ? ( tth_size(gmem[tth_gmb + 1]); gmem[tth_gmb] = 0; );
);

// ---------- Host notifications from @gfx ----------
// A plain slider assignment and sliderchange(mask) do NOT create an undo point; slider_automate(mask)
// does (sliders 1..63 via the mask 2^(n-1); slider 64 in variable form only). @slider never runs on
// assignments from @gfx - products re-derive their parameters via tt_sldirty (check and clear in @block).
// tt_slset(n, v): set slider n (1..63) from @gfx and notify the host. Returns 1 on change.
function tt_slset(n, v) (
  abs(slider(n) - v) > 0.0000001 ? ( slider(n) = v; slider_automate(2^(n - 1)); tt_sldirty = 1; 1; ) : 0;
);
// tt_undo(): state WITHOUT a slider changed (pattern, curve, preset bank, stored parameter). The undo
// point (sliderchange(-1), "Edit FX") is created once when the mouse button is released - tth_post triggers it.
function tt_undo() ( tt_undoreq = 1; );

// At the top of @gfx: remember the real mouse; while the box is open the product sees no mouse.
// Also masks the closing click (tth_hold, until the button is released) and the click on the button itself.
function tth_pre() (
  tth_rmx = mouse_x; tth_rmy = mouse_y; tth_rcap = mouse_cap; tth_rcap0 = mouse_cap;   // tth_rcap0: stays raw (tt_pb_pre zeroes tth_rcap while an overlay is open)

  tth_helpon = 0;
  // scrollbars mask the front beneath them; start a drag only on a real click edge.
  !(tth_rcap & 1) ? tth_sdrag = 0;
  tth_shot = !tth_open && !tt_pb_open && ((tth_hbar && tth_rmy >= tth_vish) || (tth_vbar && tth_rmx >= tth_visw));
  (tth_shot && (tth_rcap & 1) && !(tth_pcap & 1)) ? (
    tth_sdrag = tth_vbar && tth_rmx >= tth_visw ? 2 : 1;
  );
  tth_sdrag == 1 ? (
    tth_slen=max(24,tth_visw*tth_visw/(tth_vw*tth_uisize/100));
    tth_panx=max(0,min(tth_maxx,(tth_rmx-tth_slen*0.5)/max(1,tth_visw-tth_slen)*tth_maxx));
  ) : tth_sdrag == 2 ? (
    tth_slen=max(24,tth_vish*tth_vish/(tth_vh*tth_uisize/100));
    tth_pany=max(0,min(tth_maxy,(tth_rmy-tth_slen*0.5)/max(1,tth_vish-tth_slen)*tth_maxy));
  );
  (tth_shot || tth_sdrag) && mouse_wheel != 0 ? (
    tth_vbar && tth_rmx >= tth_visw ? tth_pany=max(0,min(tth_maxy,tth_pany-mouse_wheel/120*40))
    : tth_panx=max(0,min(tth_maxx,tth_panx-mouse_wheel/120*40));
  );
  (tth_shot || tth_sdrag) ? ( mouse_cap=0; mouse_x=-10000; mouse_y=-10000; mouse_wheel=0; );

  tt_testok() ? tth_testcmd();      // unlock via token instead of tth_test
  tth_open ? ( tth_hold = 1; );
  (tth_hold && (tth_rcap & 1) == 0 && !tth_open) ? ( tth_hold = 0; );
  // the button masks only when the press did NOT start outside it - otherwise a knob drag crossing
  // the button would break off and leaving would show the product a click edge (phantom click).
  tth_ib = tth_bw > 0 && tth_rmx >= tth_bx && tth_rmx < tth_bx + tth_bw && tth_rmy >= tth_by && tth_rmy < tth_by + tth_bh;
  (tth_rcap & 1) == 0 ? ( tth_dnout = 0; ) : ( !(tth_pcap & 1) ? ( tth_dnout = !tth_ib; ); );
  (tth_open || tth_hold || (tth_ib && !tth_dnout))
    ? ( mouse_cap = 0; mouse_x = -10000; mouse_y = -10000; mouse_wheel = 0; );
);

// At the end of @gfx: draw button + box. Returns: newly chosen scheme (0..9) or -1.
function tth_post(px, py, sc) local(bw, bh, pw, ph, x0, y0, i, sx, sy, sw, sh, click, hotb, hov, chosen, fs, tw, th, ry, bx1, tx1, tx2, svx, svy, svw, svh, hxx, cxr, syy, warn, v, k, n) (
  tth_scrollbars();
  sc = max(0.5, min(2, sc));
  // OPTIONS stays reachable under zoom/scroll (independent of the front origin).
  tth_hbar || tth_vbar ? ( px = max(4, gfx_w - 80*sc - 14*tth_vbar); py = 4; );
  px = max(4,min(px,gfx_w - 74*sc)); py = max(4,min(py,gfx_h - 21*sc));
  chosen = -1;
  click = (tth_rcap & 1) && !(tth_pcap & 1);
  bw = 70*sc; bh = 17*sc;
  tth_bx = px; tth_by = py; tth_bw = bw; tth_bh = bh;
  hotb = tth_inbox(px, py, bw, bh);
  fs = max(9, floor(10*sc + 0.5));
  tth_fsCur != fs ? ( gfx_setfont(TTH_FONT, "Arial", fs); tth_fsCur = fs; ) : gfx_setfont(TTH_FONT);
  gfx_mode = 0;
  // box scale: always small enough for the box to fit the window completely
  // the drop shadow (4/5*scb right/bottom) is part of the drawn area and goes into the clamp.
  tth_scb = max(0.4, min(sc, min((gfx_w - 14)/353, (gfx_h - 10)/357)));
  pw = 348*tth_scb; ph = 352*tth_scb;
  // drawn area: x0 .. x0+pw+4*scb, y0 .. y0+ph+5*scb -> click/mask area = this area incl. shadow
  x0 = max(4, min(px, gfx_w - pw - 4*tth_scb - 4)); y0 = py + bh + 4*sc;
  y0 + ph + 5*tth_scb > gfx_h - 4 ? ( y0 = max(4, py - ph - 5*tth_scb - 4*sc); );
  y0 = min(y0, gfx_h - ph - 5*tth_scb - 4);
  y0 = max(0, y0);
  // evaluate click (button toggles; a click outside the DRAWN box incl. shadow closes - except while dragging in the picker)
  click ? (
    // a click outside the percent field confirms the entry, even if it closes the box.
    tth_edit && !tth_inbox(x0+252*tth_scb,y0+129*tth_scb,60*tth_scb,17*tth_scb) ? (
      v=tth_parsepercent(#tth_szinput); v>0 ? tth_size(v); tth_edit=0;
    );
    hotb ? ( tth_open = !tth_open; )
    : tth_open && !tth_inbox(x0, y0, pw + 4*tth_scb, ph + 5*tth_scb) && tth_cdrag == 0 ? ( tth_open = 0; );
  );
  // Button
  gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); gfx_rect(px, py, bw, bh, 1);
  (tth_open || hotb) ? gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.95) : gfx_set(tth_bdR, tth_bdG, tth_bdB, 1);
  gfx_rect(px, py, bw, bh, 0);
  gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 1); gfx_rect(px + 4*sc, py + 4*sc, 9*sc, bh - 8*sc, 1);
  gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, (hotb || tth_open) ? 1 : 0.8);
  gfx_measurestr("OPTIONS", tw, th);
  gfx_x = px + 18*sc; gfx_y = py + (bh - th)*0.5; gfx_drawstr("OPTIONS");
  tth_open ? (
    // on first open / scheme change the HSV field must match the real target colour.
    (!tth_oprev || tth_cscheme!=tth_cur) ? ( tth_tgtcol(); tth_rgb2hsv(tth_tr,tth_tg,tth_tb); );
    sc = tth_scb;               // from here on in box scale
    fs = max(9, floor(10*sc + 0.5));
    tth_fsCur != fs ? ( gfx_setfont(TTH_FONT, "Arial", fs); tth_fsCur = fs; );
    gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 0.45); gfx_rect(x0 + 4*sc, y0 + 5*sc, pw, ph, 1);
    gfx_set(tth_bgR*1.25, tth_bgG*1.25, tth_bgB*1.25, 1); gfx_rect(x0, y0, pw, ph, 1);
    gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); gfx_rect(x0 + 1, y0 + 1, pw - 2, 22*sc, 1);
    gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.9); gfx_rect(x0, y0, pw, ph, 0);
    gfx_set(0.92, 0.95, 0.92, 1); gfx_x = x0 + 12*sc; gfx_y = y0 + 6*sc; gfx_drawstr("OPTIONS");
    // --- tooltips on/off, right in the title bar. tth_tipoff = 1 disables ALL tooltips of the product
    // (the kit checks it in tt_tip; products with their own tooltip drawing check tth_tipoff themselves).
    // Deliberately an "off" flag: default 0 = tooltips on, even without initialisation and with old chunks.
    bx1 = x0 + pw - 100*sc;
    tth_sbtn(bx1, y0 + 3*sc, 92*sc, 16*sc, tth_tipoff ? "TOOLTIPS OFF" : "TOOLTIPS ON", tth_inbox(bx1, y0 + 3*sc, 92*sc, 16*sc), !tth_tipoff);
    (click && tth_cdrag == 0 && tth_inbox(bx1, y0 + 3*sc, 92*sc, 16*sc)) ? ( tth_tipoff = !tth_tipoff; );
    tth_hint(bx1,y0+3*sc,92*sc,16*sc,"Enable or disable all tooltips for this instance.");
    gfx_set(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, 1); gfx_x = x0 + 12*sc; gfx_y = y0 + 28*sc; gfx_drawstr("COLOR");
    // --- scheme fields
    hov = -1;
    sw = 36*sc; sh = 26*sc;
    i = 0;
    loop(10,
      sx = x0 + 12*sc + (i % 5)*(sw + 6*sc);
      sy = y0 + 42*sc + floor(i/5)*(sh + 7*sc);
      tth_inbox(sx, sy, sw, sh) ? ( hov = i; click && tth_cdrag == 0 ? ( chosen = i; ); );
      tth_swatch(i);
      tth_hint(sx,sy,sw,sh,"Choose the colour scheme for this instance.");
      gfx_set(tth_sgR, tth_sgG, tth_sgB, 1); gfx_rect(sx, sy, sw, sh, 1);
      gfx_set(tth_saR, tth_saG, tth_saB, 1); gfx_rect(sx + 2, sy + 2, sw - 4, (sh - 4)*0.62, 1);
      gfx_set(tth_slR, tth_slG, tth_slB, 1); gfx_rect(sx + 2, sy + 2 + (sh - 4)*0.68, sw - 4, (sh - 4)*0.32, 1);
      i == tth_cur ? ( gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 1); gfx_rect(sx - 1, sy - 1, sw + 2, sh + 2, 0); gfx_rect(sx, sy, sw, sh, 0); )
      : i == hov ? ( gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 0.6); gfx_rect(sx, sy, sw, sh, 0); );
      i += 1;
    );

    // --- UI SIZE: five steps plus a directly editable percent value.
    gfx_set(tth_pnR,tth_pnG,tth_pnB,1); gfx_rect(x0+12*sc,y0+108*sc,pw-24*sc,1,1);
    gfx_set(tth_dmR,tth_dmG,tth_dmB,1); gfx_x=x0+12*sc; gfx_y=y0+112*sc; gfx_drawstr("UI SIZE");
    i=0;
    loop(5,
      v=i==0 ? 100 : i==1 ? 125 : i==2 ? 150 : i==3 ? 200 : 300;
      sx=x0+12*sc+i*47*sc; sy=y0+129*sc;
      sprintf(#tth_szlabel,"%d%%",v);
      tth_sbtn(sx,sy,43*sc,17*sc,#tth_szlabel,tth_inbox(sx,sy,43*sc,17*sc),tth_uisize==v);
      click && tth_inbox(sx,sy,43*sc,17*sc) ? ( tth_size(v); tth_edit=0; );
      tth_hint(sx,sy,43*sc,17*sc,"Set UI zoom; scrollbars keep enlarged controls reachable.");
      i+=1;
    );
    sx=x0+252*sc; sy=y0+129*sc;
    !tth_edit ? sprintf(#tth_szinput,"%d",tth_uisize);
    tth_sbtn(sx,sy,60*sc,17*sc,#tth_szinput,tth_inbox(sx,sy,60*sc,17*sc),tth_edit);
    gfx_set(tth_ikR,tth_ikG,tth_ikB,1); gfx_x=sx+64*sc; gfx_y=sy+2*sc; gfx_drawstr("%");
    tth_hint(sx,sy,60*sc,17*sc,"Enter UI zoom from 50 to 400 percent; Enter applies, Escape cancels.");
    click && tth_inbox(sx,sy,60*sc,17*sc) ? ( tth_edit=1; tth_editfirst=1; );
    tth_edit ? (
      k=gfx_getchar(); n=0;
      while(k>0 && n<32) (
        tth_sizekey(k);
        k=gfx_getchar(); n+=1;
      );
      click && !tth_inbox(sx,sy,60*sc,17*sc) ? (
        v=tth_parsepercent(#tth_szinput); v>0 ? tth_size(v); tth_edit=0;
      );
    );

    // --- font sizes (step ~8 %, range -4..+8)
    gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); gfx_rect(x0 + 12*sc, y0 + 156*sc, pw - 24*sc, 1, 1);
    gfx_set(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, 1); gfx_x = x0 + 12*sc; gfx_y = y0 + 160*sc; gfx_drawstr("FONT SIZE");
    gfx_set(0.92, 0.95, 0.92, 1);
    gfx_x = x0 + 12*sc; gfx_y = y0 + 177*sc; gfx_drawstr("FONT 1 (TITLE)");
    gfx_x = x0 + 12*sc; gfx_y = y0 + 197*sc; gfx_drawstr("FONT 2 (TEXT)");
    ry = y0 + 172*sc;
    bx1 = x0 + pw - 112*sc;
    tth_sbtn(bx1, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc, "-", tth_inbox(bx1, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc), 0);
    (click && tth_inbox(bx1, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc)) ? ( tth_f1sz = max(-4, tth_f1sz - 1); );
    tth_hint(bx1,ry,20*sc,16*sc,"Decrease title font size; range -4 to +8 steps.");
    gfx_set(0.92, 0.95, 0.92, 1);
    sprintf(#tth_s, "%+d", tth_f1sz); gfx_measurestr(#tth_s, tw, th);
    gfx_x = bx1 + 20*sc + (48*sc - tw)*0.5; gfx_y = ry + (16*sc - th)*0.5; gfx_drawstr(#tth_s);
    tth_sbtn(bx1 + 68*sc, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc, "+", tth_inbox(bx1 + 68*sc, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc), 0);
    (click && tth_inbox(bx1 + 68*sc, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc)) ? ( tth_f1sz = min(8, tth_f1sz + 1); );
    tth_hint(bx1+68*sc,ry,20*sc,16*sc,"Increase title font size; range -4 to +8 steps.");
    ry = y0 + 192*sc;
    tth_sbtn(bx1, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc, "-", tth_inbox(bx1, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc), 0);
    (click && tth_inbox(bx1, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc)) ? ( tth_f2sz = max(-4, tth_f2sz - 1); );
    tth_hint(bx1,ry,20*sc,16*sc,"Decrease text font size; range -4 to +8 steps.");
    gfx_set(0.92, 0.95, 0.92, 1);
    sprintf(#tth_s, "%+d", tth_f2sz); gfx_measurestr(#tth_s, tw, th);
    gfx_x = bx1 + 20*sc + (48*sc - tw)*0.5; gfx_y = ry + (16*sc - th)*0.5; gfx_drawstr(#tth_s);
    tth_sbtn(bx1 + 68*sc, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc, "+", tth_inbox(bx1 + 68*sc, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc), 0);
    (click && tth_inbox(bx1 + 68*sc, ry, 20*sc, 16*sc)) ? ( tth_f2sz = min(8, tth_f2sz + 1); );
    tth_hint(bx1+68*sc,ry,20*sc,16*sc,"Increase text font size; range -4 to +8 steps.");
    // --- HSV colour picker (targets FONT 1 / FONT 2 / BG)
    gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); gfx_rect(x0 + 12*sc, y0 + 216*sc, pw - 24*sc, 1, 1);
    gfx_set(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, 1); gfx_x = x0 + 12*sc; gfx_y = y0 + 220*sc; gfx_drawstr("CUSTOM COLOR");
    ry = y0 + 234*sc;
    tx1 = x0 + 12*sc; tx2 = tx1 + 62*sc; cxr = tx2 + 62*sc;
    tth_sbtn(tx1, ry, 58*sc, 16*sc, "FONT 1", tth_inbox(tx1, ry, 58*sc, 16*sc), tth_ctgt == 0);
    (click && tth_inbox(tx1, ry, 58*sc, 16*sc)) ? ( tth_ctgt = 0; tth_tgtcol(); tth_rgb2hsv(tth_tr, tth_tg, tth_tb); );
    tth_sbtn(tx2, ry, 58*sc, 16*sc, "FONT 2", tth_inbox(tx2, ry, 58*sc, 16*sc), tth_ctgt == 1);
    (click && tth_inbox(tx2, ry, 58*sc, 16*sc)) ? ( tth_ctgt = 1; tth_tgtcol(); tth_rgb2hsv(tth_tr, tth_tg, tth_tb); );
    tth_sbtn(cxr, ry, 44*sc, 16*sc, "BG", tth_inbox(cxr, ry, 44*sc, 16*sc), tth_ctgt == 2);
    (click && tth_inbox(cxr, ry, 44*sc, 16*sc)) ? ( tth_ctgt = 2; tth_tgtcol(); tth_rgb2hsv(tth_tr, tth_tg, tth_tb); );
    tth_hint(tx1,ry,58*sc,16*sc,"Edit the custom title colour for this instance.");
    tth_hint(tx2,ry,58*sc,16*sc,"Edit the custom text colour for this instance.");
    tth_hint(cxr,ry,44*sc,16*sc,"Edit the custom background colour for this instance.");
    // preview box (active colour of the target)
    tth_tgtcol();
    gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 0.5); gfx_rect(x0 + pw - 58*sc, ry + 1, 46*sc, 16*sc, 1);
    gfx_set(tth_tr, tth_tg, tth_tb, 1); gfx_rect(x0 + pw - 58*sc, ry, 46*sc, 16*sc, 1);
    gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 0.35); gfx_rect(x0 + pw - 58*sc, ry, 46*sc, 16*sc, 0);
    // SV field (x = saturation, y = brightness) + hue bar (vertical)
    svx = x0 + 12*sc; svy = y0 + 258*sc; svw = 170*sc; svh = 74*sc;
    hxx = svx + svw + 8*sc;
    tth_hint(svx,svy,svw,svh,"Set saturation horizontally and brightness vertically, from 0 to 100 percent.");
    tth_hint(hxx,svy,16*sc,svh,"Set the hue of the selected custom colour.");
    (click && tth_inbox(svx, svy, svw, svh)) ? ( tth_cdrag = 1; );
    (click && tth_inbox(hxx, svy, 16*sc, svh)) ? ( tth_cdrag = 2; );
    (tth_cdrag > 0 && (tth_rcap & 1)) ? (
      tth_cdrag == 1 ? (
        tth_cs = min(1, max(0, (tth_rmx - svx)/svw));
        tth_cv = min(1, max(0, 1 - (tth_rmy - svy)/svh));
      ) : (
        tth_ch = min(1, max(0, (tth_rmy - svy)/svh));
      );
      tth_pick();
    );
    // draw SV field: 16 x 8 cells
    i = 0;
    loop(128,
      sx = svx + (i % 16)*svw/16; sy = svy + floor(i/16)*svh/8;
      tth_hsv(tth_ch, (i % 16 + 0.5)/16, 1 - (floor(i/16) + 0.5)/8);
      gfx_set(tth_hr, tth_hg, tth_hb, 1);
      gfx_rect(sx, sy, svw/16 + 1, svh/8 + 1, 1);
      i += 1;
    );
    gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 0.5); gfx_rect(svx, svy, svw, svh, 0);
    // crosshair on the SV field
    cxr = svx + tth_cs*svw; syy = svy + (1 - tth_cv)*svh;
    gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 0.8); gfx_rect(cxr - 1, syy - 4, 3, 8, 1); gfx_rect(cxr - 4, syy - 1, 8, 3, 1);
    gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 0.9); gfx_rect(cxr - 0.5, syy - 3, 1, 6, 1); gfx_rect(cxr - 3, syy - 0.5, 6, 1, 1);
    // hue bar: 24 stripes
    i = 0;
    loop(24,
      tth_hsv(i/24, 1, 1);
      gfx_set(tth_hr, tth_hg, tth_hb, 1);
      gfx_rect(hxx, svy + i*svh/24, 16*sc, svh/24 + 1, 1);
      i += 1;
    );
    gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 0.5); gfx_rect(hxx, svy, 16*sc, svh, 0);
    gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 0.9); gfx_rect(hxx - 1, svy + tth_ch*svh - 1, 16*sc + 2, 2, 1);
    // right column: RESET per target + RESET ALL + warning note
    cxr = hxx + 22*sc;
    tth_sbtn(cxr, svy, 84*sc, 15*sc, "RESET", tth_inbox(cxr, svy, 84*sc, 15*sc), 0);
    (click && tth_inbox(cxr, svy, 84*sc, 15*sc)) ? ( tth_reset_tgt(); tth_tgtcol(); tth_rgb2hsv(tth_tr,tth_tg,tth_tb); );
    tth_hint(cxr,svy,84*sc,15*sc,"Restore the selected title, text or background colour to its scheme default.");
    tth_sbtn(cxr, svy + 19*sc, 84*sc, 15*sc, "RESET ALL", tth_inbox(cxr, svy + 19*sc, 84*sc, 15*sc), 0);
    tth_hint(cxr,svy+19*sc,84*sc,15*sc,"Restore both font sizes and all custom colours to their scheme defaults.");
    (click && tth_inbox(cxr, svy + 19*sc, 84*sc, 15*sc)) ? (
      tth_f1on = 0; tth_f2on = 0; tth_bgon = 0; tth_f1sz = 0; tth_f2sz = 0; tth_apply(tth_cur);
      tth_tgtcol(); tth_rgb2hsv(tth_tr,tth_tg,tth_tb);
    );
    warn = 0;
    (tth_f1on && tth_cr(tth_f1R, tth_f1G, tth_f1B, tth_bgR, tth_bgG, tth_bgB) < 3) ? ( warn = 1; );
    (tth_f2on && tth_cr(tth_f2R, tth_f2G, tth_f2B, tth_bgR, tth_bgG, tth_bgB) < 3) ? ( warn = 1; );
    warn ? (
      gfx_set(tth_alR, tth_alG, tth_alB, 1);
      gfx_x = cxr; gfx_y = svy + 42*sc; gfx_drawstr("low contrast");
      gfx_x = cxr; gfx_y = svy + 53*sc; gfx_drawstr("vs background");
    );
    // footer: scheme name (secondary colour) + "per instance" (dimmed)
    hov < 0 ? ( hov = tth_cur; );
    gfx_set(tth_alR, tth_alG, tth_alB, 1); gfx_x = x0 + 12*sc; gfx_y = y0 + ph - 16*sc;
    gfx_drawstr(tth_name(hov));
    gfx_set(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, 1); gfx_measurestr("per instance", tw, th);
    gfx_x = x0 + pw - tw - 12*sc; gfx_y = y0 + ph - 16*sc; gfx_drawstr("per instance");
    chosen >= 0 ? ( tth_apply(chosen); tth_tgtcol(); tth_rgb2hsv(tth_tr,tth_tg,tth_tb); );
  );
  !(tth_rcap & 1) ? ( tth_cdrag = 0; );
  // style changed in the box (TOOLTIPS, font sizes, custom colours) -> undo point. Only with the box open AND
  // mouse button (now or in the previous frame): a project load/undo changes the values without a click and must not set a new point.
  !tth_open ? tth_edit = 0;
  tth_oprev=tth_open; tth_cscheme=tth_cur;
  tth_stsum = 149*tth_uisize + 151*tth_ctgt + tth_tipoff + 3*tth_f1sz + 7*tth_f2sz + 11*tth_f1on + 13*tth_f2on + 17*tth_bgon
    + 101*tth_f1R + 103*tth_f1G + 107*tth_f1B + 109*tth_f2R + 113*tth_f2G + 127*tth_f2B + 131*tth_bgUR + 137*tth_bgUG + 139*tth_bgUB;
  tth_stsum != tth_stprev ? (
    (tth_stini && tth_open && ((tth_rcap0 | tth_pcap) & 1)) ? tt_undo();
    tth_stprev = tth_stsum; tth_stini = 1;
  );
  tth_pcap = tth_rcap0;      // raw button (tth_rcap is zeroed while the preset overlay is open)
  (tt_undoreq && (tth_rcap0 & 1) == 0) ? ( tt_undoreq = 0; sliderchange(-1); );      // undo point for state without a slider
  chosen;
);
// ==========================  End TT-Theme  ============================
// __THEME_END__
// __PRESETS_BEGIN__   // generated from _shared/tt-presets.jsfx-inc
// ==========================  TT-Presets (TTPB_VER 3)  ==================
// Uniform preset bar (factory presets + user bank with 32 slots) for all TT plugins.
// The bar sits in the header immediately LEFT of the OPTIONS button of the theme module:
//   [<] [ preset name  v ] [>] [SAVE] [...]
// Requirement: the theme module (tt-theme.jsfx-inc) comes before it (globals accR/G/B, tth_*, tth_pre/tth_post).
// The module needs NO UI kit (only raw gfx_* calls), font slot 11 (theme uses 10, products 1..5 and 9).
// JSFX cannot write files: the user bank lives in the plugin state (@serialize = project, FX chain,
// track template AND every native REAPER preset file of the plugin).
// Division of labour without callbacks: the module provides storage, names, surface, serialisation and action codes;
// the plugin reads out its state / applies it (it knows sliders, memory blocks and resync paths).
// Integration (code template: _shared/PRESETS.md):
//   @init      : tt_pb_init(nFactory, 32, memBase, wordsPerSlot);  tt_pb_fname(i, "Name"); ...   // AFTER the module definitions
//   @gfx       : tth_pre();  tt_pb_pre();  ...  uikit_begin ... front ...
//                a = tt_pb_post(px, py, sc);   // before tth_post; px/py = top left corner of the bar (window pixels), width tt_pb_w(sc)
//                action a: 0 nothing | 1 LOAD_FACTORY (index tt_pb_arg) | 2 LOAD_USER (slot tt_pb_arg) | 3 SAVE (slot tt_pb_arg) | 4 INIT
//                tt_pb_track(checksum);        // after applying, every frame: sets tt_pb_mod (star "*")
//   @serialize : ...own data...;  tt_pb_serialize();   // LAST, reading and writing
// Globals (prefix tt_pb_ / TTPB_): tt_pb_buf = scratch buffer (wordsPerSlot words), tt_pb_arg, tt_pb_cur/tt_pb_curKind
// (0 none, 1 factory, 2 user; serialized), tt_pb_mod, tt_pb_open (overlay open), tt_pb_hasinit.
// Memory needed from memBase: nUser + (nFactory+nUser)*25 + (nUser+1)*wordsPerSlot + 25 words (tt_pb_end = first free address).
TTPB_VER   = 3;
TTPB_MAGIC = 21584;    // 0x5450, chosen small: float32-exact, comparison tolerant
TTPB_MAG2  = 22032;    // "TTS" style block: marker + version + 14 values (see tt_pb_serialize)
TTPB_FONT  = 11;       // font slot
TTPB_NW    = 25;       // words per name field (24 chars + null)
TTPB_NMAX  = 24;       // chars per name
TTPB_ROWS  = 14;       // visible rows in the dropdown
// State variables deliberately NOT initialised at top level (a repeated @init - e.g. on transport
// start - must not close an open overlay); presetting only the first time in tt_pb_init.
// Allocate memory. Clear only the first time: a repeated @init (samplerate, transport start) keeps bank and selection.
function tt_pb_init(nf, nu, base, wps) (
  tt_pb_nfac = nf; tt_pb_nusr = max(1, min(64, nu)); tt_pb_wps = wps; tt_pb_hf = nf > 0 ? 1 : 0;
  tt_pb_used  = base;                                     // nUser words: 1 = slot used
  tt_pb_names = tt_pb_used + tt_pb_nusr;                  // (nFactory + nUser) * 25 words, chars as words
  tt_pb_data  = tt_pb_names + (nf + tt_pb_nusr)*TTPB_NW;  // nUser * wps words
  tt_pb_buf   = tt_pb_data + tt_pb_nusr*wps;              // wps words: scratch buffer plugin <-> slot
  tt_pb_ebuf  = tt_pb_buf + wps;                          // 25 words: name edit buffer (= "pending" name for commit)
  tt_pb_end   = tt_pb_ebuf + TTPB_NW;
  tt_pb_ready != 1 ? (
    memset(base, 0, tt_pb_end - base);
    tt_pb_cur = -1; tt_pb_curKind = 0; tt_pb_elen = 0; tt_pb_ready = 1;
    tt_pb_hasinit = 1; tt_pb_open = 0; tt_pb_hold = 0; tt_pb_pcap = 0; tt_pb_rmx = -10000; tt_pb_rmy = -10000; tt_pb_rcap = 0; tt_pb_rwh = 0; tt_pb_act = 1;
    tt_pb_bx = 0; tt_pb_by = 0; tt_pb_bw = 0; tt_pb_bh = 0; tt_pb_scr = 0; tt_pb_sbd = 0; tt_pb_frm = 0; tt_pb_msgt = 0; tt_pb_conf = 0;
    tt_pb_emode = 1; tt_pb_eslot = 0; tt_pb_mod = 0; tt_pb_reset = 1; tt_pb_chkok = 0; tt_pb_chk = 0; tt_pb_fsCur = 0;
  );
);

// write name k (0..nFactory-1 factory, then user) from a string index into the word representation
function tt_pb_setname(k, s) local(a, i, n) (
  a = tt_pb_names + k*TTPB_NW;
  n = min(strlen(s), TTPB_NMAX);
  memset(a, 0, TTPB_NW);
  i = 0;
  loop(n, a[i] = str_getchar(s, i); i += 1; );
);

function tt_pb_fname(i, s) ( i >= 0 && i < tt_pb_nfac ? tt_pb_setname(i, s); );

// word representation (chars as words, null-terminated) from address a -> #tt_pb_s
function tt_pb_wstr(a) local(i, c) (
  strcpy(#tt_pb_s, "");
  i = 0; c = a[0];
  while (c > 0 && i < TTPB_NMAX) (
    sprintf(#tt_pb_t, "%c", c); strcat(#tt_pb_s, #tt_pb_t);
    i += 1; c = a[i];
  );
);

// name k (0..nFactory-1 factory, then user) -> #tt_pb_s
function tt_pb_getname(k) ( tt_pb_wstr(tt_pb_names + k*TTPB_NW); );

// number of used user slots / first free slot (-1 = none)
function tt_pb_count() local(j, n) ( n = 0; j = 0; loop(tt_pb_nusr, tt_pb_used[j] > 0 ? n += 1; j += 1; ); n; );
function tt_pb_free() local(j, r) ( r = -1; j = 0; loop(tt_pb_nusr, (r < 0 && tt_pb_used[j] <= 0) ? r = j; j += 1; ); r; );

// round to 24 significant bits = float32-exact (serialisation writes float32)
function tt_pb_q(v) local(e, st) (
  (v == 0 || abs(v) > 1000000000000000000000000000) ? v : (
    e = floor(log(abs(v))/log(2));
    st = 2^(e - 23);
    floor(v/st + 0.5)*st;
  );
);

// set pending name (tt_pb_ebuf) from a string
function tt_pb_setpend(s) local(i, n) (
  n = min(strlen(s), TTPB_NMAX);
  memset(tt_pb_ebuf, 0, TTPB_NW);
  i = 0;
  loop(n, tt_pb_ebuf[i] = str_getchar(s, i); i += 1; );
  tt_pb_elen = n;
);

// fetch a slot/factory preset name into the edit buffer
function tt_pb_loadpend(k) local(a) (
  a = tt_pb_names + k*TTPB_NW;
  memcpy(tt_pb_ebuf, a, TTPB_NW);
  tt_pb_elen = 0;
  while (tt_pb_ebuf[tt_pb_elen] > 0 && tt_pb_elen < TTPB_NMAX) ( tt_pb_elen += 1; );
);

// slot -> buffer; returns word count (0 = empty)
function tt_pb_fetch(slot) local(n) (
  memset(tt_pb_buf, 0, tt_pb_wps);
  n = 0;
  (slot >= 0 && slot < tt_pb_nusr && tt_pb_used[slot] > 0) ? (
    memcpy(tt_pb_buf, tt_pb_data + slot*tt_pb_wps, tt_pb_wps);
    n = tt_pb_wps;
  );
  n;
);

// buffer (filled by the plugin, n words, the rest is padded with 0) -> slot; name = pending name (tt_pb_ebuf)
function tt_pb_commit(slot, n) local(a, i) (
  (slot >= 0 && slot < tt_pb_nusr) ? (
    n = max(0, min(n, tt_pb_wps));
    a = tt_pb_data + slot*tt_pb_wps;
    memset(a, 0, tt_pb_wps);
    i = 0;
    loop(n, a[i] = tt_pb_q(tt_pb_buf[i]); i += 1; );
    memcpy(tt_pb_names + (tt_pb_nfac + slot)*TTPB_NW, tt_pb_ebuf, TTPB_NW);
    tt_pb_used[slot] = 1; tt_undo();      // SAVE -> undo point (the product need not report anything more)
    tt_pb_cur = slot; tt_pb_curKind = 2; tt_pb_reset = 1;
  );
);

// default name "User NN" for a slot -> pending name
function tt_pb_defname(slot) (
  sprintf(#tt_pb_s, "User %02d", slot + 1);
  tt_pb_setpend(#tt_pb_s);
);

// "same state" detection: the plugin calls this every frame with a checksum of its state (after applying).
// After load/save/init (tt_pb_reset) and after reading from the project (tt_pb_chkok = 0) the reference is taken anew.
function tt_pb_track(s) (
  (tt_pb_chkok == 0 || tt_pb_reset) ? ( tt_pb_chk = s; tt_pb_chkok = 1; tt_pb_reset = 0; );
  tt_pb_mod = (tt_pb_curKind > 0 && s != tt_pb_chk) ? 1 : 0;
);

// selection (kind 1 factory / 2 user, index i) -> action code
function tt_pb_select(kind, i) (
  tt_pb_curKind = kind; tt_pb_cur = i; tt_pb_arg = i; tt_pb_reset = 1;
  kind;
);

// neighbour in direction dir (+1/-1): factory presets, then used user slots, wrapping; returns action code (0 = none)
function tt_pb_step(dir) local(p, tot, tries, found, r) (
  tot = tt_pb_nfac + tt_pb_nusr;
  p = tt_pb_curKind == 1 ? tt_pb_cur : tt_pb_curKind == 2 ? tt_pb_nfac + tt_pb_cur : (dir > 0 ? -1 : tot);
  found = 0; tries = 0; r = 0;
  while (!found && tries < tot) (
    p += dir;
    p = (p + tot) % tot;
    found = (p < tt_pb_nfac) || (tt_pb_used[max(0, p - tt_pb_nfac)] > 0);
    tries += 1;
  );
  found ? ( r = p < tt_pb_nfac ? tt_pb_select(1, p) : tt_pb_select(2, p - tt_pb_nfac); );
  r;
);

function tt_pb_in(x, y, w, h) ( tt_pb_rmx >= x && tt_pb_rmx < x + w && tt_pb_rmy >= y && tt_pb_rmy < y + h; );

// width of the bar in design units: tt_pb_wu (default 250; small windows set e.g. tt_pb_wu = 190 in @init)
tt_pb_wu == 0 ? ( tt_pb_wu = 250; );
function tt_pb_w(sc) ( tt_pb_wu*max(0.5, sc); );

// set font (slot 11, Arial), recreate only on a size change
function tt_pb_font(sz) (
  tt_pb_fsCur != sz ? ( gfx_setfont(TTPB_FONT, "Arial", sz); tt_pb_fsCur = sz; ) : gfx_setfont(TTPB_FONT);
);

// text (#tt_pb_s) into a rectangle: align 0 = centred, otherwise left-aligned
function tt_pb_txt(x, y, w, h, align) local(tw, th) (
  gfx_measurestr(#tt_pb_s, tw, th);
  gfx_x = align ? x : x + (w - tw)*0.5;
  gfx_y = y + (h - th)*0.5;
  tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(#tt_pb_s);
);

// shorten #tt_pb_s to width w (".." at the end)
function tt_pb_fit(w) local(tw, th, n, n0) (
  gfx_measurestr(#tt_pb_s, tw, th);
  n0 = strlen(#tt_pb_s); n = n0;
  while (tw > w && n > 2) (
    n -= 1;
    strcpy_substr(#tt_pb_s2, #tt_pb_s, 0, n); strcat(#tt_pb_s2, "..");
    gfx_measurestr(#tt_pb_s2, tw, th);
  );
  n < n0 ? strcpy(#tt_pb_s, #tt_pb_s2);
);

// button face: panel + border; then sets the text colour
function tt_pb_btn(x, y, w, h, hot, on) (
  gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); gfx_rect(x, y, w, h, 1);
  (hot || on) ? gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.95) : gfx_set(tth_bdR, tth_bdG, tth_bdB, 1);
  gfx_rect(x, y, w, h, 0);
  gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, (hot || on) ? 1 : 0.8);
);

// overlay face (shadow, area, border)
function tt_pb_ovl(x, y, w, h, sc) (
  gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 0.45); gfx_rect(x + 4*sc, y + 5*sc, w, h, 1);
  gfx_set(tth_bgR*1.25, tth_bgG*1.25, tth_bgB*1.25, 1); gfx_rect(x, y, w, h, 1);
  gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.9); gfx_rect(x, y, w, h, 0);
);

// row r of the dropdown -> tt_pb_rk (0 header, 1 factory, 2 user), tt_pb_ri (index; header 0 = FACTORY, 1 = USER)
function tt_pb_rowinfo(r) (
  r < tt_pb_hf ? ( tt_pb_rk = 0; tt_pb_ri = 0; )
  : r < tt_pb_hf + tt_pb_nfac ? ( tt_pb_rk = 1; tt_pb_ri = r - tt_pb_hf; )
  : r == tt_pb_hf + tt_pb_nfac ? ( tt_pb_rk = 0; tt_pb_ri = 1; )
  : ( tt_pb_rk = 2; tt_pb_ri = r - tt_pb_hf - tt_pb_nfac - 1; );
);

// dropdown (overlay). Draws and evaluates; returns action code. x/y = bottom left corner of the bar, w = width.
function tt_pb_dropdown(x, y, w, sc, click) local(rh, nr, vis, room, h, x0, y0, r, rr, hov, sbw, sbx, th0, thh, a, ry, lw, cr, hot) (
  a = 0;
  rh = 16*sc; nr = tt_pb_hf + tt_pb_nfac + 1 + tt_pb_nusr;
  room = gfx_h - (y + 2*sc) - 6;
  vis = max(3, min(TTPB_ROWS, min(nr, floor((room - 4*sc)/rh))));
  h = vis*rh + 4*sc;
  x0 = max(4, min(x, gfx_w - w - 4)); y0 = y + 2*sc;
  sbw = 7*sc; sbx = x0 + w - sbw - 2*sc; lw = w - sbw - 4*sc;
  tt_pb_scr = max(0, min(nr - vis, tt_pb_scr));
  hot = tt_pb_in(x0, y0, w, h);
  (hot && tt_pb_rwh != 0) ? ( tt_pb_scr = max(0, min(nr - vis, tt_pb_scr - (tt_pb_rwh > 0 ? 3 : -3))); );
  // row under the pointer
  hov = -1;
  ry = y0 + 2*sc;
  (hot && tt_pb_rmx < sbx - 2*sc && tt_pb_rmy >= ry) ? (
    r = floor((tt_pb_rmy - ry)/rh);
    r < vis ? ( hov = tt_pb_scr + r; );
  );
  // drag scrollbar
  (tt_pb_sbd && (tt_pb_rcap & 1)) ? (
    tt_pb_scr = max(0, min(nr - vis, floor((tt_pb_rmy - y0)/h*(nr - vis + 1))));
  ) : ( tt_pb_sbd = 0; );
  click ? (
    hot ? (
      hov >= 0 ? (
        tt_pb_rowinfo(hov);
        (tt_pb_rk == 1) ? ( a = tt_pb_select(1, tt_pb_ri); tt_pb_open = 0; )
        : (tt_pb_rk == 2 && tt_pb_used[tt_pb_ri] > 0) ? ( a = tt_pb_select(2, tt_pb_ri); tt_pb_open = 0; );
      ) : ( tt_pb_rmx >= sbx - 2*sc && nr > vis ? ( tt_pb_sbd = 1; tt_pb_scr = max(0, min(nr - vis, floor((tt_pb_rmy - y0)/h*(nr - vis + 1)))); ); );
    ) : ( tt_pb_open = 0; );
  );
  tt_pb_open == 1 ? (
    tt_pb_ovl(x0, y0, w, h, sc);
    cr = tt_pb_curKind == 1 ? tt_pb_hf + tt_pb_cur : tt_pb_curKind == 2 ? tt_pb_hf + tt_pb_nfac + 1 + tt_pb_cur : -1;
    r = 0;
    loop(vis,
      rr = tt_pb_scr + r;
      tt_pb_rowinfo(rr);
      ry = y0 + 2*sc + r*rh;
      tt_pb_rk == 0 ? (
        gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); gfx_rect(x0 + 1, ry, w - 2, rh, 1);
        gfx_set(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, 1);
        strcpy(#tt_pb_s, tt_pb_ri == 0 ? "FACTORY" : "USER");
        tt_pb_txt(x0 + 8*sc, ry, lw, rh, 1);
      ) : (
        tt_pb_rk == 1 ? ( tt_pb_getname(tt_pb_ri); sprintf(#tt_pb_s2, "%s", #tt_pb_s); )
        : ( tt_pb_getname(tt_pb_nfac + tt_pb_ri); sprintf(#tt_pb_s2, "%02d  %s", tt_pb_ri + 1, #tt_pb_s); );
        strcpy(#tt_pb_s, #tt_pb_s2);
        (tt_pb_rk == 2 && tt_pb_used[tt_pb_ri] <= 0) ? ( sprintf(#tt_pb_s, "%02d  - empty -", tt_pb_ri + 1); );
        tt_pb_fit(lw - 14*sc);
        rr == hov ? ( gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.20); gfx_rect(x0 + 1, ry, w - 2, rh, 1); );
        rr == cr ? (
          gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.16); gfx_rect(x0 + 1, ry, w - 2, rh, 1);
          gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 1); gfx_rect(x0 + 1, ry, 3*sc, rh, 1);
        );
        (tt_pb_rk == 2 && tt_pb_used[tt_pb_ri] <= 0) ? gfx_set(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, 1)
        : rr == cr ? gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 1) : gfx_set(0.92, 0.95, 0.92, 1);
        tt_pb_txt(x0 + 12*sc, ry, lw, rh, 1);
      );
      r += 1;
    );
    // scrollbar
    nr > vis ? (
      gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); gfx_rect(sbx, y0 + 2*sc, sbw, h - 4*sc, 1);
      thh = max(10*sc, (h - 4*sc)*vis/nr);
      th0 = y0 + 2*sc + ((h - 4*sc) - thh)*tt_pb_scr/max(1, nr - vis);
      gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.7); gfx_rect(sbx, th0, sbw, thh, 1);
    );
  );
  a;
);

// menu "..." (overlay). x = right edge of the bar, y = bottom edge. Returns action code (only INIT = 4).
function tt_pb_menu(x, y, sc, click) local(rh, w, h, x0, y0, n, i, hov, a, en, item, ry, ok) (
  a = 0;
  rh = 17*sc; w = 116*sc; n = tt_pb_hasinit ? 4 : 3; h = n*rh + 4*sc;
  x0 = max(4, min(x - w, gfx_w - w - 4)); y0 = y + 2*sc;
  hov = -1;
  tt_pb_in(x0, y0, w, h) ? ( hov = floor((tt_pb_rmy - y0 - 2*sc)/rh); hov < 0 || hov >= n ? hov = -1; );
  ok = tt_pb_curKind == 2;   // RENAME / COPY / DELETE for user presets only
  click ? (
    hov >= 0 ? (
      hov == 0 && ok ? (           // RENAME
        tt_pb_emode = 2; tt_pb_eslot = tt_pb_cur; tt_pb_loadpend(tt_pb_nfac + tt_pb_cur); tt_pb_open = 3; tt_pb_conf = 0;
      ) : hov == 1 && ok ? (       // COPY into the next free slot
        i = tt_pb_free();
        i < 0 ? ( tt_pb_msgt = 90; strcpy(#tt_pb_msg, "BANK FULL"); ) : (
          memcpy(tt_pb_data + i*tt_pb_wps, tt_pb_data + tt_pb_cur*tt_pb_wps, tt_pb_wps);
          tt_pb_getname(tt_pb_nfac + tt_pb_cur);
          sprintf(#tt_pb_s2, "Copy of %s", #tt_pb_s); tt_pb_setpend(#tt_pb_s2);
          memcpy(tt_pb_names + (tt_pb_nfac + i)*TTPB_NW, tt_pb_ebuf, TTPB_NW);
          tt_pb_used[i] = 1; tt_undo();      // bank changed -> undo point
          tt_pb_msgt = 90; sprintf(#tt_pb_msg, "COPIED TO %02d", i + 1);
        );
        tt_pb_open = 0; tt_pb_conf = 0;
      ) : hov == 2 && ok ? (       // DELETE (second click confirms)
        tt_pb_conf ? (
          tt_pb_used[tt_pb_cur] = 0; memset(tt_pb_names + (tt_pb_nfac + tt_pb_cur)*TTPB_NW, 0, TTPB_NW);
          memset(tt_pb_data + tt_pb_cur*tt_pb_wps, 0, tt_pb_wps); tt_undo();
          tt_pb_curKind = 0; tt_pb_cur = -1; tt_pb_reset = 1;
          tt_pb_open = 0; tt_pb_conf = 0;
        ) : ( tt_pb_conf = 1; );
      ) : (hov == 3 && tt_pb_hasinit) ? (   // INIT
        a = 4; tt_pb_curKind = 0; tt_pb_cur = -1; tt_pb_reset = 1; tt_pb_open = 0; tt_pb_conf = 0;
      );
    ) : ( !tt_pb_in(x0, y0, w, h) ? ( tt_pb_open = 0; tt_pb_conf = 0; ); );
  );
  tt_pb_open == 2 ? (
    tt_pb_ovl(x0, y0, w, h, sc);
    i = 0;
    loop(n,
      ry = y0 + 2*sc + i*rh;
      item = (i == 0 || i == 1 || i == 2) ? ok : 1;
      i == hov && item ? ( gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.20); gfx_rect(x0 + 1, ry, w - 2, rh, 1); );
      item ? gfx_set(0.92, 0.95, 0.92, 1) : gfx_set(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, 1);
      i == 2 && tt_pb_conf ? gfx_set(tth_alR, tth_alG, tth_alB, 1);
      strcpy(#tt_pb_s, i == 0 ? "RENAME" : i == 1 ? "COPY" : i == 2 ? (tt_pb_conf ? "CONFIRM DELETE?" : "DELETE") : "INIT");
      tt_pb_txt(x0 + 10*sc, ry, w, rh, 1);
      i += 1;
    );
  );
  a;
);

// process one key in the name field (flags tt_pb_kdone / tt_pb_kcanc)
function tt_pb_key(c) (
  tt_pb_lk = c; tt_pb_nk += 1;                  // diagnostics: last key / count (Q command 19 in the plugin)
  c == 13 || c == 10 ? ( tt_pb_kdone = 1; )
  : c == 27 ? ( tt_pb_kcanc = 1; )
  : c == 8 ? ( tt_pb_elen > 0 ? ( tt_pb_elen -= 1; tt_pb_ebuf[tt_pb_elen] = 0; ); )
  : (c >= 32 && c < 127 && tt_pb_elen < TTPB_NMAX) ? ( tt_pb_ebuf[tt_pb_elen] = c; tt_pb_elen += 1; tt_pb_ebuf[tt_pb_elen] = 0; );
);

// name entry (overlay). Keyboard via gfx_getchar. REAPER intercepts Space (transport) and - depending on settings - Esc (close window)
// itself: blank via Shift+Space, cancel via the CANCEL button or a click beside it. Returns 3 (SAVE confirmed; slot in tt_pb_arg, name in tt_pb_ebuf).
function tt_pb_entry(x, y, sc, click) local(w, h, x0, y0, c, n, done, canc, bw, bh, okx, cx, tw, th, a, i, hokk, hcan, fy) (
  a = 0; done = 0; canc = 0;
  w = 250*sc; h = 90*sc; bh = 17*sc; bw = 56*sc;
  x0 = max(4, min(x, gfx_w - w - 4)); y0 = y + 2*sc;
  // keyboard
  tt_pb_kdone = 0; tt_pb_kcanc = 0;
  c = gfx_getchar(); n = 0;
  while (c > 0 && n < 40) (
    tt_pb_key(c);
    c = gfx_getchar(); n += 1;
  );
  done = tt_pb_kdone; canc = tt_pb_kcanc;
  okx = x0 + w - 2*bw - 12*sc; fy = y0 + 67*sc;
  hokk = tt_pb_in(okx, fy, bw, bh); hcan = tt_pb_in(okx + bw + 4*sc, fy, bw, bh);
  click ? (
    hokk ? ( done = 1; ) : hcan ? ( canc = 1; ) : !tt_pb_in(x0, y0, w, h) ? ( canc = 1; );
  );
  done ? (
    tt_pb_elen < 1 ? ( sprintf(#tt_pb_s, "User %02d", tt_pb_eslot + 1); tt_pb_setpend(#tt_pb_s); );
    tt_pb_emode == 2 ? (
      memcpy(tt_pb_names + (tt_pb_nfac + tt_pb_eslot)*TTPB_NW, tt_pb_ebuf, TTPB_NW); tt_undo();
    ) : ( a = 3; tt_pb_arg = tt_pb_eslot; tt_pb_reset = 1; );
    tt_pb_open = 0;
  );
  canc ? ( tt_pb_open = 0; );
  tt_pb_open == 3 ? (
    tt_pb_ovl(x0, y0, w, h, sc);
    gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); gfx_rect(x0 + 1, y0 + 1, w - 2, 20*sc, 1);
    gfx_set(0.92, 0.95, 0.92, 1);
    sprintf(#tt_pb_s, tt_pb_emode == 2 ? "RENAME PRESET  (slot %02d)" : "SAVE PRESET  (slot %02d)", tt_pb_eslot + 1);
    tt_pb_txt(x0 + 10*sc, y0 + 1, w, 20*sc, 1);
    // text field
    gfx_set(tth_bgR, tth_bgG, tth_bgB, 1); gfx_rect(x0 + 8*sc, y0 + 26*sc, w - 16*sc, 17*sc, 1);
    gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 0.8); gfx_rect(x0 + 8*sc, y0 + 26*sc, w - 16*sc, 17*sc, 0);
    tt_pb_wstr(tt_pb_ebuf);
    gfx_set(1, 1, 1, 1);
    tt_pb_txt(x0 + 12*sc, y0 + 26*sc, w, 17*sc, 1);
    gfx_measurestr(#tt_pb_s, tw, th);
    (floor(tt_pb_frm/15) & 1) == 0 ? ( gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, 1); gfx_rect(x0 + 12*sc + tw + 1, y0 + 29*sc, max(1, sc), 11*sc, 1); );
    // buttons + hint
    gfx_set(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, 1); strcpy(#tt_pb_s, "Enter = OK    Shift+Space = blank");
    tt_pb_txt(x0 + 10*sc, y0 + 46*sc, w, 16*sc, 1);
    tt_pb_btn(okx, fy, bw, bh, hokk, 0); strcpy(#tt_pb_s, "OK"); tt_pb_txt(okx, fy, bw, bh, 0);
    tt_pb_btn(okx + bw + 4*sc, fy, bw, bh, hcan, 0); strcpy(#tt_pb_s, "CANCEL"); tt_pb_txt(okx + bw + 4*sc, fy, bw, bh, 0);
  );
  a;
);

// end of the run of same kind (zeros / non-zeros) from i
function tt_pb_run(a, i, n) local(z, j) (
  z = a[i] == 0; j = i;
  while (j < n && (a[j] == 0) == z) ( j += 1; );
  j;
);

// read: one slot record (RLE) into the buffer, then transfer to slot j. Returns 1 = ok.
function tt_pb_rdone(j, sw) local(u, i, i0, k, ok) (
  u = 0; file_var(0, u);
  ok = 1;
  u > 0 ? (
    file_mem(0, tt_pb_ebuf, TTPB_NW);
    memset(tt_pb_buf, 0, tt_pb_wps);
    i = 0;
    while (ok && i < sw) (
      k = 0; file_var(0, k);
      ok = (k < 0 && i - k <= sw) || (k > 0 && i + k <= sw);
      i0 = i; i += ok ? abs(k) : 0;
      (ok && k > 0) ? file_mem(0, tt_pb_buf + i0, k);
    );
    ok ? (
      memcpy(tt_pb_data + j*tt_pb_wps, tt_pb_buf, tt_pb_wps);
      memcpy(tt_pb_names + (tt_pb_nfac + j)*TTPB_NW, tt_pb_ebuf, TTPB_NW);
      tt_pb_used[j] = 1;
    );
  ) : (
    tt_pb_used[j] = 0;
    memset(tt_pb_names + (tt_pb_nfac + j)*TTPB_NW, 0, TTPB_NW);
    memset(tt_pb_data + j*tt_pb_wps, 0, tt_pb_wps);
  );
  ok;
);

// write: one used slot j (name + RLE data)
function tt_pb_wrone(j) local(u, a, i, i0, jj, k, z) (
  u = tt_pb_used[j] > 0 ? 1 : 0;
  file_var(0, u);
  u > 0 ? (
    file_mem(0, tt_pb_names + (tt_pb_nfac + j)*TTPB_NW, TTPB_NW);
    a = tt_pb_data + j*tt_pb_wps;
    i = 0;
    while (i < tt_pb_wps) (
      z = a[i] == 0;
      jj = tt_pb_run(a, i, tt_pb_wps);
      k = z ? i - jj : jj - i;
      file_var(0, k);
      i0 = i; i = jj;
      z == 0 ? file_mem(0, a + i0, k);
    );
  );
);

// serialisation (call at the END of the plugin's @serialize; reading and writing)
// format: MAGIC, VER, nUser, wps, cur, curKind, then per slot: used [, name (25 words), RLE-packed data].
// RLE per slot: word k < 0 = |k| zeros; k > 0 = k literal words follow.
// Read: if the block is missing (old project) or magic/version/nUser/wps mismatch, the bank stays unchanged.
// Behind it the style block TTPB_MAG2, style version, 14 values (tth_f1sz/f2sz, f1on+f1RGB,
// f2on+f2RGB, bgon+bgURGB). Backward compatible: old chunks end before the block (file_avail = 0
// -> nothing read), old module versions read new chunks up to the bank end and leave the rest.
// The style values are NOT preset bar data: they apply per instance, not per preset.
function tt_pb_serialize() local(rd, m, ver, nu, sw, cu, ck, j, ok, m2, v2) (
  rd = file_avail(0) >= 0;
  rd ? (
    file_avail(0) > 0 ? (
      m = 0; file_var(0, m);
      abs(m - TTPB_MAGIC) < 256 ? (
        ver = 0; nu = 0; sw = 0; cu = 0; ck = 0;
        file_var(0, ver); file_var(0, nu); file_var(0, sw); file_var(0, cu); file_var(0, ck);
        (ver == 1 && nu >= 1 && nu <= tt_pb_nusr && sw >= 1 && sw <= tt_pb_wps) ? (   // old chunk with fewer user slots stays loadable (rest = empty)
          // explicitly clear slots the chunk does not carry (nu < tt_pb_nusr) - otherwise the
          // presets of the previous instance would remain in the trailing slots.
          ok = 1; j = nu;
          loop(max(0, tt_pb_nusr - nu),
            tt_pb_used[j] = 0;
            memset(tt_pb_names + (tt_pb_nfac + j)*TTPB_NW, 0, TTPB_NW);
            memset(tt_pb_data + j*tt_pb_wps, 0, tt_pb_wps);
            j += 1;
          );
          j = 0;
          while (ok && j < nu) (
            ok = tt_pb_rdone(j, sw);
            j += 1;
          );
          ok ? (
            tt_pb_curKind = (ck == 1 || ck == 2) ? floor(ck) : 0;
            tt_pb_cur = tt_pb_curKind == 1 ? (cu >= 0 && cu < tt_pb_nfac ? floor(cu) : -1)
                      : tt_pb_curKind == 2 ? (cu >= 0 && cu < tt_pb_nusr && tt_pb_used[floor(cu)] > 0 ? floor(cu) : -1) : -1;
            tt_pb_cur < 0 ? tt_pb_curKind = 0;
          );
          // style block. A chunk that carries the bank determines the style completely:
          // first back to scheme defaults, then - only if data follows - read the block.
          // Old chunks (before the style block) end after the bank -> style = scheme defaults.
          ok ? (
            tth_f1sz = 0; tth_f2sz = 0; tth_f1on = 0; tth_f2on = 0; tth_bgon = 0;
            tth_uisize = 125; tth_panx = 0; tth_pany = 0; tth_ctgt = 0;
            tth_tipoff = 0;                     // tooltips on (default; old chunks do not know the switch)
            file_avail(0) > 0 ? (
              m2 = 0; file_var(0, m2);
              abs(m2 - TTPB_MAG2) < 256 ? (
                v2 = 0; file_var(0, v2);
                // exact v1: an unknown later block is not misinterpreted
                // (the pointer then stays put - the style block is the last in the chunk,
                // on the next save it is rewritten anyway)
                (v2 == 1 || v2 == 2 || v2 == 3) ? (       // v2 = v1 + one value behind it (tth_tipoff)
                  file_var(0, tth_f1sz); file_var(0, tth_f2sz);
                  file_var(0, tth_f1on); file_var(0, tth_f1R); file_var(0, tth_f1G); file_var(0, tth_f1B);
                  file_var(0, tth_f2on); file_var(0, tth_f2R); file_var(0, tth_f2G); file_var(0, tth_f2B);
                  file_var(0, tth_bgon); file_var(0, tth_bgUR); file_var(0, tth_bgUG); file_var(0, tth_bgUB);
                  tth_f1sz = max(-4, min(8, floor(tth_f1sz + 0.5)));
                  tth_f2sz = max(-4, min(8, floor(tth_f2sz + 0.5)));
                  tth_f1on = tth_f1on > 0.5; tth_f2on = tth_f2on > 0.5; tth_bgon = tth_bgon > 0.5;
                  v2 >= 2 ? ( file_var(0, tth_tipoff); tth_tipoff = tth_tipoff > 0.5; );
                  // version 3: UI zoom, scroll position and picker target. v1/v2 stay readable.
                  v2 >= 3 ? (
                    file_var(0,tth_uisize); file_var(0,tth_panx); file_var(0,tth_pany); file_var(0,tth_ctgt);
                    tth_uisize=max(50,min(400,floor(tth_uisize+0.5)));
                    tth_panx=max(0,tth_panx); tth_pany=max(0,tth_pany); tth_ctgt=max(0,min(2,floor(tth_ctgt+0.5)));
                  );
                  tth_edit=0; tth_cdrag=0; tth_sdrag=0; tth_stini=0;
                );
              );
            );
            // re-apply scheme (+ custom base); tth_cur < 0 means never synced
            // (FX never drawn) - then the first tth_sync adopts the slider scheme.
            tth_cur >= 0 ? ( tth_apply(tth_cur); tth_tgtcol(); tth_rgb2hsv(tth_tr,tth_tg,tth_tb); );
          );
        );
      );
    );
    tt_pb_chkok = 0;
  ) : (
    m = TTPB_MAGIC; ver = 1; nu = tt_pb_nusr; sw = tt_pb_wps; cu = tt_pb_cur; ck = tt_pb_curKind;
    file_var(0, m); file_var(0, ver); file_var(0, nu); file_var(0, sw); file_var(0, cu); file_var(0, ck);
    j = 0;
    loop(tt_pb_nusr, tt_pb_wrone(j); j += 1; );
    // append style block
    m2 = TTPB_MAG2; v2 = 3;                     // block version 3 (v2 added tth_tipoff)
    file_var(0, m2); file_var(0, v2);
    file_var(0, tth_f1sz); file_var(0, tth_f2sz);
    file_var(0, tth_f1on); file_var(0, tth_f1R); file_var(0, tth_f1G); file_var(0, tth_f1B);
    file_var(0, tth_f2on); file_var(0, tth_f2R); file_var(0, tth_f2G); file_var(0, tth_f2B);
    file_var(0, tth_bgon); file_var(0, tth_bgUR); file_var(0, tth_bgUG); file_var(0, tth_bgUB);
    file_var(0, tth_tipoff);
    file_var(0,tth_uisize); file_var(0,tth_panx); file_var(0,tth_pany); file_var(0,tth_ctgt);
  );
);

// at the top of @gfx (after tth_pre): remember the raw mouse; while an overlay is open (and until release), the
// product sees no mouse. The bar itself masks too. During an overlay the OPTIONS button is deaf as well.
function tt_pb_pre() (
  tt_pb_rmx = tth_rmx; tt_pb_rmy = tth_rmy; tt_pb_rcap = tth_rcap; tt_pb_rwh = mouse_wheel;
  tt_pb_act = (tth_open || tth_hold) ? 0 : 1;
  !tt_pb_act ? ( tt_pb_open = 0; tt_pb_conf = 0; );
  tt_pb_open ? ( tt_pb_hold = 1; );
  (tt_pb_hold && (tt_pb_rcap & 1) == 0 && !tt_pb_open) ? ( tt_pb_hold = 0; );
  // the bar masks only when the press did NOT start outside it (otherwise a knob drag across
  // the bar would break off and leave a phantom click on release). tth_rcap0/tth_pcap = raw button now/previous frame.
  tt_pb_ib = tt_pb_bw > 0 && tt_pb_in(tt_pb_bx, tt_pb_by, tt_pb_bw, tt_pb_bh);
  (tth_rcap0 & 1) == 0 ? ( tt_pb_dnout = 0; ) : ( !(tth_pcap & 1) ? ( tt_pb_dnout = !tt_pb_ib; ); );
  (tt_pb_open || tt_pb_hold || (tt_pb_ib && !tt_pb_dnout))
    ? ( mouse_cap = 0; mouse_x = -10000; mouse_y = -10000; mouse_wheel = 0; );
  (tt_pb_open || tt_pb_hold)
    ? ( tth_rcap = 0; tth_rmx = -10000; tth_rmy = -10000; );
);

// at the end of @gfx (before tth_post): draw bar + overlays. px/py = top left corner of the bar in window pixels,
// sc = scale. Returns: action code (see header).
function tt_pb_post(px, py, sc)
  local(bh, aw, gp, sw, mw, nw, W, x1, x2, x3, x4, click, act, wasopen, hl, hn, hr, hs, hm, fs, a, b, kk, so) (
  sc = max(0.5, sc);
  a = 0;
  tt_pb_frm += 1;
  tt_pb_msgt > 0 ? tt_pb_msgt -= 1;
  bh = 17*sc; aw = 17*sc; gp = 2*sc; sw = 42*sc; mw = 24*sc; W = tt_pb_wu*sc;
  nw = W - 2*aw - sw - mw - 4*gp;
  x1 = px + aw + gp; x2 = x1 + nw + gp; x3 = x2 + aw + gp; x4 = x3 + sw + gp;
  tt_pb_bx = px; tt_pb_by = py; tt_pb_bw = W; tt_pb_bh = bh;
  tt_pb_e1 = x1; tt_pb_e2 = x2; tt_pb_e3 = x3; tt_pb_e4 = x4;      // element bounds for tt_modtips (kit)
  fs = max(9, floor(10*sc + 0.5));
  tt_pb_font(fs);
  gfx_mode = 0;
  click = tt_pb_act && (tt_pb_rcap & 1) && !(tt_pb_pcap & 1);
  wasopen = tt_pb_open;
  // overlays (draw last; evaluate first so a click counts only once)
  // bar: clicks (only when no overlay was open)
  hl = tt_pb_act && !wasopen && tt_pb_in(px, py, aw, bh);
  hn = tt_pb_act && !wasopen && tt_pb_in(x1, py, nw, bh);
  hr = tt_pb_act && !wasopen && tt_pb_in(x2, py, aw, bh);
  hs = tt_pb_act && !wasopen && tt_pb_in(x3, py, sw, bh);
  hm = tt_pb_act && !wasopen && tt_pb_in(x4, py, mw, bh);
  (click && !wasopen) ? (
    hl ? ( a = tt_pb_step(-1); )
    : hr ? ( a = tt_pb_step(1); )
    : hn ? (
        tt_pb_open = 1; tt_pb_scr = 0;
        tt_pb_curKind == 1 ? ( tt_pb_scr = max(0, tt_pb_hf + tt_pb_cur - 5); )
        : tt_pb_curKind == 2 ? ( tt_pb_scr = max(0, tt_pb_hf + tt_pb_nfac + 1 + tt_pb_cur - 5); );
      )
    : hs ? (
        // SAVE: current user slot, otherwise first free
        kk = tt_pb_curKind == 2 ? tt_pb_cur : tt_pb_free();
        kk < 0 ? ( tt_pb_msgt = 90; strcpy(#tt_pb_msg, "BANK FULL - DELETE A SLOT"); ) : (
          tt_pb_emode = 1; tt_pb_eslot = kk;
          tt_pb_curKind == 2 ? tt_pb_loadpend(tt_pb_nfac + kk) : tt_pb_defname(kk);
          tt_pb_open = 3;
        );
      )
    : hm ? ( tt_pb_open = 2; tt_pb_conf = 0; );
  );
  // --- draw the bar
  tt_pb_btn(px, py, aw, bh, hl, 0); strcpy(#tt_pb_s, "<"); tt_pb_txt(px, py, aw, bh, 0);
  tt_pb_btn(x1, py, nw, bh, hn, tt_pb_open == 1);
  tt_pb_msgt > 0 ? (
    gfx_set(tth_alR, tth_alG, tth_alB, 1); strcpy(#tt_pb_s, #tt_pb_msg);
  ) : (
    tt_pb_curKind == 1 ? tt_pb_getname(tt_pb_cur)
    : tt_pb_curKind == 2 ? tt_pb_getname(tt_pb_nfac + tt_pb_cur)
    : strcpy(#tt_pb_s, "- no preset -");
    tt_pb_curKind > 0 && tt_pb_mod ? strcat(#tt_pb_s, " *");
    tt_pb_curKind == 0 ? gfx_set(tth_dmR + 0.15, tth_dmG + 0.15, tth_dmB + 0.15, 1) : gfx_set(0.92, 0.95, 0.92, 1);
  );
  tt_pb_fit(nw - 22*sc);
  tt_pb_txt(x1 + 6*sc, py, nw, bh, 1);
  // dropdown arrow
  gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, (hn || tt_pb_open == 1) ? 1 : 0.8);
  gfx_triangle(x1 + nw - 14*sc, py + bh*0.36, x1 + nw - 6*sc, py + bh*0.36, x1 + nw - 10*sc, py + bh*0.68);
  tt_pb_btn(x2, py, aw, bh, hr, 0); strcpy(#tt_pb_s, ">"); tt_pb_txt(x2, py, aw, bh, 0);
  tt_pb_btn(x3, py, sw, bh, hs, tt_pb_open == 3); strcpy(#tt_pb_s, "SAVE"); tt_pb_txt(x3, py, sw, bh, 0);
  tt_pb_btn(x4, py, mw, bh, hm, tt_pb_open == 2); strcpy(#tt_pb_s, "..."); tt_pb_txt(x4, py, mw, bh, 0);
  // --- Overlays
  // overlays have a minimum size (small window: text must not be clipped), width = W or at least 250*0.85
  so = max(sc, 0.85);
  tt_pb_font(max(9, floor(10*so + 0.5)));
  wasopen == 1 ? ( a = tt_pb_dropdown(px, py + bh, max(W, 250*so), so, click); );
  wasopen == 2 ? ( b = tt_pb_menu(px + W, py + bh, so, click); b > 0 ? a = b; );
  wasopen == 3 ? ( b = tt_pb_entry(px, py + bh, so, click); b > 0 ? a = b; );
  // overlay was just opened this frame: draw it now already
  (!wasopen && tt_pb_open == 1) ? ( tt_pb_dropdown(px, py + bh, max(W, 250*so), so, 0); );
  (!wasopen && tt_pb_open == 2) ? ( tt_pb_menu(px + W, py + bh, so, 0); );
  (!wasopen && tt_pb_open == 3) ? ( tt_pb_entry(px, py + bh, so, 0); );
  tt_pb_pcap = tt_pb_rcap;
  a;
);
// ==========================  End TT-Presets  ==========================
// __PRESETS_END__

// Theme test hook and the test commands (sliders 37..40) run only with the
// test unlock tt_testok() (token 20261001 in gmem[tth_gmb - 1] = gmem[5189], namespace tt303_acid;
// only the test scripts write it). The pattern export gmem[0..71] lies far below.

// the ONE version location in the code (the front measures and draws #tt_ver; tt_version_check.py checks it).
strcpy(#tt_ver, "v2.0.0");

// ---------- Memory map ----------
// Note: M_SEQ deliberately lies in a gap that the memset skips.
// @init runs again on every samplerate change and on transport start —
// without this gap the pattern would be gone every time, including the
// one just loaded from the project.
M_STK    = 0;        // 32     note stack (mono, last-note priority); in use: STK_MAX entries
// stack depth 10, the oldest key falls out.
// Devil Fish MIDI In Manual V1.0.4, "Monophonic reception of multiple notes": "a ten-deep internal stack of the most
// recently turned on notes". (M_STK reserves 32 entries; STK_MAX limits how many are used.)
STK_MAX  = 10;
// diagnostics/test cells in the gmem namespace tt303_acid (written only with the test unlock tt_testok(), never otherwise):
//   DG+0 logged events (counter), DG+1 note-ons (velocity > 0), DG+2 note-offs, DG+3 CC-64 events,
//   DG+4 startNote counter (new strikes), DG+10 command "play scenario" (test -> plugin, is set to 0)
//   event log, the first 32 events, 10 cells each from DG+16 + n*10:
//   [0] time in s (play_position + offset), [1..3] MIDI bytes, then the state AFTER the event: [4] stkN, [5] gateHeld,
//   [6] susOn, [7] noteCur, [8] startNote counter, [9] accentNow.
I303_DG  = 5300;
M_SCOPE  = 64;       // 512    oscilloscope ring buffer
M_PAR    = 1792;     // 128    Freeverb layout and state
M_PRE    = 2048;     // 8192   reverb predelay
M_EVT    = 10240;    // 2048   MIDI queue, 512 events x 4 values
M_SEQ    = 12288;    // 1024   4 banks x 16 steps x 4 values [is preserved]
M_UNDO   = 13312;    // 64     one bank of undo (RND/MUT/CLEAR)
M_SEQEND = 13376;
M_DLY1   = 16384;
// v1.2 preset bank: fixed area far above the dynamic delay/reverb buffers (MEMTOP stays below 4 M
// up to 384 kHz), so it lies outside the memsets and does not move with the samplerate.
M_PST    = 5990000;  // 128    slider table of the preset state (32 entries x 4)
M_PBANK  = 6000000;  // ~12 k  tt_pb_* bank (32 user slots), no overlap with anything else

// Size follows the longest possible delay: a half note at 40 BPM
// is 3.0 s. At 1.6 s the buffer already hit the limit below 75 BPM
// and the delay lost its timing.
dlyBufLen = ceil(3.3*srate);
M_DLY2 = M_DLY1 + dlyBufLen + 16;
M_RVB  = M_DLY2 + dlyBufLen + 16;

rvSc     = max(1, srate/44100);              // scale Freeverb lengths
rvSpread = ceil(23*rvSc);
rvbTotal = ceil(25174*rvSc) + 12*rvSpread + 128;
MEMTOP   = M_RVB + rvbTotal + 16;

EVT_MAX = 512;                               // room in the MIDI queue

SRX = srate*2;                               // working rate of the filter (2x)

// step fields and bank size
SF_NOTE = 0; SF_GATE = 1; SF_ACC = 2; SF_SLIDE = 3;
SEQ_BANK = 64;                               // 16 steps x 4 values per bank
SEQ_NLO = 24; SEQ_NHI = 48;                  // C1 .. C3 in the step editor

// layout of the front in the design grid; SC scales to the window size
UI_W = 900; UI_H = 732;
LANE_Y = 544; LANE_H = 92; ROW_H = 3.68;     // 25 semitones in the note lane
GRID_X = 52; GRID_W = 52;                    // 16 columns of 52 points

// HiDPI: REAPER then delivers the real pixel resolution, and because SC
// falls out of gfx_w/gfx_h, the front is automatically drawn larger
// instead of staying tiny.
gfx_ext_retina = 1;

/* ---------- small math helpers ---------- */

// tanh replacement (not every REAPER build has tanh as a builtin)
function fastTanh(x) local(a) (
  a = min(30, max(-30, 2*x));
  (1 - exp(-a))/(1 + exp(-a));
);

// soft saturation without exp — Pade approximation of tanh, saturates at +-1
function softSat(x) local(a) (
  a = min(3, max(-3, x));
  a*(27 + a*a)/(27 + 9*a*a);
);

// 1-sample PolyBLEP. Stays with the classic 1-sample core; the
// improvement comes from the 3-point decimation further down.
function polyBlep(t, dt) (
  t < dt ? ( t /= dt; t + t - t*t - 1 )
  : t > 1 - dt ? ( t = (t - 1)/dt; t*t + t + t + 1 )
  : 0;
);

// Soft limiting instead of a hard clip. Fully linear up to 0.7,
// above that a tanh knee with continuous slope, limit exactly 1.0.
// This way a resonance overshoot no longer clips off rectangularly.
function softClip(x) local(a) (
  a = abs(x);
  a <= 0.7 ? x : (x >= 0 ? 1 : -1)*(0.7 + 0.3*fastTanh((a - 0.7)*3.3333333));
);

/* ---------- Parameters ---------- */

function readSliders() (
  seqMode   = slider1;
  waveSel   = slider2;
  tuneSemi  = slider3;
  fineCent  = slider4;
  cutN      = slider5*0.01;
  resN      = slider6*0.01;
  envN      = slider7*0.01;
  decN      = slider8*0.01;
  accN      = slider9*0.01;
  volG      = slider10*0.01;
  slideSec  = slider11*0.001;
  accThresh = slider12;
  fxDistOn  = slider13;
  distModel = slider14;
  driveG    = max(1, slider15);
  dlyMix    = slider16*0.01;
  dlyDiv    = slider17 == 0 ? 0.5 : slider17 == 1 ? 0.75 : slider17 == 2 ? 1 : 2;
  dlyFb     = slider18*0.01;
  rvbMix    = slider19*0.01;
  roomSz    = (slider20 - 20)/80;
  patLen    = max(1, min(16, floor(slider21)));
  bankBase  = floor(slider25)*SEQ_BANK;
  midiOut   = slider26;
  midiThru  = slider33;
  compOn    = slider34;                        // compressor can be switched off
  compMix   = slider35*0.01;                   // 1 = full (as before), 0 = bypass
  swFrac    = slider22/200;                  // up to 0.375 step offset
  gateFrac  = slider23*0.01;
  freeRun   = slider24;
  eqDLoHz   = slider27; eqDHiHz = slider28;    // input EQs of the FX units
  eqYLoHz   = slider29; eqYHiHz = slider30;
  eqRLoHz   = slider31; eqRHiHz = slider32;
);

function updateParams() (
  // --- Filter. Curves fitted to a Roland TB-303 VST (measured against
  // ref_f_*.wav). The resonance hump is allowed to move up with rising
  // resonance, as on the reference — hence the (1+resN) term in baseF
  // and only a mild poleScale.
  baseF   = 145*exp(cutN*1.95)*(1 + resN);   // ~145 Hz .. ~2 kHz, resonance
                                             // lifts the corner additionally
  kRes    = 1.6 + 6.0*(resN^0.7);            // reso 0 already carries Q~1.6;
                                             // maximum kRes ~7.6
  resMakeUp = 0.62;                          // -4.2 dB flat level trim
  poleScale = 1/(1 + 0.10*kRes);             // mild peak correction
  envOct  = envN*5.2;                        // depth of the envelope
  // Decay curve fitted to ref_dec_0/50/100.wav (decay of the 400-3000 Hz
  // band = "filter closing"): reference tau ~30 / 130 / 574 ms.
  decTau  = 0.03*exp(decN*2.95);             // ~30 ms .. ~570 ms
  mDecC   = exp(-1/(decTau*srate));
  mDecAcc = exp(-1/(0.20*srate));            // accent: fixed 0.2 s
  aDecC   = exp(-1/(0.085*srate));           // accent extra a bit faster
  fcMax   = min(16000, 0.45*SRX);
  // --- couplings in the VCF path
  oscHpA  = exp(-2*$pi*40/SRX);
  sqHpA   = exp(-2*$pi*28/SRX);              // slightly lower tilt
  // Feedback high-pass 20 Hz: DC block only. Higher values pulled the
  // pole frequency below the HP and smothered resonance at low cutoff.
  fbHpA   = exp(-2*$pi*20/SRX);
  // --- VCA. susTau is constant: measured against ref_dec_0/50/100.wav
  // (fundamental decay) at tau ~1.05..1.10 s, largely independent of the
  // decay knob.
  attSec  = 0.003;                           // normal attack
  attSecAcc = 0.0018;                        // accent attack (sharper)
  susTau  = 1.10;                            // ~1.1 s, knob-independent
  susCoef = exp(-1/(susTau*srate));
  relCoef = exp(-1/(0.012*srate));
  // --- Accent capacitor (slightly more aggressive Devil Fish)
  accDecC = exp(-1/(0.10*srate));
  slideSamps = slideSec*srate;              // time constant tau of the RC slide
  // --- Distortion
  // Every model has its own compensation so that a model change does
  // not alter the loudness. Measured against a filtered saw over
  // driveG 1..40: Hard -1.13 dB, Fold -7.92 dB, Fuzz -1.10 dB
  // versus Soft. Fold is trimmed to 2.40 so the peaks keep headroom.
  distMk    = distModel == 1 ? 1.14 : distModel == 2 ? 2.40
            : distModel == 3 ? 1.14 : 1;
  distPreG  = fxDistOn ? driveG : 1;
  distPostG = fxDistOn ? 0.9*distMk/(driveG^0.35) : 1;
  // --- Compressor (3 ms / 250 ms, knee 30, threshold -14 dB, 5:1).
  // The curve below is algebraically identical to the textbook form
  //   over<=-K/2: 0 | |over|<K/2: -(over+K/2)^2/(2K)*(1-1/R)
  //   over>=K/2 : -over*(1-1/R)
  // with K=30, R=5, so (1-1/R)=0.8 and 2K=60. Do not rewrite.
  cAtk = 1 - exp(-1/(0.003*srate));
  cRel = 1 - exp(-1/(0.25*srate));
  // --- Delay
  lpG24   = 1 - exp(-2*$pi*2400/srate);
  // The cross-coupling now runs undamped, the feedback carries the
  // square in return — so the loop gain per round trip stays the same
  // as before, but the right channel also gets signal at 0 %
  // feedback.
  dlyFb2  = dlyFb*dlyFb;
  // --- FX input EQs. 0 Hz / 20 kHz = true bypass (not a=1).
  eqDLoOn = eqDLoHz > 0;     eqDHiOn = eqDHiHz < 20000;
  eqYLoOn = eqYLoHz > 0;     eqYHiOn = eqYHiHz < 20000;
  eqRLoOn = eqRLoHz > 0;     eqRHiOn = eqRHiHz < 20000;
  eqDLoA = eqDLoOn ? exp(-2*$pi*eqDLoHz/srate) : 0;
  eqDHiG = eqDHiOn ? 1 - exp(-2*$pi*eqDHiHz/srate) : 1;
  eqYLoA = eqYLoOn ? exp(-2*$pi*eqYLoHz/srate) : 0;
  eqYHiG = eqYHiOn ? 1 - exp(-2*$pi*eqYHiHz/srate) : 1;
  eqRLoA = eqRLoOn ? exp(-2*$pi*eqRLoHz/srate) : 0;
  eqRHiG = eqRHiOn ? 1 - exp(-2*$pi*eqRHiHz/srate) : 1;
  // --- Reverb
  rhpA    = exp(-2*$pi*250/srate);
  rlpG    = 1 - exp(-2*$pi*3200/srate);
  cmbFb   = 0.7 + 0.25*roomSz;
  cmbDamp = 0.44 - 0.14*roomSz;              // shortest combs a bit deader
  preLen  = floor(min(0.012*srate, 8000));
);

// the ONE write path for sliders 1..35 (front, presets, MIDI CC, test commands).
// tt_slset (theme module) sets the slider only on change (> 1e-7), reports it via slider_automate(2^(n-1))
// to the host (undo point, automation) and sets tt_sldirty; here additionally paramsDirty -> @block re-reads.
// The colour slider 36 keeps its own write path (sliderchange + slider_automate in variable form).
function sl303set(n, v) ( tt_slset(n, v) ? ( paramsDirty = 1; ); );

// snap a value to the grid of the slider declaration (0.1 / 0.5 / 1), only in the write path of operated controls.
function qz303(v, st) ( floor(v/st + 0.5)*st; );

/* ---------- Effects ---------- */

// WaveShaper models (input limited to +-1 like a Web Audio shaper)
function distProc(x) local(c, t, m) (
  c = min(1, max(-1, x));
  distModel == 1 ? ( t = min(0.82, max(-0.82, c*4)); fastTanh(t*1.4); )
  : distModel == 2 ? ( t = c*1.7 + 1; m = t - 4*floor(t/4); (abs(m - 2) - 1)*0.82; )
  : distModel == 3 ? ( c >= 0 ? 1 - exp(-c*4.2) : -(1 - exp(c*2.1)); )
  : fastTanh(3.6*c);
);

// Freeverb comb — i = 0..15 (channel 0: 0..7, channel 1: 8..15)
function combProc(i, x) local(o, idx, y, s) (
  o = M_RVB + M_PAR[i];
  idx = M_PAR[32+i];
  y = o[idx];
  s = M_PAR[48+i]*cmbDamp + y*(1 - cmbDamp);
  M_PAR[48+i] = s;
  o[idx] = x + s*cmbFb;
  idx += 1; idx >= M_PAR[16+i] ? idx = 0;
  M_PAR[32+i] = idx;
  y;
);

// Freeverb allpass — i = 0..7
function apProc(i, x) local(o, idx, y) (
  o = M_RVB + M_PAR[64+i];
  idx = M_PAR[80+i];
  y = o[idx];
  o[idx] = x + 0.5*y;
  idx += 1; idx >= M_PAR[72+i] ? idx = 0;
  M_PAR[80+i] = idx;
  y - x;
);

/* ---------- Voice ---------- */

// The slide of the 303 recharges a capacitor to the new control voltage.
// Because the control voltage is 1 V per octave, in log frequency space
// this is an exponential approach, not a straight line. The difference is
// audible at the end: the RC curve eases out, the straight line kinks off.
// slideSamps is the time constant tau; after 3*tau 95 % is reached.
function startSlide(tl) (
  slideSamps >= 1 ? (
    slideTgt = tl;
    slideCoef = 1 - exp(-1/slideSamps);
    sliding = 1;
  ) : ( curLog = tl; sliding = 0; );
);

// Accent part on its own: recharge the capacitor and start the filter
// sweep. It stands separate because a tied slide note can be accented
// too — then exactly this part may fire, but the envelopes must not
// restart.
function fireAccent() (
  // Recovery: a rested capacitor recharges more strongly (Devil Fish)
  accBoost = accCap < 0.18 ? 1.08 : 0.95;
  accCap = min(1.65, accCap + accBoost);
  accentLed = 1;
  aEnv = 1;
  // Accent sweep: coupled to resonance + slight cutoff dependency
  // and a gentle non-linearity (accCap^1.12) for denser accents
  accOctCur = accN * (0.55 + 2.55*resN) * (0.92 + 0.08*cutN)
              * ((accCap/0.95)^1.12);
);

// Note-on. acc = accent yes/no.
function startNote(acc) (
  tt_testok() ? ( gmem[I303_DG + 4] += 1; );   // diagnostics (only with test unlock)
  accentNow = acc;
  acc ? fireAccent() : ( aEnv = 0; accOctCur = 0; );
  // Level: accent lifts it (slightly stronger at high accCap)
  peakAmp = min(1, 0.5*(1 + (acc ? 0.88*accN*(accCap/0.95) : 0)));
  // Accent gets a shorter attack (1.8 ms) -> sharper note-on
  attInc  = (peakAmp - amp)/max(1, (acc ? attSecAcc : attSec)*srate);
  envStage = 1; gateHeld = 1;
  mEnv = 1;
  mCoef = acc ? mDecAcc : mDecC;             // accent = fixed 0.2 s
);

function voiceOn(n, acc) local(f, i, j, had) (
  // The same note may appear only once in the stack. Some controllers and
  // some hosts send two note-ons without a note-off in between; if the
  // note was then in there twice, a single note-off did not remove it
  // fully any more and the voice stayed stuck. An existing entry is
  // taken out, the note thereby moves to the top and last-note priority
  // stays unchanged.
  // had = the note was already in the stack. A slide into the SAME note (SEQ: SLD step followed by the same
  // note; HOST: second note-on of the same key while the voice is held) ties (no new envelopes).
  // The dedupe stays (no per-key counter): the first note-off ends the note.
  // The HOST case "key already in the stack while the voice is held" does not arrive here (hostOn ignores that note-on).
  had = 0; i = 0; j = 0;
  loop(stkN, M_STK[i] != n ? ( M_STK[j] = M_STK[i]; j += 1; ) : ( had = 1; ); i += 1; );
  stkN = j;
  // stack depth STK_MAX = 10 (Devil Fish): the oldest key falls out.
  stkN >= STK_MAX ? ( i = 0; loop(STK_MAX - 1, M_STK[i] = M_STK[i+1]; i += 1; ); stkN = STK_MAX - 1; );
  M_STK[stkN] = n; stkN += 1;
  noteCur = n;
  f = 440*2^((n - 69 + tuneSemi + fineCent*0.01)/12);
  (stkN > 1 || (had && gateHeld)) ? (
    startSlide(log(f));                      // legato ties, no retrigger
    // A tied step may still be accented. Capacitor and filter sweep
    // fire, the amplitude envelope stays untouched — otherwise it
    // would be a retrigger and not a slide.
    acc ? ( accentNow = 1; fireAccent(); );
  ) : (
    curLog = log(f); sliding = 0;
    startNote(acc);
  );
);

function noteOff(n) local(i, j, v, found) (
  found = 0; j = 0; i = 0;
  loop(stkN,
    v = M_STK[i];
    !found && v == n ? found = 1 : ( M_STK[j] = v; j += 1; );
    i += 1;
  );
  stkN = j;
  stkN > 0 ? (
    M_STK[stkN-1] != noteCur ? (            // last-note priority
      noteCur = M_STK[stkN-1];
      startSlide(log(440*2^((noteCur - 69 + tuneSemi + fineCent*0.01)/12)));
    );
  ) : (
    // Devil Fish CC 64: while sustain is held (susOn) the gate stays on, even when no key is held any more
    // (pitch stays that of the last note). The gate only falls when CC 64 drops below 64 (handleMidi) or on CC 120/123.
    susOn ? 0 : (
      gateHeld = 0;
      envStage == 1 || envStage == 2 ? envStage = 3 : 0;
    );
  );
);

// HOST mode, note-on of a key that is already sounding. Robin Whittle, Devil Fish MIDI In Manual V1.0.4
// (www.firstpr.com.au/rwi/dfish/DF-MIDI-In-Manual.pdf) and MIDI In and Out Manual: "A second Note On event
// for a note which is already On is ignored." - the stack holds each key at most once; the second note-on
// changes nothing (no re-strike, no slide, no accent, no stack change), the first note-off frees the key, a
// further note-off of the same key hits nothing. This way no note can hang.
// Guard: only when the voice is really held (gateHeld); a stale stack entry with a free voice runs
// normally through voiceOn (dedupe + re-strike). Key not in the stack: voiceOn. SEQ: voiceOn.
// The four accent thresholds of the Devil Fish documentation (MIDI In Manual V1.0.4, parameter 6: "Threshold
// equal to or above which Note On Velocity will activate Accent": 65 [up to V1.0.3: 64], 80, 100, 120; default 65).
function accIsDf(v) ( v == 65 || v == 80 || v == 100 || v == 120; );
function accDfNext(v) ( v < 65 ? 65 : v < 80 ? 80 : v < 100 ? 100 : v < 120 ? 120 : 65; );

// CC 64: when only the sustain holds the gate (stack empty, gateHeld, susOn), the gate does not go off and on:
// "this new note does not involve the Gate going Off and On" (Devil Fish MIDI In and Out Manual, Note reception). The new
// note lands in the stack, the pitch jumps (no tie, so no slide: the slide hangs on overlapping keys, here no
// key is held any more), the envelopes keep running; an accent fires like on a tie (fireAccent).
function hostOn(n, acc) local(i, had, f) (
  had = 0; i = 0;
  loop(stkN, M_STK[i] == n ? had = 1; i += 1; );
  had && gateHeld ? 0
  : (susOn && gateHeld && stkN == 0) ? (
    M_STK[0] = n; stkN = 1; noteCur = n;
    f = 440*2^((n - 69 + tuneSemi + fineCent*0.01)/12);
    curLog = log(f); sliding = 0;
    acc ? ( accentNow = 1; fireAccent(); );
  )
  : voiceOn(n, acc);
);

// CC 120/123 also clear the sustain flag ("all Slide and Sustain (Gate) flags ... are turned Off", DF MIDI In and Out Manual).
function allOff() (
  stkN = 0; gateHeld = 0; susOn = 0;
  envStage == 1 || envStage == 2 ? envStage = 3 : 0;
);

/* ---------- Pattern ---------- */

// After loading from the project: pull all steps into valid bounds.
// A corrupted or older file could otherwise smuggle in notes far outside
// SEQ_NLO..SEQ_NHI or flags other than 0/1 — the step editor then draws
// into nothing and seqFire plays unusable notes.
function validateBanks() local(i, v) (
  i = 0;
  loop(4*SEQ_BANK,
    v = M_SEQ[i];
    (i & 3) == SF_NOTE ? ( M_SEQ[i] = min(SEQ_NHI, max(SEQ_NLO, floor(v + 0.5))); )
                       : ( M_SEQ[i] = v > 0.5 ? 1 : 0; );
    i += 1;
  );
);

function setStep(bb, s, n, g, a, sl) (
  M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_NOTE]  = n; M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_GATE]  = g;
  M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_ACC]   = a; M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_SLIDE] = sl;
);

function copyBank(src, dst) local(i) (
  src != dst ? ( i = 0; loop(SEQ_BANK, M_SEQ[dst + i] = M_SEQ[src + i]; i += 1; ); );
);

// undoBank = the bank the snapshot was taken from. The front shows UNDO as
// active only while that bank is displayed (undoArm && undoBank == bb).
function saveUndo(bb) local(i) (
  i = 0; loop(SEQ_BANK, M_UNDO[i] = M_SEQ[bb + i]; i += 1; );
  undoArm = 1; undoBank = bb;
);
function loadUndo() local(i) (
  undoArm ? ( i = 0; loop(SEQ_BANK, M_SEQ[undoBank + i] = M_UNDO[i]; i += 1; ); undoArm = 0; );
);

// COPY from the front. A copy into another bank reports an undo point (tt_undo); if it hits the
// bank the UNDO snapshot came from, the UNDO lapses (it would otherwise replace the copy with the pre-RND/MUT/CLEAR state).
function copyBankUi(src, dst) (
  src != dst ? ( copyBank(src, dst); undoBank == dst ? undoArm = 0; tt_undo(); );
  copyArm = 0;
);

function clearBank(bb) local(s) (
  s = 0; loop(16, setStep(bb, s, 36, 0, 0, 0); s += 1; );
);

// Note supply for the random function: minor pentatonic over C2 — that is
// the register where the typical acid lines sit.
function randNote() local(r) (
  r = rand(1);
  r < 0.44 ? 36 : r < 0.58 ? 39 : r < 0.70 ? 41
  : r < 0.80 ? 43 : r < 0.90 ? 46 : 48;
);

function randPattern(bb) local(s, n) (
  s = 0;
  loop(16,
    n = randNote();
    rand(1) < 0.12 ? n -= 12;                // now and then an octave lower
    M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_NOTE]  = min(SEQ_NHI, max(SEQ_NLO, n));
    M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_GATE]  = rand(1) < 0.78;
    M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_ACC]   = rand(1) < 0.22;
    M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_SLIDE] = rand(1) < 0.16;
    s += 1;
  );
  // The first step always sits and is accented, otherwise the figure
  // starts in nothing and the pattern beginning is not heard.
  setStep(bb, 0, 36, 1, 1, 0);
);

// Mutation: touch only a few steps, the rest stays recognisable.
function mutPattern(bb) local(k, s, r, n) (
  k = 0;
  loop(3,
    s = floor(rand(16));
    r = rand(1);
    r < 0.40 ? (
      n = randNote();
      M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_NOTE] = min(SEQ_NHI, max(SEQ_NLO, n));
    ) : r < 0.62 ? (
      M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_GATE] = 1 - M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_GATE];
    ) : r < 0.82 ? (
      M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_ACC] = 1 - M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_ACC];
    ) : (
      M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_SLIDE] = 1 - M_SEQ[bb + s*4 + SF_SLIDE];
    );
    k += 1;
  );
);

function defaultPattern() local(b, i) (
  setStep(0,  0, 36, 1, 1, 0);  setStep(0,  1, 36, 1, 0, 1);
  setStep(0,  2, 48, 1, 0, 0);  setStep(0,  3, 36, 1, 0, 0);
  setStep(0,  4, 39, 1, 1, 0);  setStep(0,  5, 36, 1, 0, 0);
  setStep(0,  6, 36, 0, 0, 0);  setStep(0,  7, 43, 1, 0, 1);
  setStep(0,  8, 43, 1, 0, 0);  setStep(0,  9, 36, 1, 0, 0);
  setStep(0, 10, 48, 1, 1, 0);  setStep(0, 11, 36, 1, 0, 0);
  setStep(0, 12, 41, 1, 0, 1);  setStep(0, 13, 41, 1, 0, 0);
  setStep(0, 14, 39, 1, 0, 0);  setStep(0, 15, 36, 0, 0, 0);
  b = 1; loop(3, copyBank(0, b*SEQ_BANK); b += 1; );
  // Bank D (index 3): "PUMP" — imported from TT-303_pump_134bpm.mid
  // (134 BPM). The MIDI is two identical bars long; reduced here to the
  // 16 steps of the one bar (nothing is lost). E2 bass with slide 0->1
  // (overlapping identical note in the MIDI) and 10->11, accents on
  // 0/1/8 (velocity 112), rest velocity 80.
  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  0, 40, 1, 1, 1);  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  1, 40, 1, 1, 0);
  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  2, 36, 0, 0, 0);  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  3, 40, 1, 0, 0);
  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  4, 36, 0, 0, 0);  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  5, 28, 1, 0, 0);
  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  6, 40, 1, 0, 0);  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  7, 36, 0, 0, 0);
  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  8, 43, 1, 1, 0);  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK,  9, 36, 0, 0, 0);
  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK, 10, 31, 1, 0, 1);  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK, 11, 31, 1, 0, 0);
  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK, 12, 31, 1, 0, 0);  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK, 13, 43, 1, 0, 0);
  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK, 14, 36, 0, 0, 0);  setStep(3*SEQ_BANK, 15, 31, 1, 0, 0);
);

/* ---------- Sequencer ---------- */

// MIDI to the outside. The offset is the position within the running
// block, so the sequence stays sample-accurate at the output too.
function seqSendOn(n, acc)  ( midiOut ? midisend(smplPos, 0x90, n, acc ? 127 : 100); );
function seqSendOff(n)      ( midiOut ? midisend(smplPos, 0x80, n, 0); );

function seqRelease() (
  seqHeld >= 0 ? ( noteOff(seqHeld); seqSendOff(seqHeld); seqHeld = -1; );
  gateLeft = 0;
);

// Trigger one step. A step's slide flag ties it to the FOLLOWING one —
// which is why prevSlide decides legato or retrigger.
function seqFire(s) local(n, a, oldHeld) (
  curStepDisp = s;
  M_SEQ[bankBase + s*4 + SF_GATE] ? (
    n = min(120, max(0, M_SEQ[bankBase + s*4 + SF_NOTE] + seqTrans));
    a = M_SEQ[bankBase + s*4 + SF_ACC];
    prevSlide ? (
      // do not take the same target note off the stack — otherwise the slide tone dies
      oldHeld = seqHeld;
      // tie into the same note -> no second note-on at SEQ OUT. An accent
      // on the tie step affects the voice (fireAccent in voiceOn) but is lost at SEQ OUT.
      voiceOn(n, a); oldHeld != n ? seqSendOn(n, a);
      oldHeld >= 0 && oldHeld != n ? ( noteOff(oldHeld); seqSendOff(oldHeld); );
    ) : (
      seqHeld >= 0 ? ( noteOff(seqHeld); seqSendOff(seqHeld); );
      voiceOn(n, a); seqSendOn(n, a);
    );
    seqHeld = n;
    prevSlide = M_SEQ[bankBase + s*4 + SF_SLIDE];
    gateLeft = prevSlide ? -1 : max(1, gateFrac*stepSamps);
  ) : (
    seqRelease();
    prevSlide = 0;
  );
);

/* ---------- MIDI ---------- */

// m1 & 0xF0 yields 0x90 / 0x80 / 0xB0 — that is exactly how it must be compared.
function handleMidiDo(m1, m2, m3) local(st, nv) (
  st = m1 & 0xF0;
  st == 0x90 && m3 > 0 ? (
    seqMode ? ( midiHeld += 1; seqTrans = m2 - 36; )
            : hostOn(m2, m3 >= accThresh);
  )
  : (st == 0x80 || (st == 0x90 && m3 == 0)) ? (
    seqMode ? ( midiHeld = max(0, midiHeld - 1); midiHeld == 0 ? seqTrans = 0; )
            : noteOff(m2);
  )
  : st == 0xB0 ? (
    m2 == 123 || m2 == 120 ? ( allOff(); midiHeld = 0; seqTrans = 0; )
    // controller 64 (sustain), HOST only: values 64..127 = flag on, 0..63 = off (Devil Fish: "Values 0 to 63 turn Off the
    // internal flag which can turn the Gate On. Values 64 to 127 turn the flag On."). The gate is the OR of held
    // keys and this flag; releasing with an empty stack drops the gate (release), otherwise the keys keep it.
    // The stack itself is untouched. A press with a free voice starts no tone, it only holds an existing gate.
    : (m2 == 64 && !seqMode) ? (
      m3 >= 64 ? ( susOn = 1; )
      : susOn ? (
        susOn = 0;
        stkN == 0 && gateHeld ? ( gateHeld = 0; envStage == 1 || envStage == 2 ? envStage = 3 : 0; );
      );
    )
    // via sl303set; the value stays unquantised, the host is only notified on change.
    : m2 == 74 ? ( sl303set(5,  m3 * 100 / 127); )  // Cutoff
    : m2 == 71 ? ( sl303set(6,  m3 * 100 / 127); )  // Res
    : m2 == 73 ? ( sl303set(7,  m3 * 100 / 127); )  // Env
    : m2 == 75 ? ( sl303set(8,  m3 * 100 / 127); )  // Decay
    : m2 == 16 ? ( sl303set(9,  m3 * 100 / 127); )  // Accent
    : m2 ==  7 ? ( sl303set(10, m3 * 100 / 127); )  // Volume
    : 0;
  )
  : 0;
);

// diagnostics (only with test unlock): what really reaches handleMidi, and which state the voice is in afterwards.
function i303Diag(m1, m2, m3) local(st, n, a) (
  st = m1 & 0xF0;
  (st == 0x90 && m3 > 0) ? ( gmem[I303_DG + 1] += 1; )
  : (st == 0x80 || st == 0x90) ? ( gmem[I303_DG + 2] += 1; )
  : (st == 0xB0 && m2 == 64) ? ( gmem[I303_DG + 3] += 1; );
  n = gmem[I303_DG];
  n < 32 ? (
    a = I303_DG + 16 + n*10;
    gmem[a] = play_position + smplPos/srate;
    gmem[a + 1] = m1; gmem[a + 2] = m2; gmem[a + 3] = m3;
    gmem[a + 4] = stkN; gmem[a + 5] = gateHeld; gmem[a + 6] = susOn; gmem[a + 7] = noteCur;
    gmem[a + 8] = gmem[I303_DG + 4]; gmem[a + 9] = accentNow;
    gmem[I303_DG] = n + 1;
  );
);

// all MIDI events of the voice pass through here.
function handleMidi(m1, m2, m3) (
  handleMidiDo(m1, m2, m3);
  tt_testok() ? i303Diag(m1, m2, m3);
);

// test scenarios (command in gmem[I303_DG + 10], only with test unlock): plays a fixed event sequence through
// handleMidi, independent of how REAPER outputs raw MIDI events from an item. Starts with CC 123 (base state).
//   1 = On A, On A, Off A (two ons, one off)        2 = 11 ons (40..50), then 10 offs from 50 down to 41
//   3 = sustain: on, CC64 on, off, on (other pitch), CC64 off, off, on, CC64 on, off, CC64 off
//   4 = accent threshold: velocity 64, 65, 79, 80, 99, 100, 119, 120 (each on, off)
//   5 = CC64 on with a free voice, on, off, CC64 off
function i303Inject(k) local(i, v) (
  handleMidi(0xB0, 123, 0);
  k == 1 ? ( handleMidi(0x90, 45, 90); handleMidi(0x90, 45, 90); handleMidi(0x80, 45, 0); )
  : k == 2 ? (
    i = 0; loop(11, handleMidi(0x90, 40 + i, 90); i += 1; );
    i = 0; loop(10, handleMidi(0x80, 50 - i, 0); i += 1; );
  )
  : k == 3 ? (
    handleMidi(0x90, 45, 90); handleMidi(0xB0, 64, 127); handleMidi(0x80, 45, 0);
    handleMidi(0x90, 47, 90); handleMidi(0xB0, 64, 0);   handleMidi(0x80, 47, 0);
    handleMidi(0x90, 48, 90); handleMidi(0xB0, 64, 127); handleMidi(0x80, 48, 0); handleMidi(0xB0, 64, 0);
  )
  : k == 4 ? (
    i = 0; loop(8,
      v = i == 0 ? 64 : i == 1 ? 65 : i == 2 ? 79 : i == 3 ? 80 : i == 4 ? 99 : i == 5 ? 100 : i == 6 ? 119 : 120;
      handleMidi(0x90, 45, v); handleMidi(0x80, 45, 0); i += 1;
    );
  )
  : k == 5 ? (
    handleMidi(0xB0, 64, 127); handleMidi(0x90, 45, 90); handleMidi(0x80, 45, 0); handleMidi(0xB0, 64, 0);
  );
  gmem[I303_DG + 11] = M_STK[0]; gmem[I303_DG + 12] = M_STK[max(0, stkN - 1)];
);

/* ---------- Surface building blocks ----------
   Everything is given in the 900 x 732 design grid. SC is the factor to
   the actual window size, OX/OY centre the image. The mouse is
   converted back into the grid (mX/mY) so that hit tests and drag
   sensitivity stay independent of the zoom.                            */

// Assigned drag IDs (dragId), so that later extensions do not get
// in each other's way:
//   1..17      knobs
//   20..25     handles of the three dual EQ strips
//   1000..1015 columns in the step editor
// Free: 18/19, 26..999, from 1016.

function xrect(x, y, w, h) (
  gfx_rect(OX + x*SC, OY + y*SC, max(1, w*SC), max(1, h*SC), 1);
);
function xline(x1, y1, x2, y2) (
  gfx_line(OX + x1*SC, OY + y1*SC, OX + x2*SC, OY + y2*SC, 1);
);
function xcirc(x, y, r, f) (
  gfx_circle(OX + x*SC, OY + y*SC, max(1, r*SC), f, 1);
);
function xat(x, y) ( gfx_x = OX + x*SC; gfx_y = OY + y*SC; );
function xstr(x, y, s) ( xat(x, y); tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(s); );
function xctr(x, y, w, h, s) local(tw, th) (
  gfx_measurestr(s, tw, th);
  gfx_x = OX + x*SC + (w*SC - tw)*0.5;
  gfx_y = OY + y*SC + (h*SC - th)*0.5;
  tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(s);
);
// at font step +4 and above, wordmark/subtitle, MIDI/MODE, the SYNTHESIZER knob labels, the value line and
// the effect titles overlapped. Fallback fonts at the size of step 0 (smaller steps keep working):
// slot 12 = like slot 3 (sans small), 13 = like slot 4 (mono), 14 = like slot 1 (wordmark). fit303 picks the
// normal font for a text in a box w x h (design grid) as long as it fits, otherwise the fallback font. At step 0
// everything fits -> picture unchanged. (Slot 7 = emergency font of the knobs stays as it is.) Custom text colour:
// tth_txt only knows slots 1..5 -> cap303Col sets it for the fallback font.
function cap303Fonts() local(s, m, b) (
  s = max(9,  floor(13*SC*1.08^min(0, tth_f2sz)));
  m = max(10, floor(16*SC*1.08^min(0, tth_f2sz)));
  b = max(12, floor(38*SC*1.08^min(0, tth_f1sz)));
  (s != cap303S || m != cap303M || b != cap303B) ? (
    cap303S = s; cap303M = m; cap303B = b;
    sansSel == 0 ? gfx_setfont(12, "Segoe UI", s) : sansSel == 1 ? gfx_setfont(12, "Helvetica Neue", s)
    : sansSel == 2 ? gfx_setfont(12, "DejaVu Sans", s) : sansSel == 3 ? gfx_setfont(12, "Liberation Sans", s) : gfx_setfont(12, "Arial", s);
    monoSel == 0 ? gfx_setfont(13, "Consolas", m) : monoSel == 1 ? gfx_setfont(13, "DejaVu Sans Mono", m)
    : monoSel == 2 ? gfx_setfont(13, "Menlo", m) : gfx_setfont(13, "Courier New", m);
    bigSel ? gfx_setfont(14, "Zilap Orion", b, 'b') : sansSel == 0 ? gfx_setfont(14, "Segoe UI", b, 'b')
    : sansSel == 1 ? gfx_setfont(14, "Helvetica Neue", b, 'b') : sansSel == 2 ? gfx_setfont(14, "DejaVu Sans", b, 'b')
    : sansSel == 3 ? gfx_setfont(14, "Liberation Sans", b, 'b') : gfx_setfont(14, "Arial", b, 'b');
  );
);
function fit303(slot, s, w, h) local(tw, th) (
  gfx_setfont(slot); gfx_measurestr(s, tw, th);
  cap303F = (tw > w*SC || th > h*SC) ? (slot == 1 ? 1 : 2) : 0;
  cap303F ? gfx_setfont(slot == 3 ? 12 : (slot == 4 ? 13 : 14));
);
function cap303Col() (
  (cap303F == 1 && tth_f1on) ? gfx_set(tth_f1R, tth_f1G, tth_f1B, gfx_a)
  : (cap303F == 2 && tth_f2on) ? gfx_set(tth_f2R, tth_f2G, tth_f2B, gfx_a);
);
// text fitted into w x h (set the colour beforehand): left (str303F) or centred in the box (ctr303F)
function str303F(x, y, slot, s, w, h) ( fit303(slot, s, w, h); cap303Col(); xstr(x, y, s); );
function ctr303F(x, y, w, h, slot, s) ( fit303(slot, s, w - 2, h + 2); cap303Col(); xctr(x, y, w, h, s); );

function inBox(bx, by, bw, bh) (
  mX >= bx && mX < bx + bw && mY >= by && mY < by + bh;
);

// core colours from the design kit
function colAcid(a)  ( gfx_set(accR, accG, accB, a); );   // accent (ACID = #39FF14), scheme from TT-Theme
function colDim(a)   ( gfx_set(tth_dmR, tth_dmG, tth_dmB, a); );
function colWhite(a) ( gfx_set(1, 1, 1, a); );
function colInk(a)   ( gfx_set(tth_ikR, tth_ikG, tth_ikB, a); );   // tinted, contrast-checked primary text colour of the theme module

// solder pad at the end of a trace
function pad(x, y, r) (
  colAcid(1); xcirc(x, y, r, 1);
  gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 1); xcirc(x, y, r*0.40, 1);
);

// trace: horizontal up to the bend, then 45 degrees
function trace(x1, y1, x2, y2) local(kx) (
  kx = x2 - abs(y2 - y1);
  colDim(1);
  xline(x1, y1, kx, y1);
  xline(kx, y1, x2, y2);
);

function panelBox(x, y, w, h) (
  gfx_set(tth_pnR, tth_pnG, tth_pnB, 1); xrect(x, y, w, h);
  gfx_set(tth_bdR, tth_bdG, tth_bdB, 1);
  xrect(x, y, w, 1); xrect(x, y + h - 1, w, 1);
  xrect(x, y, 1, h); xrect(x + w - 1, y, 1, h);
);

// Switch. Returns 1 if it was clicked in this frame.
function btn(x, y, w, h, on, s) local(hit, hov, fb, tw, th) (
  hov = inBox(x, y, w, h);
  hit = uiClick && hov;
  on ? (
    colAcid(0.88); xrect(x, y, w, h);
    gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 1);
  ) : (
    tth_tn(0.098, 0.103, 0.098, 1); xrect(x, y, w, h);
    hov ? tth_tn(0.30, 0.46, 0.26, 1) : tth_tn(0.15, 0.20, 0.14, 1);
    xrect(x, y, w, 1); xrect(x, y + h - 1, w, 1);
    xrect(x, y, 1, h); xrect(x + w - 1, y, 1, h);
    hov ? tth_tn(0.85, 0.95, 0.82, 1) : tth_tn(0.78, 0.84, 0.76, 1);
  );
  // if the label does not fit the button (large FONT 2 steps), draw with the fallback font (slot 7).
  // Slot 7 lies outside 2..5, so the custom FONT 2 text colour is set here itself (like tth_txt).
  // The font is touched ONLY when the text really does not fit, then reset to slot 2 - all buttons call
  // btn with slot 2, except ACCENT VEL -/+ (slot 3, text "-"/"+", always fits). In the normal state
  // (text fits) btn calls no font function.
  gfx_measurestr(s, tw, th);
  fb = tw > (w - 2)*SC;
  fb ? ( gfx_setfont(7); tth_f2on ? gfx_set(tth_f2R, tth_f2G, tth_f2B, gfx_a); );
  xctr(x, y, w, h, s);
  fb ? gfx_setfont(2);
  hit;
);

// Knob. Drag vertically, Shift = fine, mouse wheel works too.
// Returns the (possibly changed) value.
function knobDef(id) (
  id == 1 ? 0 : id == 2 ? 0 : id == 3 ? 32 : id == 4 ? 55 : id == 5 ? 62
  : id == 6 ? 35 : id == 7 ? 60 : id == 8 ? 70 : id == 9 ? 8 : id == 10 ? 15
  : id == 11 ? 60 : id == 12 ? 18 : id == 13 ? 70 : id == 14 ? 60
  : id == 15 ? 16 : id == 16 ? 0 : id == 17 ? 55 : id == 18 ? 100 : 0;
);

// st = step size like knobst in the kit. st > 0: one step per wheel notch (wheel remainders are
// collected in kn303_wacc; a touchpad delivers many small values); dragging and wheel snap to vmn + k*st.
// st = 0: continuous, wheel = 2 % of the range per notch. At idle knob returns exactly val, so the
// caller only writes when the control is really operated.
function knob(id, cx, cy, r, val, vmn, vmx, st)
  local(t, i, a, ri, ro, nv, dv, hot, sh, def, nTick, wk) (
  nv = val;
  def = knobDef(id);
  sh = (mouse_cap & 8) ? 1 : 0;
  hot = (mX - cx)*(mX - cx) + (mY - cy)*(mY - cy) <= (r + 7)*(r + 7);
  uiRClk && hot ? ( nv = def; )
  : uiClick && hot ? (
      clickId == id && clickWait > 0 ? ( nv = def; dragId = -1; clickWait = 0; )
      : ( dragId = id; dragY = mY; dragV = val; dragSh = sh; clickId = id; clickWait = 12; );
    );
  dragId == id && uiLmb ? (
    sh != dragSh ? ( dragSh = sh; dragY = mY; dragV = val; );
    dv = (dragY - mY)/(sh ? 900 : 170);
    nv = min(vmx, max(vmn, dragV + dv*(vmx - vmn)));
  );
  (st > 0 && nv != val) ? ( nv = min(vmx, max(vmn, vmn + floor((nv - vmn)/st + 0.5)*st)); );
  hot && mouse_wheel != 0 ? (
    st > 0 ? (
      kn303_wacc += mouse_wheel;
      wk = kn303_wacc > 0 ? floor(kn303_wacc/120) : 0 - floor((0 - kn303_wacc)/120);
      kn303_wacc -= wk*120;
      nv = val;
      wk != 0 ? ( nv = min(vmx, max(vmn, vmn + floor((val + wk*st - vmn)/st + 0.5)*st)); );
    ) : (
      nv = min(vmx, max(vmn, val + (mouse_wheel/120)*(vmx - vmn)*0.02));
    );
    mouse_wheel = 0;
  );
  t = (nv - vmn)/(vmx - vmn);
  gfx_set(tth_knR, tth_knG, tth_knB, 1); xcirc(cx, cy, r - 5, 1);
  hot || dragId == id ? tth_tn(0.26, 0.40, 0.24, 1) : tth_tn(0.15, 0.19, 0.14, 1);
  xcirc(cx, cy, r - 5, 0);
  nTick = (hot || dragId == id) ? 24 : 12;
  i = 0;
  loop(nTick + 1,
    a = (-225 + 270*i/nTick)*$pi/180;
    ri = r - 3; ro = r + 1;
    i/nTick <= t ? colAcid(1) : tth_tn(0.16, 0.18, 0.15, 1);
    xline(cx + cos(a)*ri, cy + sin(a)*ri, cx + cos(a)*ro, cy + sin(a)*ro);
    i += 1;
  );
  a = (-225 + 270*t)*$pi/180;
  colWhite(1);
  xline(cx + cos(a)*(r - 16), cy + sin(a)*(r - 16), cx + cos(a)*(r - 7), cy + sin(a)*(r - 7));
  tth_tn(0.30, 0.34, 0.30, 1); xcirc(cx, cy, 2, 1);
  nv;
);

// String in #vstr centred at (cx, y) — set the font beforehand
// centre in raster coordinates (w/SC) and fit the value into the column (knob spacing 65 -> 62 x 18, large font steps).
// callers set slot 4 beforehand (value line of the effect knobs).
function drawCentered(cx, y) local(w, h) (
  fit303(4, #vstr, 62, 18); cap303Col();
  gfx_measurestr(#vstr, w, h);
  xat(cx - w*0.5/SC, y); tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(#vstr);
);

// Label: label (#klbl) in grey, value (#kval) in acid green,
// from the left edge x0. The caller computes the position from the
// measured widths so nothing collides with the neighbouring text.
function kvLabel(x0, y) local(lw, vh) (
  gfx_setfont(3);
  gfx_measurestr(#klbl, lw, vh);
  xat(x0, y); colInk(1); tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(#klbl);
  xat(x0 + lw + 6, y); colAcid(1); tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(#kval);
);

/* ---------- Dual EQ slider under each effect unit ----------
   Logarithmic scale 20 Hz .. 20 kHz: f = 20*1000^t. The left edge
   (t = 0) is the lowcut and snaps to OFF (0 Hz), the right one
   (t = 1) the highcut to OFF (20 kHz). Right-click on a handle
   resets the factory setting.                                      */

// Position in the strip (0..1) for a frequency: log(hz/20)/log(1000)
// — 20 Hz far left, 20 kHz far right, OFF (0 Hz) on the left edge.
// Conversion and the way back in fxEq must be mirror images,
// otherwise the handle jumps when grabbed.
function eqT(hz) ( min(1, max(0, log(max(20, hz)*0.05)*0.144764827)); );

// compact frequency display in #vstr
function hzTxt(hz) (
  hz <= 0 || hz >= 20000 ? sprintf(#vstr, "OFF")
  : hz >= 9950 ? sprintf(#vstr, "%dk", floor(hz*0.001 + 0.5))
  : hz >= 1000 ? sprintf(#vstr, "%.1fk", hz*0.001)
  : sprintf(#vstr, "%d", floor(hz + 0.5));
);

// run of the strip; the field between the handles is the
// passed band
function eqTrack(x, y, w, tLo, tHi) (
  tth_tn(0.092, 0.097, 0.092, 1); xrect(x, y, w, 6);
  tHi > tLo ? ( colAcid(0.30); xrect(x + tLo*w, y + 1, (tHi - tLo)*w, 4); );
);

// One handle: side 0 = lowcut (left), side 1 = highcut (right).
// This function only computes, drawing happens in eqHandle.
//
// The travel factor is the strip width w, no longer the fixed 170 of the
// knobs. Only that way does the handle track exactly under the mouse
// pointer. On a 284 point wide strip it ran with 170 by a factor of
// 1.67 too fast — which is why the EQ sliders did not track cleanly.
// Shift = five times finer, with a moving reference point.
function fxEqVal(id, x, y, w, hz, side, defHz)
  local(t, hot, nv, hx, sh) (
  t  = eqT(hz);
  hx = x + t*w;
  sh = (mouse_cap & 8) ? 1 : 0;
  hot = mX >= hx - 8 && mX <= hx + 8 && mY >= y - 7 && mY <= y + 11;
  nv = hz;
  uiRClk && hot ? ( nv = defHz; )
  : uiClick && hot ? ( dragId = id; dragX = mX; dragT = t; dragSh = sh; );
  dragId == id && uiLmb ? (
    sh != dragSh ? ( dragSh = sh; dragX = mX; dragT = t; );
    t = min(1, max(0, dragT + (mX - dragX)/(sh ? w*5 : w)));
    nv = floor(20*1000^t + 0.5);
    side == 0 ? ( nv = t < 0.02 ? 0 : nv; ) : ( nv = t > 0.98 ? 20000 : nv; );
  ) : (
    hot && mouse_wheel != 0 ? (
      t = min(1, max(0, t + (mouse_wheel/120)*0.05));
      nv = floor(20*1000^t + 0.5);
      side == 0 ? ( nv = t < 0.02 ? 0 : nv; ) : ( nv = t > 0.98 ? 20000 : nv; );
      mouse_wheel = 0;
    );
  );
  nv;
);

// One handle, drawing only. Kept apart from the computing so that the
// passed band stands in the same frame as the handle — before, the
// strip ran a frame behind the handle while dragging.
function eqHandle(id, x, y, w, hz) local(hx) (
  hx = x + eqT(hz)*w;
  dragId == id || (mX >= hx - 8 && mX <= hx + 8 && mY >= y - 7 && mY <= y + 11)
    ? colAcid(1) : tth_tn(0.17, 0.44, 0.12, 1);
  xrect(hx - 4, y - 4, 8, 14);
  gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 1); xrect(hx - 1, y, 2, 6);
);

// LO/HI labelling with frequency values under an EQ strip
function eqLabels(x, y, w, loHz, hiHz) local(a, b, c, d, x0) (
  gfx_setfont(3);
  hzTxt(loHz); gfx_measurestr(#vstr, a, b);
  gfx_measurestr("LO", c, d);
  xat(x, y); colInk(1); tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr("LO");
  xat(x + c + 5, y); colAcid(0.85); tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(#vstr);
  hzTxt(hiHz); gfx_measurestr(#vstr, a, b);
  gfx_measurestr("HI", c, d);
  x0 = x + w - (a + 5 + c);
  xat(x0, y); colInk(1); tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr("HI");
  xat(x0 + c + 5, y); colAcid(0.85); tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(#vstr);
);

/* ---------- Tooltips ----------
   The plugin has no UI kit, so a small mechanics of its own in the style of tt_hov / tt_tipflush:
   each control reports its help text with tip303_hov (design grid, after drawing the element;
   with several hits the last reported wins, so small elements AFTER their field).
   tip303_flush at the end of @gfx draws the text after 0.35 s of hovering, not while dragging, and nothing
   when TOOLTIPS OFF is set in the OPTIONS box (tth_tipoff = 1). The header (preset bar, OPTIONS) lies
   under the masking of the theme/preset modules -> there tip303_hovr with the raw coordinates tth_rmx/tth_rmy. */
function tip303_hov(x, y, w, h, s) (
  inBox(x, y, w, h) ? ( strcpy(#tip303_s, s); tip303_on = 1; tip303_x = mX; tip303_y = mY; );
);
// raw-coordinate variant of tip303_hov.
function tip303_hovr(x, y, w, h, s) local(rx, ry) (
  tt_pb_act ? (                     // no tooltips under an open OPTIONS box / preset list
    rx = (tth_rmx - OX)/SC; ry = (tth_rmy - OY)/SC;
    rx >= x && rx < x + w && ry >= y && ry < y + h ? ( strcpy(#tip303_s, s); tip303_on = 1; tip303_x = rx; tip303_y = ry; );
  );
);
// header tooltips like tt_modtips in the UI kit (the plugin has no kit) - same
// conditions, same texts per element, same element bounds (tth_bx/by/bw/bh from tth_post, tt_pb_bx.. and
// tt_pb_e1..e4 from tt_pb_post, all window pixels of the previous frame).
// The mechanics stay its own: text to #tip303_s, position in the design grid for tip303_flush.
function tip303_modtips() local(hit) (
  hit = 0;
  (tth_on && !tth_open && !tth_hold && !tt_pb_open && !tt_pb_hold && (tth_rcap & 1) == 0) ? (
    (tth_bw > 0 && tth_rmx >= tth_bx && tth_rmx < tth_bx + tth_bw && tth_rmy >= tth_by && tth_rmy < tth_by + tth_bh) ? (
      strcpy(#tip303_s, "OPTIONS: colour scheme, font sizes, custom colours and TOOLTIPS ON / OFF. Per instance, saved with the project.");
      hit = 1;
    ) : (tt_pb_bw > 0 && tth_rmx >= tt_pb_bx && tth_rmx < tt_pb_bx + tt_pb_bw && tth_rmy >= tt_pb_by && tth_rmy < tt_pb_by + tt_pb_bh) ? (
      tth_rmx < tt_pb_e1 ? strcpy(#tip303_s, "Previous preset.")
      : tth_rmx < tt_pb_e2 ? strcpy(#tip303_s, "Current preset (* = changed since loading). Click opens the list of factory and user presets.")
      : tth_rmx < tt_pb_e3 ? strcpy(#tip303_s, "Next preset.")
      : tth_rmx < tt_pb_e4 ? strcpy(#tip303_s, "SAVE: store the current state as a user preset (saved with the project).")
      : strcpy(#tip303_s, "Preset menu: rename, copy or delete the current user preset, or INIT (back to the default state).");
      hit = 1;
    );
    hit ? ( tip303_on = 1; tip303_x = (tth_rmx - OX)/SC; tip303_y = (tth_rmy - OY)/SC; );
  );
);
// the two handles and the strip of an input EQ (grid like fxEqVal/eqHandle: handle +-8, y-7..y+11).
function tip303_eq(x, y, w, loHz, hiHz, sStrip) local(hx) (
  tip303_hov(x - 8, y - 8, w + 16, 32, sStrip);
  hx = x + eqT(loHz)*w;
  tip303_hov(hx - 8, y - 7, 16, 18, "Low cut: lower frequencies bypass this effect (far left = OFF). Drag; right-click resets.");
  hx = x + eqT(hiHz)*w;
  tip303_hov(hx - 8, y - 7, 16, 18, "High cut: higher frequencies bypass this effect (far right = OFF). Drag; right-click resets.");
);
// call exactly once at the end of @gfx (after the front, before the overlays tt_pb_post / tth_post).
function tip303_flush() local(t, tw, th, bw, bh, px, py) (
  tth_tipoff || !tip303_on ? (
    strcpy(#tip303_p, "");
  ) : (
    t = time_precise();
    strcmp(#tip303_s, #tip303_p) != 0 || uiLmb || (tth_rcap & 1) ? ( strcpy(#tip303_p, #tip303_s); tip303_t = t; );
    t - tip303_t >= 0.35 ? (
      gfx_setfont(5);
      gfx_measurestr(#tip303_s, tw, th);
      bw = tw + 14; bh = th + 8;
      px = OX + (tip303_x + 14)*SC; py = OY + (tip303_y + 18)*SC;
      px = max(2, min(px, gfx_w - bw - 2));
      py = max(2, min(py, gfx_h - bh - 2));
      gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 0.40); gfx_rect(px + 2, py + 3, bw, bh, 1);
      gfx_set(0.030, 0.040, 0.030, 1); gfx_rect(px, py, bw, bh, 1);
      tth_tn(0.62, 1.0, 0.50, 1); gfx_roundrect(px, py, bw - 1, bh - 1, 2, 1);
      gfx_set(0.88, 1.0, 0.85, 1);
      gfx_x = px + 7; gfx_y = py + 4;
      tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(#tip303_s);
    );
  );
  tip303_on = 0;
);

// note name, e.g. "C#2" — draws at the current text position
function noteName(n) local(k, o) (
  k = n - 12*floor(n/12); o = floor(n/12) - 1;
  tth_txt();
  k == 0 ? gfx_drawstr("C") : k == 1 ? gfx_drawstr("C#") : k == 2 ? gfx_drawstr("D")
  : k == 3 ? gfx_drawstr("D#") : k == 4 ? gfx_drawstr("E") : k == 5 ? gfx_drawstr("F")
  : k == 6 ? gfx_drawstr("F#") : k == 7 ? gfx_drawstr("G") : k == 8 ? gfx_drawstr("G#")
  : k == 9 ? gfx_drawstr("A") : k == 10 ? gfx_drawstr("A#") : gfx_drawstr("B");
  gfx_printf("%d", o);
);

// Is this note currently in the stack? (for the keyboard display)
function noteHeld(n) local(i, r) (
  r = 0; i = 0;
  loop(stkN, M_STK[i] == n ? r = 1; i += 1; );
  r;
);

/* ---------- Sound presets ---------- */

// Five factory patches plus INIT, tuned for the current engine.
// SCREAM and HOOVER use the square wave. INIT also sets Comp ON/100 %
// and the delay/reverb input EQs (250 Hz..3.0 kHz resp. 300 Hz..2.3 kHz).
// written via sl303set (only reports what changed).
function apSet12(a2, a5, a6, a7, a8, a9, a13, a14, a15, a16, a18, a19) (
  sl303set(2, a2);   sl303set(5, a5);   sl303set(6, a6);   sl303set(7, a7);
  sl303set(8, a8);   sl303set(9, a9);   sl303set(13, a13); sl303set(14, a14);
  sl303set(15, a15); sl303set(16, a16); sl303set(18, a18); sl303set(19, a19);
);
function applyPatch(p) (
  p == 1 ? ( apSet12(0, 14, 40, 40, 64, 35, 0, 0, 7,  14, 50, 16); )              // DEEP
  : p == 2 ? ( apSet12(0, 52, 80, 82, 22, 80, 1, 0, 8,  16, 62, 12); )            // SQUELCH
  : p == 3 ? ( apSet12(1, 72, 88, 92, 15, 95, 1, 1, 16, 10, 55, 9); )             // SCREAM
  : p == 4 ? ( apSet12(1, 74, 68, 96, 55, 70, 1, 2, 11, 20, 62, 24); )            // HOOVER
  : p == 5 ? ( apSet12(0, 18, 52, 44, 82, 50, 0, 0, 7,  46, 80, 44); )            // DUB
  : ( apSet12(0, 32, 55, 62, 35, 60, 0, 0, 8,  15, 60, 18);
      sl303set(11, 60);  sl303set(17, 1);     sl303set(20, 70);
      sl303set(27, 0);   sl303set(28, 20000); sl303set(29, 250); sl303set(30, 3000);
      sl303set(31, 300); sl303set(32, 2300);  sl303set(34, 1);   sl303set(35, 100); );   // INIT
  patchSel = p;
  paramsDirty = 1;
);

/* ---------- Base state ---------- */

readSliders();

// @init runs again at EVERY transport start (no ext_noinit). Three stages:
//   i303_first  first run (loading)                    -> preset everything, including the UI state
//   i303_hard   first run, samplerate change OR        -> buffers (memset), voice, effect and sequencer state
//               the device is currently silent            anew; silent = inaudible, and a render starts
//                                                           from the base state (renders stay reproducible)
//   else        transport start while something sounds -> reset nothing: voice, delay/reverb tail and
//                                                           sequencer keep running; @block rejoins the sequencer
// "silent": voice at rest (like needVoice in @sample), delay/reverb output and the last 512 scope values
// (~21 ms at 48 kHz) below 1e-5 (-100 dBFS). An echo currently sitting in a pause in the delay buffer is then
// discarded (without a click, the output is quiet). UI state only on the first run.
i303_first = i303_ini1 != 1;
i303_quiet = amp < 0.00002 && stkN == 0 && envStage == 0 && !sliding
          && abs(lpL) + abs(lpR) + abs(rlpL) + abs(rlpR) < 0.00001;
i = 0; loop(512, abs(M_SCOPE[i]) >= 0.00001 ? i303_quiet = 0; i += 1; );
i303_hard = i303_first || i303_sr != srate || i303_quiet;
// a held SEQ OUT note whose state is about to be discarded gets its note-off in the next @block.
(!i303_first && i303_hard && seqHeld >= 0) ? ( seqOffPend = seqHeld + 1; );
i303_ini1 = 1; i303_sr = srate;

// Two memsets: the pattern gap stays untouched.
// only on i303_hard.
i303_hard ? (
  memset(0, 0, M_SEQ);
  memset(M_SEQEND, 0, MEMTOP - M_SEQEND);
);

// Freeverb: 8 combs + 4 allpasses per channel, lengths scale with srate
M_PAR[16] = ceil(1116*rvSc); M_PAR[17] = ceil(1188*rvSc);
M_PAR[18] = ceil(1277*rvSc); M_PAR[19] = ceil(1356*rvSc);
M_PAR[20] = ceil(1422*rvSc); M_PAR[21] = ceil(1491*rvSc);
M_PAR[22] = ceil(1557*rvSc); M_PAR[23] = ceil(1617*rvSc);
i = 0; loop(8, M_PAR[24+i] = M_PAR[16+i] + rvSpread; i += 1; );
p = 0;
i = 0; loop(8, M_PAR[i]   = p; p += M_PAR[16+i]; i += 1; );
i = 0; loop(8, M_PAR[8+i] = p; p += M_PAR[24+i]; i += 1; );
M_PAR[72] = ceil(556*rvSc); M_PAR[73] = ceil(441*rvSc);
M_PAR[74] = ceil(341*rvSc); M_PAR[75] = ceil(225*rvSc);
i = 0; loop(4, M_PAR[76+i] = M_PAR[72+i] + rvSpread; i += 1; );
i = 0; loop(4, M_PAR[64+i] = p; p += M_PAR[72+i]; i += 1; );
i = 0; loop(4, M_PAR[68+i] = p; p += M_PAR[76+i]; i += 1; );

updateParams();

// Start pattern only the very first time — after that either the
// self-built banks or the ones loaded from the project stand here.
patInit != 1 ? ( defaultPattern(); patInit = 1; );

// voice, effect state and sequencer run only on i303_hard (first run, samplerate change, silent).
i303_hard ? (
  // Voice
  stkN = 0; gateHeld = 0; envStage = 0; amp = 0; peakAmp = 0.5; accentNow = 0;
  accCap = 0; sliding = 0; slideTgt = 0; slideCoef = 0; noteCur = 36;
  curLog = log(65.406); phase = 0;
  mEnv = 0; aEnv = 0; mCoef = 1; accOctCur = 0;
  s1 = 0; s2 = 0; s3 = 0; y3prev = 0;
  oscHpY = 0; oscHpX = 0; sqHpY = 0; sqHpX = 0; fbHpY = 0; fbHpX = 0;
  // Effect state
  envDb = -100; dlyPos = 0; prePos = 0;
  hpY = 0; hpPrev = 0; lpL = 0; lpR = 0;
  dHpY = 0; dHpX = 0; dLpY = 0; dlyLpY = 0;    // FX input EQs
  dPrevIn = 0; dsPrev = 0;                     // drive oversampling
  rvHpY = 0; rvHpX = 0; rvLpY = 0;
  rhpL = 0; rhpXL = 0; rlpL = 0; rhpR = 0; rhpXR = 0; rlpR = 0;
  scopePos = 0; accentLed = 0; bpmNow = 120;
  dlySamps = min(dlyBufLen - 4, 0.75*(60/120)*srate);
  // control flow (sequencer run; @block restarts it as soon as seqWant != seqRunning)
  seqHeld = -1; prevSlide = 0; gateLeft = 0; lastStep = -1; seqPos = 0;
  curStepDisp = 0; seqRunning = 0;
  stepSamps = srate*0.125; stepInc = 1/stepSamps;
  fcPrev = -1; osPrev = 0; osA = 0; osB = 0; scopeDiv = 0;
  rvbWas = rvbMix > 0.005;      // state of the reverb bypass, see @sample
  g = 0; G = 0;
);
// control flow - reset in every @block anyway (MIDI queue, block offset), so always.
evN = 0; evRd = 0; smplPos = 0; paramsDirty = 0;
// UI and playing state only on the first run.
// A held transpose key (midiHeld/seqTrans) and modePrev survive a transport start (modePrev = -1
// would make @block run seqRelease()/allOff() at every start and lose the transposition).
i303_first ? (
  seqTrans = 0; midiHeld = 0; modePrev = -1;
  susOn = 0;                       // CC 64 flag (UI state like the transpose key: survives a transport start)
  // Surface
  SC = 1; OX = 0; OY = 0; mX = -1; mY = -1;
  dragId = -1; dragX = 0; dragY = 0; dragV = 0; dragT = 0; dragSh = 0;
  bigSel = 0;
  paintRow = -1; lmbPrev = 0; rmbPrev = 0;
  tip303_on = 0; tip303_t = 0; tip303_x = 0; tip303_y = 0;   // tooltip state
  monoSel = 0; sansSel = 0; fontChk = 0; patchSel = 0; copyArm = 0;
  fBigP = -1; fMedP = -1; fSmlP = -1; fCapP = -1;
  clickId = -1; clickWait = 0; undoArm = 0; undoBank = 0;
  kn303_wacc = 0; seqOffPend = 0;
);

// TT-Theme: colour scheme from the hidden slider (UI Color, not part of patches/random/undo)
tth_sync(slider36);

/* ---------- Preset bank (module tt-presets) ----------
   Preset state: 31 sliders (table M_PST: number, min, max, default) + the four
   pattern banks (4*SEQ_BANK = 256 words). Slot layout (PB_PSW words): [0] layout version 1, [1..31] sliders in
   table order, [32..287] M_SEQ, rest reserved (wordsPerSlot may only grow).
   NOT part of it: slider1 MODE, 24 FREE RUN, 26 SEQ OUT, 33 MIDI THRU, 36 UI COLOR, 37..40 test interface.
   Applied in @gfx like applyPatch/RND/copyBank (same thread as every other pattern edit). */
PB_N   = 31;
PB_PSW = 320;
function pbMap(i, sn, lo, hi, df) local(a) ( a = M_PST + i*4; a[0] = sn; a[1] = lo; a[2] = hi; a[3] = df; );
pbMap(0, 2, 0, 1, 0);       pbMap(1, 3, -24, 24, 0);    pbMap(2, 4, -50, 50, 0);
pbMap(3, 5, 0, 100, 32);    pbMap(4, 6, 0, 100, 55);    pbMap(5, 7, 0, 100, 62);
pbMap(6, 8, 0, 100, 35);    pbMap(7, 9, 0, 100, 60);    pbMap(8, 10, 0, 100, 70);
pbMap(9, 11, 0, 300, 60);   pbMap(10, 12, 1, 127, 65);   // default 65 (Devil Fish) pbMap(11, 13, 0, 1, 0);
pbMap(12, 14, 0, 3, 0);     pbMap(13, 15, 1, 40, 8);    pbMap(14, 16, 0, 100, 15);
pbMap(15, 17, 0, 3, 1);     pbMap(16, 18, 0, 90, 60);   pbMap(17, 19, 0, 100, 18);
pbMap(18, 20, 20, 100, 70); pbMap(19, 21, 1, 16, 16);   pbMap(20, 22, 0, 75, 0);
pbMap(21, 23, 10, 100, 55); pbMap(22, 25, 0, 3, 0);     pbMap(23, 27, 0, 20000, 0);
pbMap(24, 28, 20, 20000, 20000); pbMap(25, 29, 0, 20000, 250); pbMap(26, 30, 20, 20000, 3000);
pbMap(27, 31, 0, 20000, 300); pbMap(28, 32, 20, 20000, 2300); pbMap(29, 34, 0, 1, 1);
pbMap(30, 35, 0, 100, 100);

// pbApply/pbInit write via sl303set (same mask 2^(n-1), plus tt_sldirty/paramsDirty).

function pbCapture() local(i, a) (            // state -> tt_pb_buf
  memset(tt_pb_buf, 0, PB_PSW);
  tt_pb_buf[0] = 1;
  i = 0; loop(PB_N, a = M_PST + i*4; tt_pb_buf[1 + i] = slider(a[0]); i += 1; );
  memcpy(tt_pb_buf + 1 + PB_N, M_SEQ, 4*SEQ_BANK);
);

function pbApply() local(i, a, v) (           // tt_pb_buf -> state
  i = 0;
  loop(PB_N,
    a = M_PST + i*4;
    v = min(a[2], max(a[1], tt_pb_buf[1 + i]));   // guard against damaged bank data
    sl303set(a[0], v);
    i += 1;
  );
  memcpy(M_SEQ, tt_pb_buf + 1 + PB_N, 4*SEQ_BANK);
  validateBanks(); patInit = 1;
  paramsDirty = 1; patchSel = -1; undoArm = 0; copyArm = 0;
);

function pbInit() local(i, a) (                // basic state: slider defaults + start pattern
  i = 0; loop(PB_N, a = M_PST + i*4; sl303set(a[0], a[3]); i += 1; );
  defaultPattern(); patInit = 1;
  paramsDirty = 1; patchSel = -1; undoArm = 0; copyArm = 0;
);

function pbSum() local(i, a, s) (              // checksum for the '*' (state differs from the loaded preset)
  s = 0;
  i = 0; loop(PB_N, a = M_PST + i*4; s += slider(a[0])*(i + 1); i += 1; );
  i = 0; loop(4*SEQ_BANK, s += M_SEQ[i]*(i + 1); i += 1; );
  s;
);

tt_pb_init(6, 32, M_PBANK, PB_PSW);
tt_pb_fname(0, "INIT");  tt_pb_fname(1, "DEEP");  tt_pb_fname(2, "SQUELCH");
tt_pb_fname(3, "SCREAM"); tt_pb_fname(4, "HOOVER"); tt_pb_fname(5, "DUB");


/* ============================================================
   @serialize — all four banks travel into the project and into presets
   ============================================================ */
@serialize

seqVer = 2;
file_var(0, seqVer);
file_mem(0, M_SEQ, 4*SEQ_BANK);
// Runs in both directions. On write it is a no-op, because the values
// are valid anyway; on read it catches corrupted or foreign data.
// Future format changes belong here via seqVer.
validateBanks();
patInit = 1;
// preset bank AFTER the old blob (seqVer + 4 banks stay untouched; old projects end here,
// file_avail = 0 -> the bank stays empty).
tt_pb_serialize();
// since tt_undo() REAPER plays the state back into the RUNNING instance via this read branch on every Ctrl+Z.
// Checked: only M_SEQ (validateBanks clamps) and the bank are read here; REAPER restores the sliders itself
// (@slider -> readSliders/updateParams). Voice, stack, seqHeld, sequencer position and SEQ OUT note stay
// untouched - the next step releases the held note as usual, nothing hangs. No factory preset is loaded
// afterwards (patInit = 1). UNDO arm/undoBank deliberately stay (M_UNDO is a valid pattern).

/* ============================================================
   @slider
   ============================================================ */
@slider

readSliders();
updateParams();

/* ============================================================
   @block — transport, timing, collecting MIDI
   ============================================================ */
@block

// reset block offset and MIDI queue first. seqRelease() further down (mode change,
// transport stop) sends its note-off with smplPos - which would otherwise still hold the previous block's length.
evN = 0; evRd = 0; smplPos = 0;

// play a test scenario (only with test unlock), see i303Inject
(tt_testok() && gmem[I303_DG + 10] > 0) ? ( k303 = gmem[I303_DG + 10]; gmem[I303_DG + 10] = 0; i303Inject(k303); );

// note-off for a SEQ OUT note whose state an @init rebuild discarded.
seqOffPend > 0 ? ( midiOut ? midisend(0, 0x80, seqOffPend - 1, 0); seqOffPend = 0; );

// clear the flag BEFORE reading - if @gfx (other thread) sets it again during readSliders(), the
// change is no longer lost. tt_sldirty (tt_slset in the theme module) is queried and cleared here too.
(paramsDirty || tt_sldirty) ? ( paramsDirty = 0; tt_sldirty = 0; readSliders(); updateParams(); );

// Test interface for the preset bank (hidden sliders 37..40, never touched in normal use):
// CMD 11 count/current, 12 slot checksum (IDX = slot), 13 state checksum + '*', 14 save into slot IDX,
// 15 load user slot IDX, 16 load factory IDX (0..5), 17 INIT, 18 name checksum (IDX = slot), 19 last key/count, 20 RND
// Q CMD is an automatable parameter. Writing commands (14..17, 20) and those with
// loops over bank/state (12, 13, 18 - sustained load in the audio thread while the value stands) run only with the
// test unlock tt_testok() (gmem[5189] = 20261001, set only by the test scripts); without the unlock the command
// is discarded (slider38 = 0 as usual after a command). 11 and 19 only read two values and stay free.
pbQ = floor(slider37);
pbC = slider38;
(pbC != 0 && pbC != 11 && pbC != 19 && !tt_testok()) ? ( slider38 = 0; pbC = 0; );
pbC == 11 ? ( slider39 = tt_pb_count(); slider40 = tt_pb_curKind*1000 + tt_pb_cur; );
pbC == 12 ? (
  pbBs = 0; pbBj = 0;
  loop(PB_PSW, pbBs += (tt_pb_data + (pbQ & 31)*PB_PSW)[pbBj]*(pbBj + 1); pbBj += 1; );
  slider39 = pbBs; slider40 = tt_pb_used[pbQ & 31];
);
pbC == 13 ? ( slider39 = pbSum(); slider40 = tt_pb_mod; );
pbC == 14 ? ( pbCapture(); tt_pb_defname(pbQ & 31); tt_pb_commit(pbQ & 31, PB_PSW); slider38 = 0; );
pbC == 15 ? ( tt_pb_fetch(pbQ & 31) > 0 ? ( pbApply(); tt_pb_select(2, pbQ & 31); ); slider38 = 0; );
pbC == 16 ? ( applyPatch(min(5, pbQ)); tt_pb_select(1, min(5, pbQ)); slider38 = 0; );
pbC == 17 ? ( pbInit(); slider38 = 0; );
pbC == 18 ? (
  pbBs = 0; pbBj = 0;
  loop(TTPB_NW, pbBs += (tt_pb_names + (tt_pb_nfac + (pbQ & 31))*TTPB_NW)[pbBj]*(pbBj + 1); pbBj += 1; );
  slider39 = pbBs; slider40 = 0;
);
pbC == 19 ? ( slider39 = tt_pb_lk; slider40 = tt_pb_nk; );
pbC == 20 ? ( saveUndo(bankBase); randPattern(bankBase); slider38 = 0; );   // 20 = RND on the active bank (test only)
// note: 14..17/20 run in the audio thread on tt_pb_buf resp. M_SEQ, which @gfx also uses; with the
// unlock only in test runs (the test scripts do not operate the front at the same time).

bpmNow    = tempo > 10 ? tempo : 120;
stepSamps = max(16, srate*15/bpmNow);        // one 16th in samples
stepInc   = 1/stepSamps;
dlySamps  = min(dlyBufLen - 4, (60/bpmNow)*dlyDiv*srate);

// catch a mode change cleanly
seqMode != modePrev ? (
  modePrev = seqMode;
  seqRelease(); allOff();
  midiHeld = 0; seqTrans = 0; lastStep = -1; prevSlide = 0;
);

hostPlay = play_state & 1;
seqWant  = seqMode && (hostPlay || freeRun);
seqWant != seqRunning ? (
  seqRunning = seqWant;
  seqRunning ? (
    prevSlide = 0;
    hostPlay ? ( seqPos = beat_position*4; ) : ( seqPos = 0; );
    lastStep = floor(seqPos) - 1;             // the step under the cursor fires
  ) : ( seqRelease(); );
);
// Hang on the timeline, but do NOT hard-reset every block.
// beat_position rounds, and if seqPos in @sample has just crossed a
// step boundary, the block start nudges it minimally back — the step
// then fires twice or drops out. That was the timing jitter. It is
// re-synced only on a real offset: loop jump, position change, tempo
// change. 0.02 steps are 2.3 ms at 130 BPM.
// a small correction (< 0.5 step) keeps lastStep - no step index ever fires twice per pass:
//   - forward or within the same step: seqPos = tgtPos (the next step fires regularly, possibly at once);
//   - back behind the start of the last fired step: hold seqPos at its start (lastStep)
//     until the host catches up (the next blocks correct the rest).
// Large jumps (>= 0.5 step: loop, position change, start with FREE RUN) as before with lastStep = floor - 1,
// the step under the cursor fires. Without correction (normal case) everything runs as before.
seqRunning && hostPlay ? (
  tgtPos = beat_position*4;
  abs(tgtPos - seqPos) > 0.02 ? (
    abs(tgtPos - seqPos) < 0.5 ? (
      seqPos = floor(tgtPos) >= lastStep ? tgtPos : lastStep;
    ) : (
      seqPos = tgtPos;
      lastStep = floor(seqPos) - 1;
    );
  );
);

// MIDI with offset into the queue, triggering happens sample-accurately in @sample
while (midirecv(offs, m1, m2, m3)) (
  evN < EVT_MAX ? (
    M_EVT[evN*4] = offs;   M_EVT[evN*4+1] = m1;
    M_EVT[evN*4+2] = m2;   M_EVT[evN*4+3] = m3;
    evN += 1;
  ) : ( handleMidi(m1, m2, m3); );
  // Instrument: notes are consumed. CC/pitchbend/clock keep going.
  stThru = m1 & 0xF0;
  midiThru ? midisend(offs, m1, m2, m3)
           : ( stThru != 0x80 && stThru != 0x90 ? midisend(offs, m1, m2, m3) );
);

// --- Pattern export for the companion ReaScript tt303_pattern_to_midi.lua.
// Mirrors the CURRENTLY DISPLAYED bank (slider25) unchanged into gmem.
// Pure copy from M_SEQ, no DSP, no effect on the sound.
gmem[0] = 30303;                     // handshake / magic
gmem[1] = 1;                         // layout version
gmem[2] = gmem[2] + 1;               // heartbeat: running instance
gmem[3] = floor(slider25);           // displayed bank 0..3 (A..D)
gmem[4] = slider21;                  // SEQ pattern length, raw (script clamps 1..16)
gmem[5] = slider23;                  // global SEQ GATE % (non-slide steps)
gmem[6] = slider22;                  // SEQ SHUFFLE %
gmem[7] = 36;                        // note number of the original pitch (C2)
exBase = floor(slider25)*SEQ_BANK;
exI = 0;
loop(64,
  gmem[8 + exI] = M_SEQ[exBase + exI];
  exI += 1;
);

/* ============================================================
   @sample — one voice, signal path as in the hardware
   ============================================================ */
@sample

// --- due MIDI events
while (evRd < evN && M_EVT[evRd*4] <= smplPos) (
  handleMidi(M_EVT[evRd*4+1], M_EVT[evRd*4+2], M_EVT[evRd*4+3]);
  evRd += 1;
);

// --- Sequencer clock. Odd steps move back on shuffle.
seqRunning ? (
  seqPos += stepInc;
  stepIdx = floor(seqPos);
  sFrac = seqPos - stepIdx;
  ((stepIdx & 1) ? sFrac >= swFrac : 1) && stepIdx != lastStep ? (
    lastStep = stepIdx;
    seqFire(stepIdx - patLen*floor(stepIdx/patLen));
  );
  gateLeft > 0 ? ( gateLeft -= 1; gateLeft <= 0 ? seqRelease(); );
);

// --- Slide. RC approach in log frequency space (capacitor recharge).
sliding ? (
  curLog += (slideTgt - curLog)*slideCoef;
  // stop when the remainder is below one cent (ln(2)/1200 = 0.000578)
  abs(slideTgt - curLog) < 0.0005 ? ( curLog = slideTgt; sliding = 0; );
);
freq = exp(curLog);

// --- Envelopes. Accent runs on a second, faster curve,
//     the capacitor discharges further independently of it.
mEnv *= mCoef;
aEnv *= aDecC;
accCap *= accDecC;
fc = baseF*exp((envOct*mEnv + accOctCur*aEnv)*0.6931472);
fc = min(fcMax, max(30, fc));

// --- VCA
envStage == 1 ? (
  amp += attInc;
  (attInc >= 0 ? amp >= peakAmp : amp <= peakAmp) ? ( amp = peakAmp; envStage = 2; );
);
envStage == 2 ? amp *= susCoef;
envStage == 3 ? ( amp *= relCoef; amp < 0.00002 ? ( amp = 0; envStage = 0; ); );

needVoice = amp > 0.00002 || stkN > 0 || envStage > 0 || sliding;

needVoice ? (
  // recompute tan() only when fc really moves. The threshold is
  // RELATIVE (0.15 per mille), not absolute — a fixed limit in hertz
  // would be an audible quantisation at a low cutoff and ineffective
  // at a high one.
  abs(fc - fcPrev) > fc*0.00015 ? (
    fcPrev = fc;
    g = tan($pi*fc*poleScale/SRX);
    G = g/(1 + g);
  );
  inc  = min(max(freq, 8), 0.45*SRX)/SRX;
  A    = G*G*G;
  // The square of the 303 comes from a transistor comparator with an
  // asymmetric operating point. The offset shrinks in high registers,
  // because the recharge time there takes a larger share of the period.
  // Duty ~1/5, fitted to the reference square's even-harmonic content
  // (strong H2/H4/H6, spectral nulls at H5/H10/H15; ref_f_c50_r50_sq.wav).
  sqDuty = waveSel ? (0.19 - 0.025*min(1, freq*0.0005)) : 0.5;
  osA = 0; osB = 0; osi = 0;
  loop(2,
    phase += inc; phase >= 1 ? phase -= 1;
    waveSel ? (
      // second edge at phase = sqDuty, so (phase - sqDuty) mod 1
      tp = phase + (1 - sqDuty); tp -= floor(tp);
      sqRaw = (phase < sqDuty ? 1 : -1)
            + polyBlep(phase, inc) - polyBlep(tp, inc);
      sqHpY = sqHpA*(sqHpY + sqRaw - sqHpX); sqHpX = sqRaw;
      oscv = sqHpY;
    ) : (
      oscv = 2*phase - 1 - polyBlep(phase, inc);
    );
    oscHpY = oscHpA*(oscHpY + oscv - oscHpX); oscHpX = oscv;
    xin = softSat(oscHpY*0.8);

    // Level-dependent feedback: it belongs INSIDE the oversampling,
    // otherwise the second pass computes with the value from the
    // previous sample.
    kEff = kRes/(1 + 0.4*abs(y3prev));

    // High-pass 20 Hz IN the feedback path. Its share is affine in y3,
    // so the loop stays solvable without delay:
    //   u  = xin - fbHp(kEff*y3) = (xin - fbC) - fbHpA*kEff*y3
    //   y3 = A*u + B   ->   y3 = (A*(xin - fbC) + B)/(1 + A*fbHpA*kEff)
    fbC = fbHpA*(fbHpY - fbHpX);
    B   = G*G*(1 - G)*s1 + G*(1 - G)*s2 + (1 - G)*s3;
    y3  = (A*(xin - fbC) + B)/(1 + A*fbHpA*kEff);
    fbI = kEff*y3;
    fbHpY = fbHpA*(fbHpY + fbI - fbHpX); fbHpX = fbI;
    u = xin - fbHpY;

    v = (u  - s1)*G; o1 = v + s1; s1 = o1 + v;
    v = (o1 - s2)*G; o2 = v + s2; s2 = o2 + v;
    v = (o2 - s3)*G; o3 = v + s3; s3 = o3 + v;
    y3prev = o3;
    osi == 0 ? osA = o3 : osB = o3;
    osi += 1;
  );
  // Decimation with 1/4-1/2-1/4 instead of plain averaging. The third
  // point is the second pass of the PREVIOUS sample. Lowers the alias
  // floor of the bare oscillator by 4.3 dB (little behind the filter,
  // but almost free). Plain average: 0.5*(osA + osB)*resMakeUp*amp.
  voice = (0.25*osPrev + 0.5*osA + 0.25*osB)*resMakeUp*amp;
  osPrev = osB;
) : (
  // Voice sleeps. The filter states must NOT simply stay put: amp acts
  // only behind the filter, so at high resonance the ladder still rings
  // at full level when amp is long below the threshold. Frozen, these
  // values would be heard as a click on the next note-on. Hence a short
  // decay of all states here (around 5 ms time constant).
  voice = 0;
  s1 *= 0.99; s2 *= 0.99; s3 *= 0.99;
  fbHpX *= 0.99; fbHpY *= 0.99; y3prev *= 0.99;
  oscHpX *= 0.99; oscHpY *= 0.99; sqHpX *= 0.99; sqHpY *= 0.99;
  osPrev *= 0.5;
);

// --- Drive: the EQ selects the band that gets distorted.
//
// The EQ is NOT in series any more. dBand is the share the EQ passes
// and that goes into the WaveShaper; dRest is exactly what the EQ has
// removed, and runs past it undistorted. Because dRest is formed as a
// difference, dBand + dRest is again exactly the input signal — with
// the distortion switched off the whole stage is thereby bit-exact
// transparent, no matter how the EQ is set.
//
// In practice that means: raising the lowcut takes the bass out of the
// DISTORTION, not out of the output. That is exactly how a drive input
// EQ is meant — the fundamental stays clean, only the mids get dirty.
dIn   = voice;
dBand = dIn;
eqDLoOn ? ( dHpY = eqDLoA*(dHpY + dBand - dHpX); dHpX = dBand; dBand = dHpY; )
        : ( dHpY = dBand; dHpX = dBand; );
eqDHiOn ? ( dLpY += eqDHiG*(dBand - dLpY); dBand = dLpY; )
        : ( dLpY = dBand; );
dRest = dIn - dBand;

// WaveShaper 2x oversampled. The intermediate point is linearly
// interpolated, then the same 1/4-1/2-1/4 decimation as in the filter.
// Measured at the real filter output, this lowers the alias floor behind
// the drive by 7.6 to 9.8 dB — depending on model and drive from -15..-56
// to -24..-60 dBc. That is the largest remaining alias lever in the
// whole device, clearly larger than 4x oversampling of osc+filter.
//
// The decimated chain thereby runs half a sample period behind
// dRest. With the flat one-pole EQs that is less than 0.1 dB sum error
// in the transition band; with the EQ switched off dRest is exactly
// zero and the question does not arise.
fxDistOn ? (
  dMid  = 0.5*(dPrevIn + dBand); dPrevIn = dBand;
  dsA   = distProc(dMid*distPreG)*distPostG;
  dsB   = distProc(dBand*distPreG)*distPostG;
  dy    = 0.25*dsPrev + 0.5*dsA + 0.25*dsB + dRest;
  dsPrev = dsB;
) : (
  // Bypass is true unity — dBand + dRest is dIn again.
  dy = dIn;
  dPrevIn = dBand; dsPrev *= 0.5;
);

// --- Ping-pong delay (fully bypassed at mix < 0.5 %)
dlyMix > 0.005 ? (
  dlyIn = dy;
  eqYLoOn ? ( hpY = eqYLoA*(hpY + dlyIn - hpPrev); hpPrev = dlyIn; dlyIn = hpY; ) : ( hpY = dlyIn; hpPrev = dlyIn; );
  eqYHiOn ? ( dlyLpY += eqYHiG*(dlyIn - dlyLpY); dlyIn = dlyLpY; ) : ( dlyLpY = dlyIn; );
  rp = dlyPos - floor(dlySamps); rp < 0 ? rp += dlyBufLen;
  i2 = rp - 1; i2 < 0 ? i2 += dlyBufLen;
  fr = dlySamps - floor(dlySamps);
  dl = M_DLY1[rp]*(1 - fr) + M_DLY1[i2]*fr;
  dr = M_DLY2[rp]*(1 - fr) + M_DLY2[i2]*fr;
  lpL += lpG24*(dl - lpL);
  lpR += lpG24*(dr - lpR);
  M_DLY1[dlyPos] = dlyIn + dlyFb2*lpR;
  M_DLY2[dlyPos] = lpL;
  dlyPos += 1; dlyPos >= dlyBufLen ? dlyPos = 0;
  wetDL = lpL*dlyMix;
  wetDR = lpR*dlyMix;
 ) : (
  wetDL = 0; wetDR = 0;
  lpL *= 0.995; lpR *= 0.995; dlyLpY *= 0.995;
  // The input high-pass is carried along, otherwise hpPrev stands on an
  // old value when switched back in and the differentiator sees a
  // level jump — that was a plop when turning the mix up.
  hpPrev = dy; hpY *= 0.995;
  // The write pointer keeps running and lays down silence, so that no
  // old content is preserved in the buffer that comes back when switched in.
  M_DLY1[dlyPos] = 0; M_DLY2[dlyPos] = 0;
  dlyPos += 1; dlyPos >= dlyBufLen ? dlyPos = 0;
);

// --- Reverb (fully bypassed at mix < 0.5 %)
// When switching TO bypass, predelay, combs, allpasses and the output
// filters are cleared once. Without that the buffers and indices would
// stand still (combProc/apProc do not run at all in bypass) and on
// turning back up seconds-old content came back. The one memset costs
// around 220 kB, occurs exactly once at the zero crossing of the knob
// and lies below one sample time.
rvbOn = rvbMix > 0.005;
rvbOn != rvbWas ? (
  rvbWas = rvbOn;
  !rvbOn ? (
    memset(M_PRE, 0, 8192);
    memset(M_RVB, 0, rvbTotal);
    ri = 48; loop(16, M_PAR[ri] = 0; ri += 1; );   // comb damping store
    prePos = 0;
    ri = 32; loop(16, M_PAR[ri] = 0; ri += 1; );   // comb read indices
    ri = 80; loop(8,  M_PAR[ri] = 0; ri += 1; );   // allpass read indices
    rvHpX = 0; rvHpY = 0; rvLpY = 0;
    rhpL = 0; rhpR = 0; rhpXL = 0; rhpXR = 0; rlpL = 0; rlpR = 0;
  );
);
rvbOn ? (
  rvIn = dy + (wetDL + wetDR)*0.5;
  eqRLoOn ? ( rvHpY = eqRLoA*(rvHpY + rvIn - rvHpX); rvHpX = rvIn; rvIn = rvHpY; ) : ( rvHpY = rvIn; rvHpX = rvIn; );
  eqRHiOn ? ( rvLpY += eqRHiG*(rvIn - rvLpY); rvIn = rvLpY; ) : ( rvLpY = rvIn; );
  M_PRE[prePos] = rvIn;
  prePos += 1; prePos >= preLen ? prePos = 0;
  rvbX = M_PRE[prePos];
  sum1 = 0; sum2 = 0;
  i = 0;
  loop(8,
    sum1 += combProc(i, rvbX);
    sum2 += combProc(i + 8, rvbX);
    i += 1;
  );
  w1 = sum1*0.015; w2 = sum2*0.015;
  i = 0;
  loop(4,
    w1 = apProc(i, w1);
    w2 = apProc(i + 4, w2);
    i += 1;
  );
  rhpL = rhpA*(rhpL + w1 - rhpXL); rhpXL = w1;
  rhpR = rhpA*(rhpR + w2 - rhpXR); rhpXR = w2;
  rlpL += rlpG*(rhpL - rlpL);
  rlpR += rlpG*(rhpR - rlpR);
);

// --- Compressor on dry only, then delay/reverb added (303 punch stays)
lv = abs(dy);
db = 20*log(lv + 0.00000001)*0.43429448;
db > envDb ? ( envDb += (db - envDb)*cAtk; ) : ( envDb += (db - envDb)*cRel; );
over = envDb + 14;
k15 = min(30, max(0, over + 15));
gr = -0.8*(k15*k15/60 + max(0, over - 15));
cg = 10^(gr/20)*1.78;
// compOn = 0 -> dry unprocessed (compression AND the ~+5 dB make-up 1.78
// out, so ~5 dB quieter, compensate with VOLUME). compMix blends linearly
// between dy (0 %) and dy*cg (100 %). envDb/cg always run along -> click-free.
dry = compOn ? dy*(1 + compMix*(cg - 1)) : dy;
sumL = dry + wetDL + rlpL*rvbMix;
sumR = dry + wetDR + rlpR*rvbMix;
spl0 = min(1, max(-1, softClip(sumL*volG)));
spl1 = min(1, max(-1, softClip(sumR*volG)));

// --- Oscilloscope (every 2nd sample is enough at gfx 45 Hz)
scopeDiv ? (
  M_SCOPE[scopePos] = (spl0 + spl1)*0.5;
  scopePos += 1; scopePos >= 512 ? scopePos = 0;
);
scopeDiv = 1 - scopeDiv;

// Advance the block position only here: while sample n is processed
// smplPos stays at n, and the offset in the MIDI output matches the sample.
smplPos += 1;

/* ============================================================
   @gfx — device front after the Tim Techlor design kit
   Core Black as the ground, Acid Green as the only accent colour,
   Core White only for pointers and keyboard. Traces at a
   45 degree angle end in solder pads and structure the layout.
   Drawing happens in the 900 x 732 grid, SC scales to the window.
   ============================================================ */
@gfx 1125 915

// TT-Theme: mask the mouse while the OPTIONS box is open; scheme from slider36
tth_pre(); tt_pb_pre(); tth_sync(slider36);   // tt_pb_pre = preset bar masks the mouse (before any control is drawn)

// ---------- Scale ----------
// Lower limit only as an emergency brake against SC = 0. At 0.45 the
// front was drawn larger than the window at small window sizes and
// cut off on the right and at the bottom.
tth_view(UI_W,UI_H);

/* ---------- Fonts ----------
   Two families: a sans-serif one for all labels and a monospaced one
   only for numeric values, so digits do not jitter when turning.

   Each candidate is measured against a font that is guaranteed not to
   exist. If it measures the same, it is not installed and REAPER has
   fallen back to the same system default — then the next one is tried.
   Without this check the whole device used to end up in Courier New:
   "Liberation Mono" does not exist on Windows, GDI fell back to the
   standard fixed-width font, and the old M/i test did not notice,
   because Courier New is likewise monospaced. Hence the serifs.

     1  wordmark      Zilap Orion, else sans-serif bold
     2  sans-serif    medium      3  sans-serif    small
     4  monospaced    medium      5  monospaced    small               */

fontChk == 0 ? (
  fontChk = 1;
  gfx_setfont(9, "TT303NoSuchFace", 16);
  gfx_measurestr("HAMBURGEFONSIV", refW, refH);
  gfx_measurestr("M", refM, refH2);

  sansSel = -1;
  sansSel < 0 ? ( gfx_setfont(9, "Segoe UI", 16);        gfx_measurestr("HAMBURGEFONSIV", tw1, th1);
                  (tw1 != refW || th1 != refH) ? sansSel = 0; );
  sansSel < 0 ? ( gfx_setfont(9, "Helvetica Neue", 16);  gfx_measurestr("HAMBURGEFONSIV", tw1, th1);
                  (tw1 != refW || th1 != refH) ? sansSel = 1; );
  sansSel < 0 ? ( gfx_setfont(9, "DejaVu Sans", 16);     gfx_measurestr("HAMBURGEFONSIV", tw1, th1);
                  (tw1 != refW || th1 != refH) ? sansSel = 2; );
  sansSel < 0 ? ( gfx_setfont(9, "Liberation Sans", 16); gfx_measurestr("HAMBURGEFONSIV", tw1, th1);
                  (tw1 != refW || th1 != refH) ? sansSel = 3; );
  sansSel < 0 ? sansSel = 4;                 // last resort: Arial

  // monospaced: must be present AND really equal in width
  monoSel = -1;
  monoSel < 0 ? ( gfx_setfont(9, "Consolas", 16);
                  gfx_measurestr("M", tw1, th1); gfx_measurestr("i", tw2, th2);
                  (tw1 == tw2 && tw1 != refM) ? monoSel = 0; );
  monoSel < 0 ? ( gfx_setfont(9, "DejaVu Sans Mono", 16);
                  gfx_measurestr("M", tw1, th1); gfx_measurestr("i", tw2, th2);
                  (tw1 == tw2 && tw1 != refM) ? monoSel = 1; );
  monoSel < 0 ? ( gfx_setfont(9, "Menlo", 16);
                  gfx_measurestr("M", tw1, th1); gfx_measurestr("i", tw2, th2);
                  (tw1 == tw2 && tw1 != refM) ? monoSel = 2; );
  monoSel < 0 ? monoSel = 3;                 // last resort: Courier New

  // house font for the wordmark only if it is really there
  gfx_setfont(9, "Zilap Orion", 16); gfx_measurestr("HAMBURGEFONSIV", tw1, th1);
  bigSel = (tw1 != refW || th1 != refH);
);

// Sizes grow with the window. The small sizes sit one point higher
// than before, the wordmark stays as it was.
// steps from the theme module (tth_f1sz = title slot 1, tth_f2sz = text slots 2..5), ~8 % per step
fBig = max(12, floor(38*SC*1.08^tth_f1sz));
fMed = max(10, floor(16*SC*1.08^tth_f2sz));
fSml = max(9,  floor(13*SC*1.08^tth_f2sz));
// fallback font (slot 7) for button and row labels that do not fit their box
// in their font: sans-serif small, only grows up to step +2 (at step 0 and below = fSml). btn and the
// row labels only fall back when the measured text is too wide - at step 0 nothing changes.
fCap = max(9,  floor(13*SC*1.08^min(2, tth_f2sz)));

(fBig != fBigP || fMed != fMedP || fSml != fSmlP || fCap != fCapP) ? (
  fBigP = fBig; fMedP = fMed; fSmlP = fSml; fCapP = fCap;
  bigSel ? gfx_setfont(1, "Zilap Orion", fBig, 'b')
  : sansSel == 0 ? gfx_setfont(1, "Segoe UI", fBig, 'b')
  : sansSel == 1 ? gfx_setfont(1, "Helvetica Neue", fBig, 'b')
  : sansSel == 2 ? gfx_setfont(1, "DejaVu Sans", fBig, 'b')
  : sansSel == 3 ? gfx_setfont(1, "Liberation Sans", fBig, 'b')
  : gfx_setfont(1, "Arial", fBig, 'b');
  sansSel == 0 ? ( gfx_setfont(2, "Segoe UI", fMed);        gfx_setfont(3, "Segoe UI", fSml);        gfx_setfont(7, "Segoe UI", fCap); )
  : sansSel == 1 ? ( gfx_setfont(2, "Helvetica Neue", fMed);  gfx_setfont(3, "Helvetica Neue", fSml);  gfx_setfont(7, "Helvetica Neue", fCap); )
  : sansSel == 2 ? ( gfx_setfont(2, "DejaVu Sans", fMed);     gfx_setfont(3, "DejaVu Sans", fSml);     gfx_setfont(7, "DejaVu Sans", fCap); )
  : sansSel == 3 ? ( gfx_setfont(2, "Liberation Sans", fMed); gfx_setfont(3, "Liberation Sans", fSml); gfx_setfont(7, "Liberation Sans", fCap); )
  : ( gfx_setfont(2, "Arial", fMed); gfx_setfont(3, "Arial", fSml); gfx_setfont(7, "Arial", fCap); );
  monoSel == 0 ? ( gfx_setfont(4, "Consolas", fMed);         gfx_setfont(5, "Consolas", fSml); )
  : monoSel == 1 ? ( gfx_setfont(4, "DejaVu Sans Mono", fMed); gfx_setfont(5, "DejaVu Sans Mono", fSml); )
  : monoSel == 2 ? ( gfx_setfont(4, "Menlo", fMed);            gfx_setfont(5, "Menlo", fSml); )
  : ( gfx_setfont(4, "Courier New", fMed); gfx_setfont(5, "Courier New", fSml); );
);
cap303Fonts();   // fallback fonts for large FONT steps (only sets on a size change)

// Mouse state: click as an edge, so switches do not fire continuously
uiLmb   = mouse_cap & 1;
uiClick = uiLmb && !lmbPrev;
uiRClk  = (mouse_cap & 2) && !rmbPrev;
!uiLmb ? ( dragId = -1; );
!uiLmb ? ( paintRow = -1; );
clickWait > 0 ? clickWait -= 1;

accentLed *= 0.88;

// ---------- Ground ----------
gfx_set(tth_bgR, tth_bgG, tth_bgB, 1);
gfx_rect(0, 0, gfx_w, gfx_h, 1);

// ---------- Header ----------
gfx_setfont(1);
colAcid(1);
str303F(24, 8, 1, "TT-303", 180, 42);
// Version badge to the right of the title (small font, on the title baseline)
gfx_measurestr("TT-303", hdrTW, hdrTH);
gfx_setfont(3);
// #tt_ver is set once in @init
gfx_measurestr(#tt_ver, hdrVW, hdrVH);
colInk(1);
gfx_x = OX + 24*SC + hdrTW + 10*SC;
gfx_y = OY + 8*SC + hdrTH - hdrVH - 1*SC;
tth_txt(); gfx_drawstr(#tt_ver);
colInk(1);
// fitted up to just before the ACCENT display (x 496), line to y 66
str303F(26, 48, 3, "ACID MACHINE // TIM TECHLOR // MONO BASS SYNTHESIZER", 470, 18);

trace(212, 20, 320, 60);
trace(320, 20, 448, 60);
pad(212, 20, 4); pad(320, 20, 4);
pad(320, 60, 3); pad(448, 60, 3);
colDim(1); xline(0, 70, UI_W, 70);
colAcid(1); xrect(0, 70, 232, 1);

// Accent display (charge of the accent capacitor)
colInk(1); xstr(500, 22, "ACCENT");
tth_tn(0.11, 0.13, 0.11, 1); xrect(500, 38, 64, 8);
ledA = min(1, max(accentLed, accCap*0.6));
gfx_set(accR*ledA, accG*ledA, accB*ledA, 1);
ledA > 0.01 ? xrect(501, 39, 62*ledA, 6);

// Operating mode + MIDI thru
// label above the switch (y 32)
colInk(1); str303F(572, 20, 3, "MIDI", 70, 13);
gfx_setfont(2);
// switches via sl303set
btn(572, 32, 70, 26, slider33 == 1, "THRU") ? ( sl303set(33, 1 - slider33); );
gfx_setfont(3);
colInk(1); str303F(726, 20, 3, "MODE", 74, 13);
gfx_setfont(2);
btn(726, 32, 74, 26, slider1 == 0, "HOST") ? ( sl303set(1, 0); );
btn(804, 32, 74, 26, slider1 == 1, "SEQ")  ? ( sl303set(1, 1); );
// tooltips of the header
tip303_hov(500, 20, 66, 30, "Accent indicator: shows the charge of the accent capacitor and lights on accented notes.");
tip303_hov(572, 32, 70, 26, "Passes incoming MIDI notes on to the output (CC and pitch bend always pass through).");
tip303_hov(726, 32, 74, 26, "HOST: piano roll plays the voice; velocity >= ACCENT VEL = accent, overlap = slide, repeated key ignored, 10-note stack, CC 64 sustain.");
tip303_hov(804, 32, 74, 26, "SEQ: the internal 16-step sequencer plays; incoming MIDI notes transpose the pattern.");

/* ---------- Panel SYNTHESIZER ---------- */
panelBox(14, 78, 872, 148);
gfx_setfont(3);
colAcid(1); xstr(26, 84, "SYNTHESIZER");
colInk(1);  xstr(26, 98, "VCO / VCF 18 dB / VCA");

// --- Knobs
// write path sl303set; integer knobs with step size 1 (knob snaps itself),
// continuous knobs (grid 0.1) via qz303 onto the grid of the declaration. Written only when the knob
// is operated (idle: knob returns exactly the slider value) - no constant writing against an envelope.
nv = knob(1, 60, 152, 27, slider3, -24, 24, 1);
nv != slider3 ? ( sl303set(3, nv); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(2, 158, 152, 27, slider4, -50, 50, 1);
nv != slider4 ? ( sl303set(4, nv); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(3, 256, 152, 27, slider5, 0, 100, 0);
nv != slider5 ? ( sl303set(5, qz303(nv, 0.1)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(4, 354, 152, 27, slider6, 0, 100, 0);
nv != slider6 ? ( sl303set(6, qz303(nv, 0.1)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(5, 452, 152, 27, slider7, 0, 100, 0);
nv != slider7 ? ( sl303set(7, qz303(nv, 0.1)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(6, 550, 152, 27, slider8, 0, 100, 0);
nv != slider8 ? ( sl303set(8, qz303(nv, 0.1)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(7, 648, 152, 27, slider9, 0, 100, 0);
nv != slider9 ? ( sl303set(9, qz303(nv, 0.1)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(8, 746, 152, 27, slider10, 0, 100, 0);
nv != slider10 ? ( sl303set(10, qz303(nv, 0.1)); patchSel = -1; );

// labels fitted into the 98-wide column and its row (value line from y 196)
colInk(1);
ctr303F(11, 182, 98, 12, 3, "TUNING");
ctr303F(109, 182, 98, 12, 3, "FINE");
ctr303F(207, 182, 98, 12, 3, "CUTOFF FREQ");
ctr303F(305, 182, 98, 12, 3, "RESONANCE");
ctr303F(403, 182, 98, 12, 3, "ENV MOD");
ctr303F(501, 182, 98, 12, 3, "DECAY");
ctr303F(599, 182, 98, 12, 3, "ACCENT");
ctr303F(697, 182, 98, 12, 3, "VOLUME");

// value fitted up to the next column (88 wide, row 18) - sprintf + str303F
colAcid(1);
str303F(20, 196, 4, sprintf(#v303, "%+d st", slider3), 88, 18);
str303F(120, 196, 4, sprintf(#v303, "%+d ct", slider4), 88, 18);
// The CUTOFF/DECAY display mirrors baseF and decTau from updateParams():
// baseF = 145*exp(cutN*1.95)*(1+resN) (reso lifts the corner with it),
// decTau = 30*exp(decN*2.95) ms.
str303F(210, 196, 4, sprintf(#v303, "%d Hz", floor(145*exp(slider5*0.0195)*(1 + slider6*0.01))), 94, 18);
str303F(322, 196, 4, sprintf(#v303, "%d %%", floor(slider6)), 80, 18);
str303F(420, 196, 4, sprintf(#v303, "%.1f oct", slider7*0.052), 88, 18);
str303F(512, 196, 4, sprintf(#v303, "%d ms", floor(30*exp(slider8*0.0295))), 88, 18);
str303F(616, 196, 4, sprintf(#v303, "%d %%", floor(slider9)), 80, 18);
str303F(714, 196, 4, sprintf(#v303, "%d %%", floor(slider10)), 80, 18);
// tooltips of the knobs (column = label + knob + value, 98 wide)
tip303_hov(11, 122, 98, 88, "Transposes the voice in semitones, -24 to +24. Right-click resets.");
tip303_hov(109, 122, 98, 88, "Fine tuning in cents, -50 to +50. Right-click resets.");
tip303_hov(207, 122, 98, 88, "Filter cutoff, about 150 Hz to 2 kHz; the readout rises with resonance.");
tip303_hov(305, 122, 98, 88, "Feedback of the 18 dB ladder filter, up to self-oscillation.");
tip303_hov(403, 122, 98, 88, "How far the filter envelope opens the cutoff, up to 5.2 octaves.");
tip303_hov(501, 122, 98, 88, "Decay of the filter envelope, about 30 to 570 ms (accented notes use a fixed 0.2 s).");
tip303_hov(599, 122, 98, 88, "Strength of the accent: louder notes and a stronger filter sweep.");
tip303_hov(697, 122, 98, 88, "Output volume; raise it when COMP is off (about 5 dB quieter).");

gfx_setfont(3); colInk(1); xctr(800, 104, 78, 12, "WAVEFORM");
gfx_setfont(2);
btn(800, 118, 78, 22, slider2 == 0, "SAW") ? ( sl303set(2, 0); );
btn(800, 144, 78, 22, slider2 == 1, "SQUARE") ? ( sl303set(2, 1); );
tip303_hov(800, 118, 78, 22, "Sawtooth oscillator: bright and buzzy.");
tip303_hov(800, 144, 78, 22, "Square oscillator: hollower and more nasal than the saw.");

// Accent threshold — belongs to the synthesizer and now stands here;
// no function in SEQ mode, so only drawn then
slider1 == 0 ? (
  // fitted into the column (78) and row (value from y 184)
  colInk(1); str303F(800, 172, 3, "ACCENT VEL", 80, 13);
  gfx_setfont(4); colAcid(1);
  xat(800, 184); tth_txt(); gfx_printf("%d", floor(slider12));
  gfx_setfont(3);
  btn(800, 202, 20, 18, 0, "-") ? ( sl303set(12, max(1, floor(slider12 + 0.5) - 1)); );     // grid 1
  btn(826, 202, 20, 18, 0, "+") ? ( sl303set(12, min(127, floor(slider12 + 0.5) + 1)); );
  // DF = the four thresholds of the Devil Fish documentation (parameter 6: 65, 80, 100, 120) as grid points; lit
  // when the value is one of them; a click jumps to the next (from an intermediate value to the next higher, after 120 to 65).
  btn(852, 202, 26, 18, accIsDf(floor(slider12 + 0.5)), "DF") ? ( sl303set(12, accDfNext(floor(slider12 + 0.5))); );
  tip303_hov(800, 170, 78, 28, "Velocity from which a MIDI note counts as accented in HOST mode (1-127); default 65 as on the Devil Fish.");
  tip303_hov(800, 202, 20, 18, "Lowers the accent velocity threshold by 1.");
  tip303_hov(826, 202, 20, 18, "Raises the accent velocity threshold by 1.");
  tip303_hov(852, 202, 26, 18, "Steps through the four Devil Fish accent thresholds 65, 80, 100 and 120 (lit when the value is one of them).");
);

/* ---------- Panel EFFECTS ----------
   DRIVE and DELAY are narrower, REVERB wider in return. Under each
   unit sits its input EQ as a dual slider: lowcut on the left,
   highcut on the right, logarithmic scale 20 Hz..20 kHz, at the
   outer edges the edge snaps to OFF. Right-click on a handle
   restores the factory setting. */
panelBox(14, 234, 872, 156);
colAcid(1);
// effect titles fitted into their row (switches from y 256)
str303F(26, 240, 3, "DRIVE", 120, 14); str303F(342, 240, 3, "DELAY", 120, 14); str303F(566, 240, 3, "REVERB", 120, 14);
str303F(772, 240, 3, "COMP", 100, 14);
gfx_setfont(3);
colDim(1);
xline(328, 244, 328, 382);
xline(558, 244, 558, 382);
xline(762, 244, 762, 382);
pad(328, 244, 3); pad(558, 244, 3); pad(762, 244, 3);

gfx_setfont(2);
btn(26, 254, 54, 18, slider13 == 1, slider13 == 1 ? "ON" : "OFF") ? ( sl303set(13, 1 - slider13); );
btn(86, 254, 44, 18, slider14 == 0, "SOFT") ? ( sl303set(14, 0); );
btn(134, 254, 44, 18, slider14 == 1, "HARD") ? ( sl303set(14, 1); );
btn(182, 254, 44, 18, slider14 == 2, "FOLD") ? ( sl303set(14, 2); );
btn(230, 254, 44, 18, slider14 == 3, "FUZZ") ? ( sl303set(14, 3); );

btn(342, 254, 42, 18, slider17 == 0, "1/8")  ? ( sl303set(17, 0); );
btn(388, 254, 42, 18, slider17 == 1, "1/8.") ? ( sl303set(17, 1); );
btn(434, 254, 42, 18, slider17 == 2, "1/4")  ? ( sl303set(17, 2); );
btn(480, 254, 42, 18, slider17 == 3, "1/2")  ? ( sl303set(17, 3); );

// Compressor: own column on the right (divider at 762). ON/OFF in the
// button row, MIX as a knob (id 18) in the knob row. Drawing only.
btn(772, 254, 64, 18, slider34 == 1, slider34 == 1 ? "ON" : "OFF")
  ? ( sl303set(34, 1 - slider34); );
gfx_setfont(2); colInk(1); xstr(772, 354, "-14 dB / 5:1");

// grid per declaration - DRIVE 0.1, MIX 0.5 (continuous, qz303); FEEDBACK, SIZE, COMP MIX integer with
// step size 1 (one step per notch); SLIDE 0..300 ms stays continuous (wheel 6 ms per notch) and is rounded to 1.
nv = knob(9, 171, 298, 20, slider15, 1, 40, 0);
nv != slider15 ? ( sl303set(15, qz303(nv, 0.1)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(10, 440, 298, 20, slider16, 0, 100, 0);
nv != slider16 ? ( sl303set(16, qz303(nv, 0.5)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(11, 520, 298, 20, slider18, 0, 90, 1);
nv != slider18 ? ( sl303set(18, nv); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(12, 592, 298, 20, slider19, 0, 100, 0);
nv != slider19 ? ( sl303set(19, qz303(nv, 0.5)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(13, 657, 298, 20, slider20, 20, 100, 1);
nv != slider20 ? ( sl303set(20, nv); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(14, 722, 298, 20, slider11, 0, 300, 0);
nv != slider11 ? ( sl303set(11, qz303(nv, 1)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = knob(18, 824, 298, 20, slider35, 0, 100, 1);
nv != slider35 ? ( sl303set(35, nv); );

gfx_setfont(3); colInk(1);
xctr(141, 322, 60, 12, "DRIVE");
xctr(410, 322, 60, 12, "MIX");
xctr(490, 322, 60, 12, "FEEDBACK");
xctr(562, 322, 60, 12, "MIX");
xctr(627, 322, 60, 12, "SIZE");
xctr(692, 322, 60, 12, "SLIDE");
xctr(794, 322, 60, 12, "MIX");
gfx_setfont(4); colAcid(1);
sprintf(#vstr, "%.1f", slider15);         drawCentered(171, 336);
sprintf(#vstr, "%d %%", floor(slider16)); drawCentered(440, 336);
sprintf(#vstr, "%d %%", floor(slider18)); drawCentered(520, 336);
sprintf(#vstr, "%d %%", floor(slider19)); drawCentered(592, 336);
sprintf(#vstr, "%d %%", floor(slider20)); drawCentered(657, 336);
sprintf(#vstr, "%d ms", floor(slider11)); drawCentered(722, 336);
sprintf(#vstr, "%d %%", floor(slider35)); drawCentered(824, 336);

// --- Input EQs: lowcut left, highcut right, each 0..20 kHz
// Compute first, then draw — so strip and handles stand in the same
// frame. min/max keep the lowcut below the highcut; otherwise the band
// can be pinched shut and the unit is mute without it being visible why.
// written only when the handle is operated (fxEqVal otherwise returns exactly the slider value); the
// clamp LO <= HI applies in the write path.
nv = fxEqVal(20, 26, 360, 284, slider27, 0, 0);
nv != slider27 ? ( sl303set(27, min(nv, slider28)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = fxEqVal(21, 26, 360, 284, slider28, 1, 20000);
nv != slider28 ? ( sl303set(28, max(nv, slider27)); patchSel = -1; );
eqTrack(26, 360, 284, eqT(slider27), eqT(slider28));
eqHandle(20, 26, 360, 284, slider27);
eqHandle(21, 26, 360, 284, slider28);

nv = fxEqVal(22, 342, 360, 208, slider29, 0, 250);
nv != slider29 ? ( sl303set(29, min(nv, slider30)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = fxEqVal(23, 342, 360, 208, slider30, 1, 3000);
nv != slider30 ? ( sl303set(30, max(nv, slider29)); patchSel = -1; );
eqTrack(342, 360, 208, eqT(slider29), eqT(slider30));
eqHandle(22, 342, 360, 208, slider29);
eqHandle(23, 342, 360, 208, slider30);

nv = fxEqVal(24, 562, 360, 196, slider31, 0, 300);
nv != slider31 ? ( sl303set(31, min(nv, slider32)); patchSel = -1; );
nv = fxEqVal(25, 562, 360, 196, slider32, 1, 2300);
nv != slider32 ? ( sl303set(32, max(nv, slider31)); patchSel = -1; );
eqTrack(562, 360, 196, eqT(slider31), eqT(slider32));
eqHandle(24, 562, 360, 196, slider31);
eqHandle(25, 562, 360, 196, slider32);

eqLabels(26, 370, 284, slider27, slider28);
eqLabels(342, 370, 208, slider29, slider30);
eqLabels(562, 370, 196, slider31, slider32);

// tooltips of the effect panel (titles, switches, knob columns 60 wide, EQ strips; small elements last)
tip303_hov(26, 238, 80, 14, "WaveShaper distortion on the voice; the EQ below picks the band that is distorted.");
tip303_hov(342, 238, 80, 14, "Ping-pong delay locked to the project tempo.");
tip303_hov(566, 238, 80, 14, "Freeverb-style reverb with an input EQ.");
tip303_hov(772, 238, 80, 14, "Compressor on the dry voice only, fixed at -14 dB threshold and 5:1.");
tip303_hov(26, 254, 54, 18, "Switches the distortion on or off; off is bit-transparent.");
tip303_hov(86, 254, 44, 18, "Soft: smooth tanh saturation.");
tip303_hov(134, 254, 44, 18, "Hard: peaks clip early, tighter and more aggressive.");
tip303_hov(182, 254, 44, 18, "Fold: peaks fold back instead of clipping, for metallic overtones.");
tip303_hov(230, 254, 44, 18, "Fuzz: asymmetric curve, edgy and rich in even harmonics.");
tip303_hov(342, 254, 42, 18, "Delay time: an eighth note of the project tempo.");
tip303_hov(388, 254, 42, 18, "Delay time: a dotted eighth note (3/16).");
tip303_hov(434, 254, 42, 18, "Delay time: a quarter note.");
tip303_hov(480, 254, 42, 18, "Delay time: a half note.");
tip303_hov(772, 254, 64, 18, "Compressor on or off; off also removes its make-up gain (about 5 dB quieter).");
tip303_hov(141, 276, 60, 74, "Input gain into the WaveShaper, 1.0 to 40.0 (more = denser distortion).");
tip303_hov(410, 276, 60, 74, "Level of the delay in the output; below 0.5 % the delay is bypassed.");
tip303_hov(490, 276, 60, 74, "Amount of echo fed back, 0 to 90 %: more repeats.");
tip303_hov(562, 276, 60, 74, "Level of the reverb in the output; below 0.5 % the reverb is bypassed.");
tip303_hov(627, 276, 60, 74, "Room size, 20 to 100 %: larger rooms give a longer tail.");
tip303_hov(692, 276, 60, 74, "Slide time, 0 to 300 ms: how long the pitch glides between tied notes (0 = jump).");
tip303_hov(772, 352, 90, 18, "Fixed compressor settings: threshold -14 dB, ratio 5:1.");
tip303_hov(794, 276, 60, 74, "Blend between the dry and the compressed voice, 0 to 100 %.");
tip303_eq(26, 360, 284, slider27, slider28, "Input EQ of the drive: only the band between the LO and HI handles is distorted.");
tip303_eq(342, 360, 208, slider29, slider30, "Input EQ of the delay: only the band between the LO and HI handles is echoed.");
tip303_eq(562, 360, 196, slider31, slider32, "Input EQ of the reverb: only the band between the LO and HI handles feeds the reverb.");

/* ---------- Oscilloscope (signal wave as a leitmotif) ---------- */
panelBox(14, 398, 872, 64);
tth_tn(0.042, 0.048, 0.042, 1); xrect(16, 400, 868, 60);
tth_tn(0.10, 0.13, 0.08, 1);
xline(16, 430, 884, 430);
gi = 1;
loop(7, xline(16 + gi*108.5, 400, 16 + gi*108.5, 460); gi += 1; );
colAcid(1);
gi = 0;
loop(256,
  sxp = OX + (18 + 864*gi/255)*SC;
  sv  = M_SCOPE[(scopePos + gi*2) % 512];
  syp = OY + (430 - max(-1.1, min(1.1, sv))*26)*SC;
  gi == 0 ? ( gfx_x = sxp; gfx_y = syp; ) : gfx_lineto(sxp, syp, 1);
  gi += 1;
);
gfx_setfont(5);
gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 0.75); xrect(20, 442, 384, 16);
gateHeld ? colAcid(1) : colInk(1);
xat(24, 444);
tth_txt(); gfx_printf("NOTE "); noteName(noteCur);
tth_txt(); gfx_printf("  %.1f Hz  |  VCF %d Hz  |  %d BPM", exp(curLog), floor(fc), floor(bpmNow));
tip303_hov(14, 398, 872, 64, "Oscilloscope; readout: note, pitch, current filter cutoff and project tempo.");

/* ---------- Panel SEQUENCER / MIDI ---------- */
panelBox(14, 470, 872, 250);

slider1 == 1 ? (

  bb = floor(slider25)*SEQ_BANK;

  gfx_setfont(3);
  colAcid(1); xstr(26, 478, "SEQUENCER");
  colInk(1);  xstr(26, 492, "16 STEPS");
  seqRunning ? colAcid(1) : tth_tn(0.16, 0.19, 0.15, 1);
  xcirc(150, 489, 5, 1);
  gfx_setfont(5);
  colInk(1); xat(162, 482);
  tth_txt();
  seqRunning ? gfx_printf("RUN  STEP %02d", curStepDisp + 1) : gfx_drawstr("STOP");

  gfx_setfont(2);
  btn(250, 478, 86, 22, slider24 == 1, "FREE RUN") ? ( sl303set(24, 1 - slider24); );
  // Called SEQ OUT and not MIDI OUT, so it stays clear that the
  // generated sequence goes out here — the THRU switch above, by
  // contrast, passes incoming notes on. Two sources, two switches.
  btn(344, 478, 86, 22, slider26 == 1, "SEQ OUT") ? ( sl303set(26, 1 - slider26); );
  // tooltips of the sequencer header
  tip303_hov(140, 478, 106, 22, "Sequencer state: RUN with the current step, or STOP.");
  tip303_hov(250, 478, 86, 22, "Keeps the pattern running when the transport is stopped.");
  tip303_hov(344, 478, 86, 22, "Also sends the generated sequence out as MIDI notes (accented steps at velocity 127).");
  tip303_hov(440, 478, 220, 20, "Incoming MIDI notes transpose the pattern; C2 = original pitch.");

  // MIDI note in the gap between MIDI OUT and the knobs
  gfx_setfont(3);
  midiHeld ? colAcid(1) : colInk(1);
  xat(445, 482);
  tth_txt();
  midiHeld ? gfx_printf("MIDI TRANSPOSE %+d", seqTrans) : gfx_drawstr("MIDI = TRANSPOSE");

  // --- Banks. Arm COPY, then click the target bank.
  gfx_setfont(3); colInk(1); xstr(26, 516, "BANK");
  gfx_setfont(2);
  // every pattern change reports tt_undo() (undo point "Edit FX" after release, project changed).
  // Bank selection runs via sl303set (slider_automate creates the undo point itself). COPY into the bank the
  // UNDO snapshot came from discards the UNDO (it would otherwise replace the copy with the pre-RND/MUT/CLEAR state).
  btn(70, 510, 36, 22, slider25 == 0, "A") ? ( copyArm ? copyBankUi(bb, 0)          : sl303set(25, 0); );
  btn(110, 510, 36, 22, slider25 == 1, "B") ? ( copyArm ? copyBankUi(bb, SEQ_BANK)   : sl303set(25, 1); );
  btn(150, 510, 36, 22, slider25 == 2, "C") ? ( copyArm ? copyBankUi(bb, 2*SEQ_BANK) : sl303set(25, 2); );
  btn(190, 510, 36, 22, slider25 == 3, "D") ? ( copyArm ? copyBankUi(bb, 3*SEQ_BANK) : sl303set(25, 3); );
  btn(236, 510, 56, 22, copyArm, "COPY")  ? ( copyArm = 1 - copyArm; );
  btn(300, 510, 46, 22, 0, "RND")   ? ( saveUndo(bb); randPattern(bb); copyArm = 0; tt_undo(); );
  btn(350, 510, 46, 22, 0, "MUT")   ? ( saveUndo(bb); mutPattern(bb); copyArm = 0; tt_undo(); );
  btn(400, 510, 52, 22, 0, "CLEAR") ? ( saveUndo(bb); clearBank(bb); copyArm = 0; tt_undo(); );
  // UNDO only active while the bank the snapshot came from is displayed; writes into that bank.
  undoOk = undoArm && undoBank == bb;
  btn(456, 510, 52, 22, undoOk, "UNDO") ? ( undoOk ? ( loadUndo(); tt_undo(); ); copyArm = 0; );
  bb = floor(slider25)*SEQ_BANK;
  gfx_setfont(3);
  copyArm ? ( colAcid(1); xstr(514, 516, "SELECT TARGET BANK"); );
  // tooltips of the bank/pattern buttons
  tip303_hov(70, 510, 36, 22, "Pattern bank A (four banks of 16 steps). With COPY armed: copies the current bank into A.");
  tip303_hov(110, 510, 36, 22, "Pattern bank B (four banks of 16 steps). With COPY armed: copies the current bank into B.");
  tip303_hov(150, 510, 36, 22, "Pattern bank C (four banks of 16 steps). With COPY armed: copies the current bank into C.");
  tip303_hov(190, 510, 36, 22, "Pattern bank D (four banks of 16 steps). With COPY armed: copies the current bank into D.");
  tip303_hov(236, 510, 56, 22, "Arm it, then click a bank letter to copy the current bank into that bank.");
  tip303_hov(300, 510, 46, 22, "Fills the current bank with a random acid pattern (UNDO takes it back).");
  tip303_hov(350, 510, 46, 22, "Mutates three random steps of the current bank (UNDO takes it back).");
  tip303_hov(400, 510, 52, 22, "Empties the current bank: all gates off (UNDO takes it back).");
  tip303_hov(456, 510, 52, 22, "Takes back the last RND, MUT or CLEAR of the current bank.");
  copyArm ? tip303_hov(514, 510, 150, 22, "COPY is armed: click a bank letter A-D to receive the copy.");

  // --- Sequencer knobs. Label AND value in one line beneath,
  //     so that nothing floats above the knobs any more.
  // step size 1 - LEN/SHUF/GATE move by exactly 1 per notch.
  nv = knob(15, 690, 506, 19, slider21, 1, 16, 1);
  nv != slider21 ? ( sl303set(21, nv); patchSel = -1; );
  nv = knob(16, 770, 506, 19, slider22, 0, 75, 1);
  nv != slider22 ? ( sl303set(22, nv); patchSel = -1; );
  nv = knob(17, 849, 506, 19, slider23, 10, 100, 1);
  nv != slider23 ? ( sl303set(23, nv); patchSel = -1; );
  // Values under the knobs: first measure the widths of the texts, then
  // assign the positions — minimum distance 10 to each other, right
  // margin up to 880. That way nothing overlaps, no matter how wide the
  // font is when dragging the window open or with a fallback font.
  gfx_setfont(3);
  sprintf(#klbl, "LEN");  sprintf(#kval, "%d", floor(slider21));
  gfx_measurestr(#klbl, kw1, kh1); gfx_measurestr(#kval, vw1, vh1);
  wq1 = kw1 + 6 + vw1;
  sprintf(#klbl, "SHUF"); sprintf(#kval, "%d %%", floor(slider22));
  gfx_measurestr(#klbl, kw2, kh1); gfx_measurestr(#kval, vw2, vh1);
  wq2 = kw2 + 6 + vw2;
  sprintf(#klbl, "GATE"); sprintf(#kval, "%d %%", floor(slider23));
  gfx_measurestr(#klbl, kw3, kh1); gfx_measurestr(#kval, vw3, vh1);
  wq3 = kw3 + 6 + vw3;
  qx1 = 690 - wq1*0.5;
  qx2 = max(qx1 + wq1 + 10, 770 - wq2*0.5);
  qx3 = max(qx2 + wq2 + 10, 849 - wq3*0.5);
  qx3 = min(qx3, 880 - wq3);
  qx2 = min(qx2, qx3 - wq2 - 10);
  qx1 = min(qx1, qx2 - wq1 - 10);
  sprintf(#klbl, "LEN");  sprintf(#kval, "%d", floor(slider21));     kvLabel(qx1, 528);
  sprintf(#klbl, "SHUF"); sprintf(#kval, "%d %%", floor(slider22));  kvLabel(qx2, 528);
  sprintf(#klbl, "GATE"); sprintf(#kval, "%d %%", floor(slider23));  kvLabel(qx3, 528);
  tip303_hov(650, 484, 80, 56, "Pattern length, 1 to 16 steps; steps beyond it are dimmed and skipped.");
  tip303_hov(730, 484, 80, 56, "Shuffle: pushes every second step later (0 to 75 %) for swing.");
  tip303_hov(810, 484, 76, 56, "Gate length as a percentage of a step, 10 to 100 %; steps with SLD stay held.");

  // --- Row labels
  // if they reach past x 50 into the grid at large FONT 2 steps (GRID_X 52), fallback font slot 7.
  colInk(1);
  gfx_measurestr("NOTE", rlW, rlH);
  rlW > 36*SC ? ( gfx_setfont(7); tth_f2on ? gfx_set(tth_f2R, tth_f2G, tth_f2B, gfx_a); );
  xstr(14, 584, "NOTE");
  xstr(14, 660, "GATE");
  xstr(14, 678, "ACC");
  xstr(14, 696, "SLD");
  gfx_setfont(3);

  // guide lines of the C notes
  gi = 0;
  loop(3,
    ly = LANE_Y + LANE_H - (24 + gi*12 - SEQ_NLO + 1)*ROW_H;
    tth_tn(0.14, 0.17, 0.12, 1);
    xline(GRID_X, ly, 884, ly);
    gi += 1;
  );

  // --- 16 columns. Note names monospaced, so the columns do not
  //     jitter when shifting the pitch.
  gfx_setfont(5);
  gi = 0;
  loop(16,
    cx0 = GRID_X + gi*GRID_W;
    seqRunning && curStepDisp == gi ? tth_tn(0.09, 0.16, 0.07, 1)
    : gi < patLen ? tth_tn(0.092, 0.096, 0.092, 1) : tth_tn(0.056, 0.060, 0.056, 1);
    xrect(cx0, LANE_Y, 50, LANE_H);
    (gi % 4) == 0 ? ( colDim(1); xrect(cx0, LANE_Y, 1, LANE_H); );

    uiClick && inBox(cx0, LANE_Y, 50, LANE_H) ? ( dragId = 1000 + gi; );
    // tt_undo() only when the step really changes (the undo point is created once on release).
    dragId == 1000 + gi && uiLmb ? (
      stNew = min(SEQ_NHI, max(SEQ_NLO,
        SEQ_NLO + floor((LANE_Y + LANE_H - mY)/ROW_H)));
      stNew != M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + SF_NOTE] ? ( M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + SF_NOTE] = stNew; tt_undo(); );
    );
    uiRClk && inBox(cx0, LANE_Y, 50, LANE_H) ? ( M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + SF_GATE] = 1 - M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + SF_GATE]; tt_undo(); );

    nn = M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + SF_NOTE];
    ly = LANE_Y + LANE_H - (nn - SEQ_NLO + 1)*ROW_H;
    M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + SF_GATE] ? ( M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + SF_ACC] ? colWhite(1) : colAcid(1); )
                               : tth_tn(0.20, 0.24, 0.19, 1);
    xrect(cx0 + 4, ly, 42, 4);

    M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + SF_SLIDE] ? (
      colAcid(0.55);
      xline(cx0 + 46, ly + 2, cx0 + 52, ly + 2);
      xline(cx0 + 48, ly - 1, cx0 + 52, ly + 2);
      xline(cx0 + 48, ly + 5, cx0 + 52, ly + 2);
    );

    M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + SF_GATE] ? colAcid(1) : tth_tn(0.25, 0.28, 0.24, 1);
    gfx_measurestr("C#2", tw1, th1);
    gfx_x = OX + cx0*SC + (50*SC - tw1)*0.5; gfx_y = OY + 638*SC;
    noteName(nn);

    ri = 0;
    loop(3,
      ry = 656 + ri*18;
      fld = 1 + ri;
      hitc = inBox(cx0, ry, 50, 16);
      uiClick && hitc ? (
        paintRow = ri + 1;
        paintVal = 1 - M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + fld];
        M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + fld] = paintVal; tt_undo();
      ) : (
        uiLmb && paintRow == ri + 1 && hitc && M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + fld] != paintVal ? ( M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + fld] = paintVal; tt_undo(); );
      );
      M_SEQ[bb + gi*4 + fld] ? (
        ri == 0 ? colAcid(0.90) : ri == 1 ? colWhite(0.90) : colAcid(0.50);
      ) : (
        hitc ? tth_tn(0.16, 0.19, 0.15, 1) : tth_tn(0.104, 0.109, 0.104, 1);
      );
      xrect(cx0, ry, 50, 16);
      ri += 1;
    );
    gi += 1;
  );
  patLen < 16 ? (
    gfx_set(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
    xrect(GRID_X + patLen*GRID_W, LANE_Y, 884 - (GRID_X + patLen*GRID_W), 168);
  );
  // tooltips of the step editor (one field per row across all 16 columns)
  tip303_hov(14, LANE_Y, 870, 112, "Note editor: click or drag up/down to set the pitch (C1-C3); right-click toggles the gate.");
  tip303_hov(14, 656, 870, 16, "GATE row: click to switch a step on or off (an off step is a rest); drag to paint.");
  tip303_hov(14, 674, 870, 16, "ACC row: click to accent a step (louder, stronger filter sweep); drag to paint.");
  tip303_hov(14, 692, 870, 16, "SLD row: click to glide from this step into the next without retrigger; drag to paint.");

) : (

  // ---------- HOST mode: MIDI display ----------
  gfx_setfont(3);
  colAcid(1); xstr(26, 478, "MIDI INPUT");
  // sustain (CC 64) is appended to the line while it is on
  colInk(1);  xstr(26, 492, susOn ? "PIANO ROLL PLAYS THE SOUND ENGINE   |   SUSTAIN (CC 64)" : "PIANO ROLL PLAYS THE SOUND ENGINE");
  xat(26, 514);
  tth_txt(); gfx_printf("VELOCITY >= %d = ACCENT   |   OVERLAPPING NOTES = SLIDE   |   LAST NOTE WINS   |   HELD: %d", floor(slider12), stkN);

  gi = 0; wi = 0;
  loop(37,
    nn = 24 + gi;
    kk = nn - 12*floor(nn/12);
    (kk == 1 || kk == 3 || kk == 6 || kk == 8 || kk == 10) ? 0 : (
      noteHeld(nn) ? colAcid(1) : gfx_set(0.88, 0.88, 0.88, 1);
      xrect(40 + wi*36, 544, 34, 110);
      gfx_set(0.10, 0.10, 0.10, 1);
      kk == 0 ? ( xat(45 + wi*36, 632); tth_txt(); gfx_printf("C%d", floor(nn/12) - 1); );
      wi += 1;
    );
    gi += 1;
  );
  gi = 0; wi = 0;
  loop(37,
    nn = 24 + gi;
    kk = nn - 12*floor(nn/12);
    (kk == 1 || kk == 3 || kk == 6 || kk == 8 || kk == 10) ? (
      noteHeld(nn) ? colAcid(1) : tth_tn(0.04, 0.05, 0.04, 1);
      xrect(40 + wi*36 - 11, 544, 22, 66);
      tth_tn(0.20, 0.24, 0.19, 1);
      xrect(40 + wi*36 - 11, 544, 22, 1);
    ) : ( wi += 1; );
    gi += 1;
  );
  tip303_hov(40, 544, 792, 110, "MIDI input display: keys light for held notes (display only, not playable); the line above shows sustain (CC 64) while it is on.");
  pad(40, 676, 4); pad(832, 676, 4);
  colDim(1); xline(44, 676, 828, 676);
  colInk(1);
  xstr(26, 692, "SEQ MODE (TOP RIGHT) SWITCHES ON THE INTERNAL 16-STEP SEQUENCER");
);

lmbPrev = uiLmb;
rmbPrev = mouse_cap & 2;
// tooltips of the preset bar and the OPTIONS button (raw coordinates, the mouse is masked there) and drawing
// the tooltip - exactly once, after the front and BEFORE the overlays tt_pb_post / tth_post. Bar geometry as in
// tt_pb_post (17 / 2 / 42 / 24 units, width tt_pb_wu).
// tip303_modtips() - texts and element bounds like tt_modtips in the UI kit (bounds tt_pb_e1..e4 / tth_bx.. from the modules, in window pixels).
tip303_modtips();
tip303_flush();

// OPTIONS button (header) + box with the 10 colour schemes.
// button position in the design grid -> window pixels; the colour does not belong to patches/random/undo.
// bar and button internally compute with max(0.5, SC): right edge of the button at 878 grid units, the bar
// 10 module units to its left. For SC >= 0.5 that yields the positions 548*SC and 808*SC.
hdrScm = max(0.5, SC);
hdrOptX = OX + 878*SC - 70*hdrScm;
hdrBarX = hdrOptX - 10*hdrScm - tt_pb_wu*hdrScm;
tt_pa = tt_pb_post(hdrBarX, OY + 3*SC, SC);
// loading a user slot and INIT change the pattern banks -> tt_undo(). Factory presets only set
// sliders (slider_automate reports them itself); SAVE/RENAME/COPY/DELETE are reported by the preset module.
tt_pa == 1 ? ( applyPatch(tt_pb_arg); )
: tt_pa == 2 ? ( tt_pb_fetch(tt_pb_arg) > 0 ? ( pbApply(); tt_undo(); ); )
: tt_pa == 3 ? ( pbCapture(); tt_pb_commit(tt_pb_arg, PB_PSW); )
: tt_pa == 4 ? ( pbInit(); tt_undo(); );
tt_pb_track(pbSum());
tthc = tth_post(hdrOptX, OY + 3*SC, SC);
tthc >= 0 ? ( slider36 = tthc; sliderchange(slider36); slider_automate(slider36); );
// discard the accumulated mouse wheel last (the product has no UI kit/uikit_end). At the start of @gfx it would
// be wrong: then no wheel would reach the knobs.
mouse_wheel = 0;

tth_hintflush(); // help texts always above all overlays
